hadiths[471]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1","ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān رضي الله عنه said: When the Prophet ﷺ passed away, some of the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ grieved over him so deeply that some of them were almost overcome by distressing thoughts. ʿUthmān said: I was among them. While I was sitting in the shade of one of the fortified buildings, ʿUmar passed by me and greeted me with salām, but I did not realize that he had passed by me or greeted me. ʿUmar then went until he entered upon Abū Bakr. He said to him, ""Isn't it strange that I passed by ʿUthmān and greeted him with salām, yet he did not return my greeting?"" Then ʿUmar and Abū Bakr came to me and both greeted me with salām. Abū Bakr said, ""Your brother ʿUmar came to me and mentioned that he passed by you and greeted you with salām, but you did not return his greeting. What caused you to do that?"" I said, ""I did not do that."" ʿUmar said, ""Yes, by Allah, you did. But that is your habit, O Banū Umayyah."" I said, ""By Allah, I did not realize that you had passed by me, nor did I hear you greet me."" Abū Bakr said, ""ʿUthmān has spoken the truth. Something had occupied you."" I said, ""Yes."" He said, ""And what was it?"" ʿUthmān said: Allah caused His Prophet ﷺ to die before I could ask him about the salvation of this matter. Abū Bakr said, ""I asked him about it."" So I stood before him and said, ""May my father and mother be sacrificed for you; you are more deserving of asking about it."" Abū Bakr said: I asked, ""O Messenger of Allah, what is the salvation of this matter?"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Whoever accepts from me the word which I presented to my uncle, and which he rejected, then it will be salvation for him.""**"
"2","Abū Bakr al-Ṣiddīq رضي الله عنه said: I said, ""O Messenger of Allah, what is the salvation of this matter in which we find ourselves?"" He ﷺ said: > **""Whoever testifies that there is no deity worthy of worship except Allah, then it is salvation for him.""**"
"3","Abū Wāʾil said: I was informed that Abū Bakr met Ṭalḥah and said, ""Why do I see you looking distressed?"" He said, ""There is a statement which I heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said that it is something which makes Paradise obligatory, but I did not ask him about it."" Abū Bakr said, ""I know what it is."" He said, ""What is it?"" Abū Bakr said: > **""There is no deity worthy of worship except Allah.""**"
"4","Abū Bakr رضي الله عنه said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: > **""Go out and proclaim among the people: Whoever testifies that there is no deity worthy of worship except Allah, Paradise becomes obligatory for him.""** So I went out and met ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb. He said, ""What is the matter, O Abū Bakr?"" I said, ""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: 'Go out and proclaim among the people: Whoever testifies that there is no deity worthy of worship except Allah, Paradise becomes obligatory for him.'"" ʿUmar said, ""Return to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, for I fear that they may rely upon this."" So I returned to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He ﷺ said: > **""What brought you back?""** I informed him of what ʿUmar had said. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""He has spoken the truth.""**"
"5","ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān رضي الله عنه said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: > **""Indeed, I know a word which no servant says truthfully from his heart except that he is made forbidden to the Fire.""** ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb said: ""Shall I tell you what it is? It is the word of sincere devotion which Allah, Blessed and Exalted is He, made binding upon Muḥammad ﷺ and his Companions. It is the word of taqwā which the Prophet of Allah ﷺ urged his uncle Abū Ṭālib to say at the time of death: > **'The testimony that there is no deity worthy of worship except Allah.'""**"
"6","Suhayl ibn al-Bayḍāʾ said: While we were travelling with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and I was riding behind him, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ called: ""O Suhayl ibn al-Bayḍāʾ!"" He raised his voice with this call two or three times, and each time Suhayl responded to him. The people heard the voice of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and thought that he was calling for them. Those who were ahead stopped, and those who were behind caught up, until they had gathered. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Indeed, whoever testifies that there is no deity worthy of worship except Allah, Allah will forbid him to the Fire and make Paradise obligatory for him.""**"
"7","Abū Mūsā رضي الله عنه said: I came to the Prophet ﷺ accompanied by a group of my people. He ﷺ said: > **""Receive glad tidings, and convey glad tidings to those behind you: whoever testifies sincerely that there is no deity worthy of worship except Allah will enter Paradise.""** So we left the Prophet ﷺ to convey these glad tidings to the people. Then ʿUmar رضي الله عنه met us and brought us back to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. ʿUmar said: ""O Messenger of Allah, then the people will become reliant upon this."" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ remained silent."
"8","Abū al-Dardāʾ رضي الله عنه said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Whoever says: 'There is no deity worthy of worship except Allah alone, without partner,' will enter Paradise.""** I said, ""Even if he commits adultery and steals?"" He ﷺ said: > **""Even if he commits adultery and steals.""** I said again, ""Even if he commits adultery and steals?"" He ﷺ said: > **""Even if he commits adultery and steals.""** I said again, ""Even if he commits adultery and steals?"" He ﷺ said: > **""Even if he commits adultery and steals, despite the displeasure of Abū al-Dardāʾ.""** Abū al-Dardāʾ said: I then went out to proclaim this among the people, but ʿUmar met me and said: ""Go back, for if the people learn of this, they may become reliant upon it."" So I returned and informed the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He ﷺ said: > **""ʿUmar has spoken the truth.""**"
"9","When Muʿādh ibn Jabal رضي الله عنه was near death, he said: ""Allow the people to enter upon me."" So they were admitted to him. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: > **""Whoever meets Allah without associating anything with Him, Allah will place him in Paradise.""** I did not narrate this to you except at the time of my death. The witness to this is my brother, ʿUwaymir Abū al-Dardāʾ. So they went to Abū al-Dardāʾ and said this to him. Abū al-Dardāʾ said: ""صدق أخي — My brother has spoken the truth. He did not narrate this to you except at the time of his death."""
"10","Muʿādh ibn Jabal رضي الله عنه said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: > **""The keys of Paradise are the testimony that there is no deity worthy of worship except Allah.""**"
"11","ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb رضي الله عنه narrated: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded him to announce among the people: > **""Whoever testifies sincerely that there is no deity worthy of worship except Allah alone, without partner, will enter Paradise.""** ʿUmar said, ""O Messenger of Allah, then they will rely upon this."" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Leave them.""**"
"12","Jābir رضي الله عنه said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Proclaim among the people, O ʿUmar: Whoever dies worshipping Allah sincerely from his heart, Allah will admit him into Paradise and make him forbidden to the Fire.""** ʿUmar said, ""O Messenger of Allah, should I not give the people these glad tidings?"" He ﷺ said: > **""No, lest they rely upon it.""**"
"13","Abū Hurayrah رضي الله عنه said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Whoever says: 'There is no deity worthy of worship except Allah,' it will benefit him on a day of his time, whatever may afflict him before that.""**"
"14","ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb رضي الله عنه said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""I bear witness that there is no deity worthy of worship except Allah and that I am the Messenger of Allah; and I bear witness that no one says this with true sincerity of heart except that Allah shields him from the heat of the Fire.""**"
"15","Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said one day: > **""Whoever says: 'There is no deity worthy of worship except Allah,' Paradise becomes obligatory for him.""** Muʿādh asked his permission to go out to the people to give them the glad tidings, and the Prophet ﷺ permitted him. So he went out joyfully and in haste, and ʿUmar met him. ʿUmar asked, ""What is the matter with you?"" Muʿādh informed him. ʿUmar said, ""Stay where you are; do not hasten."" Then ʿUmar entered upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, ""O Prophet of Allah, your judgment is supreme, but if the people hear this, they will rely upon it and not perform good deeds."" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Call him back.""** So he called him back."
"16","Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī رضي الله عنه said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Whoever says sincerely: 'There is no deity worthy of worship except Allah,' will enter Paradise.""**"
"17","Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī رضي الله عنه reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: > **""Whoever dies without associating anything with Allah will enter Paradise.""**"
"18","Zayd ibn Arqam رضي الله عنه said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Whoever says sincerely: 'There is no deity worthy of worship except Allah,' will enter Paradise.""** It was asked, ""And what is its sincerity?"" He ﷺ said: > **""That it restrains him from that which Allah has forbidden.""**"
"19","Bilāl رضي الله عنه said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""O Bilāl, proclaim among the people: Whoever says 'There is no deity worthy of worship except Allah' a year before his death, will enter Paradise—or a month, or a week, or a day, or an hour.""** Bilāl said, ""Then they will rely upon it."" The Prophet ﷺ said: > **""Even if they rely upon it.""**"
"20","Zayd ibn Khālid al-Juhanī رضي الله عنه said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent me to convey glad tidings to the people: > **""Whoever dies testifying that there is no deity worthy of worship except Allah alone, without partner, for him is Paradise.""**"
"21","Salamah ibn Nuʿaym al-Ashjaʿī رضي الله عنه—who was among the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ—said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Whoever meets Allah Almighty without associating anything with Him will enter Paradise.""** I said, ""O Messenger of Allah, even if he commits adultery and steals?"" He ﷺ said: > **""Even if he commits adultery and steals.""**"
"22","Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī رضي الله عنه said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: > **""Whoever says: 'There is no deity worthy of worship except Allah,' will enter Paradise.""**"
"23","Yaʿlā ibn Shaddād narrated: My father Shaddād [ibn Aws] narrated to me—while ʿUbādah ibn al-Ṣāmit was present and confirmed his account—saying: We were with the Prophet ﷺ when he asked: > **""Is there any stranger among you?""** (meaning someone from the People of the Scripture). We said, ""No, O Messenger of Allah."" He ordered the door to be closed and said: > **""Raise your hands and say: 'There is no deity worthy of worship except Allah.'""** So we raised our hands for a time. Then the Prophet ﷺ lowered his hand and said: > **""All praise is due to Allah. O Allah, You have sent me with this word, commanded me with it, and promised me Paradise on its account, and You never break Your promise.""** Then he ﷺ said: > **""Rejoice, for Allah has forgiven you!""**"
"24","A man narrated: I heard ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr ibn al-ʿĀṣ رضي الله عنهما say: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: > **""Whoever meets Allah without associating anything with Him will enter Paradise, and no sin will harm him alongside it; just as whoever meets Him associating partners with Him will enter the Fire, and no good deed will benefit him alongside it.""**"
"25","ʿImrān ibn Ḥuṣayn رضي الله عنه said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: > **""Whoever knows that Allah is his Lord and that I am His Prophet, sincerely from his heart""** — and he gestured with his hand toward his chest — **""Allah will make his flesh forbidden to the Fire.""**"
"26","Al-Nawwās ibn Samʿān رضي الله عنه reported that he heard the Prophet ﷺ say: > **""Whoever dies without associating anything with Allah, His forgiveness becomes granted for him.""**"
"27","Jarīr رضي الله عنه reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: > **""Whoever dies without associating anything with Allah and has not stained himself with unlawful blood, will be admitted through whichever of the gates of Paradise he wishes.""**"
"28","Abū ʿAmrah al-Anṣārī رضي الله عنه said: We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on an expedition when severe hunger afflicted the people. The people asked the permission of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to slaughter some of their riding camels, saying, ""Allah will allow us to reach our destination through it."" When ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb رضي الله عنه saw that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was inclined to grant them permission to slaughter some of their mounts, he said: ""O Messenger of Allah, what will become of us if we meet the enemy tomorrow on foot and hungry? Rather, if you see fit, O Messenger of Allah, call upon the people to bring the remainder of their provisions, gather them, and then supplicate to Allah for blessing in it; for Allah will surely bless us through your supplication—or deliver us through your supplication."" So the Prophet ﷺ called for the remainder of their provisions. The people began bringing handfuls of food and slightly more, and the most anyone brought was a ṣāʿ of dates. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ gathered it all, then stood and supplicated whatever Allah willed that he supplicate. He then called upon the army to bring their vessels and commanded them to take portions. There was not a vessel remaining in the army except that they filled it, and the like of it still remained! The Messenger of Allah ﷺ laughed until his molars became visible, then said: > **""I bear witness that there is no deity worthy of worship except Allah, and I bear witness that I am the Messenger of Allah; no servant meets Allah believing in them except that they shield him from the Fire on the Day of Resurrection.""**"
"29","Rifāʿah al-Juhanī رضي الله عنه said: We traveled with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ until we reached al-Kadīd—or he said Qudayd. Men began asking the permission of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to return to their families, and he granted them permission. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood up, praised and glorified Allah, and said: > **""What is the matter with men that the side of the tree nearest to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ is more displeasing to them than the other side?""** At that, everyone among the people was seen weeping. A man said, ""Indeed, whoever asks permission after this is foolish!"" The Prophet ﷺ praised Allah and spoke words of goodness, saying: > **""I bear witness before Allah: no servant dies testifying that there is no deity worthy of worship except Allah and that I am the Messenger of Allah, sincerely from his heart, and then remains steadfast, except that he is guided into Paradise.""** He ﷺ continued: > **""And my Lord, Mighty and Majestic is He, has promised me that seventy thousand from my nation will enter Paradise without any reckoning or punishment. And indeed, I hope that you will not enter it until you, and whoever is righteous among your fathers, your spouses, and your descendants, have taken up dwellings in Paradise.""**"
"30","ʿUmārah ibn Ruwaybah رضي الله عنه said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: > **""They are the two determinative realities: whoever dies without associating anything with Allah will enter Paradise, and whoever dies associating anything with Allah will enter the Fire.""**"
"31","Ibn ʿUmar رضي الله عنهما said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""There are two deeds that bring salvation and necessitate [their outcome]: as for the two that bring salvation, whoever meets Allah without associating anything with Him, Paradise becomes obligatory for him; and whoever meets Him associating anything with Him, the Fire becomes obligatory for him.""**"
"32","Khuraym ibn Fātik رضي الله عنه said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Deeds are of six types, and people are of four categories.** > > **As for the two determinative deeds: whoever dies without associating anything with Allah will enter Paradise, and whoever dies associating anything with Allah will enter the Fire.** > > **As for like for like: whoever resolves upon a good deed until his heart feels it and Allah knows it from him, one good deed is recorded for him; and whoever commits an evil deed, one evil deed is recorded against him.** > > **Whoever performs a good deed is rewarded tenfold, and whoever spends in the cause of Allah has a good deed multiplied seven-hundredfold.** > > **As for the people: there is one who is given abundance in this world but restricted in the Hereafter, and one who is restricted in this world but given abundance in the Hereafter.""**"
"33","Ibn ʿAbbās رضي الله عنهما reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Whoever meets Allah without associating anything with Him and without having unlawfully taken a life, will meet Allah light of burden.""**"
"34","Saʿd ibn ʿUbādah رضي الله عنه said: I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: > **""Whoever says: 'There is no deity worthy of worship except Allah alone, without partner'—his heart submitting to it and his tongue humbling itself to it—'and I bear witness that Muḥammad is His servant and His Messenger,' Allah, Mighty and Majestic is He, will forbid him to the Fire.""**"
"35","ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAwf رضي الله عنه said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Indeed, the Muslim remains under the protection of Allah from the day his mother gave birth to him until he stands before his Lord, Blessed and Exalted is He. So if he meets Allah with the sincere testimony that there is no deity worthy of worship except Allah, or with seeking forgiveness, freedom from the Fire is decreed for him.""**"
"36","ʿImrān ibn Ḥuṣayn رضي الله عنه said: ""Shall I not narrate to you a hadith which I have not narrated to anyone since I heard it from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, out of fear that people would become reliant upon it? I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: > **""Whoever knows that Allah is his Lord and that I am His Prophet, having certainty in his heart""** — and he pointed with his hand toward his skin — **""Allah will forbid him to the Fire.""**"
"37","ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr ibn al-ʿĀṣ رضي الله عنهما said: I arrived while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was sitting among a group of his Companions, including ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb رضي الله عنه. I caught only the end of the hadith as the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was saying: > **""Whoever prays four rakʿahs before ʿAṣr, the Fire will not touch him.""** I made a gesture with my hand [indicating admiration for this excellent virtue]. ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb said, ""What you missed from the beginning of the hadith was even better and more magnificent!"" I said, ""O Ibn al-Khaṭṭāb, tell me!"" ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ narrated to us: > **""Whoever testifies that there is no deity worthy of worship except Allah will enter Paradise.""**"
"38","Anas ibn Mālik رضي الله عنه said: While I was traveling with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, his riding camel descended from a mountain pass while he ﷺ was riding ahead by himself. When the path became level, he laughed and proclaimed the takbīr (Allāhu Akbar). So we proclaimed takbīr following his takbīr. Then he rode on a short distance, laughed again, and proclaimed takbīr, so we proclaimed takbīr following his takbīr. When we caught up with him, the people said, ""O Messenger of Allah, we proclaimed takbīr because of your takbīr, but we do not know what made you laugh!"" He ﷺ said: > **""Gabriel عليه السلام was leading the camel for me. When the path smoothed out, he turned to me and said: 'Receive glad tidings, and give glad tidings to your nation: whoever says 'There is no deity worthy of worship except Allah alone, without partner' will enter Paradise.' So I laughed and magnified my Lord.** > > **Then he traveled a short distance, turned to me again, and said: 'Receive glad tidings, and give glad tidings to your nation: whoever says 'There is no deity worthy of worship except Allah alone, without partner' will enter Paradise, and Allah has forbidden him to the Fire.' So I laughed and magnified my Lord, rejoicing in that for my nation.""**"
"39","ʿUqbah ibn ʿĀmir رضي الله عنه said: I arrived in a group of twelve riders until we halted before the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. My companions said, ""Who will graze our camels while the rest of us go to learn from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and when he returns, we will teach him what we heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?"" I said, ""I will."" Then I said to myself, ""Perhaps I am being deprived, while my companions hear what I do not hear from the Prophet of Allah ﷺ."" So one day I attended his gathering, and I heard a man say: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Whoever performs ablution thoroughly, then stands for prayer, will be cleansed of his sins just like the day his mother gave birth to him.""** I marveled at that, so ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb said, ""How much more astonished would you be if you had heard the earlier statement?!"" I said, ""Recount it to me, may Allah make me your ransom!"" ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb said: The Prophet of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Whoever dies without associating anything with Allah, the gates of Paradise will be opened for him—he may enter through whichever of its eight gates he wishes.""** Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out to us. I sat facing him, but he turned his face away from me. I stood up and faced him again, and he did that three times. When it occurred the fourth time, I said, ""O Prophet of Allah, may my father and mother be sacrificed for you, why do you turn your face away from me?"" He turned to me and said: > **""Is [the reward of] one more beloved to you, or [the reward of serving] twelve?""** — repeating it two or three times. When I realized that, I returned to my companions [to tend to their mounts]."
"40","ʿUmārah ibn Ruwaybah رضي الله عنه said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: > **""They are the two necessitating realities: whoever dies without associating anything with Allah will enter Paradise, and whoever dies associating anything with Allah will enter the Fire.""**"
"41","A man from the Anṣār رضي الله عنه narrated: He brought a black slave girl and said, ""O Messenger of Allah, I am obligated to free a believing slave. If you consider her to be a believer, I will free her."" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ asked her: ""Do you testify that there is no deity worthy of worship except Allah?"" She said, ""Yes."" He asked: ""Do you testify that I am the Messenger of Allah?"" She said, ""Yes."" He asked: ""Do you believe in the Resurrection after death?"" She said, ""Yes."" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Free her.""**"
"42","Abū Hurayrah رضي الله عنه said: A man came to the Prophet ﷺ bringing a non-Arab black slave girl, and said, ""O Messenger of Allah, I am obligated to free a believing slave."" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to her: ""Where is Allah?"" She gestured toward the sky with her head and index finger. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ asked her: ""Who am I?"" She gestured with her finger toward the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and toward the sky—signifying: you are the Messenger of Allah. He ﷺ said: > **""Free her.""**"
"43","Ḥabīb ibn Abī Thābit said: Ḥassān ibn Thābit رضي الله عنه recited verses of poetry before the Prophet ﷺ, saying: ""I bear witness, by Allah's leave, that Muḥammad is the Messenger of the One Who is exalted high above the heavens; And that Abū Yaḥyā and Yaḥyā—both of them— have their deeds accepted in His religion; And that the brother of Al-Aḥqāf [Hūd عليه السلام], when he stood among them, stood for the sake of Allah among them with justice."" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""And I [bear witness as well].""**"
"44","Jābir رضي الله عنه said: A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, ""I have a hypocrite neighbor who does such-and-such [wicked things]."" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ asked: ""Does he say: 'There is no deity worthy of worship except Allah'?"" He replied, ""Yes."" He ﷺ said: > **""Those are the ones I have been forbidden from harming.""**"
"45","ʿUbaydullāh ibn ʿAdī ibn al-Khiyār said that a man from the Anṣār رضي الله عنه narrated to him: He came to the Prophet ﷺ while he was in a gathering, and whispered to him, seeking permission to kill a certain hypocrite. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said aloud: ""Does he not testify that there is no deity worthy of worship except Allah?"" The Anṣārī man said, ""Yes, O Messenger of Allah, but his testimony is of no value!"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""Does he not testify that Muḥammad is the Messenger of Allah?"" He said, ""Yes, O Messenger of Allah, but his testimony is of no value!"" He ﷺ asked: ""Does he not pray?"" He said, ""Yes, O Messenger of Allah, but his prayer is of no value!"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Those are the ones whom Allah has forbidden me from killing.""**"
"46","Jarīr رضي الله عنه said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""I have been commanded to fight the people until they say: 'There is no deity worthy of worship except Allah.' When they say it, their blood and wealth are protected from me, except by its rightful due, and their reckoning is with Allah, Mighty and Majestic.""**"
"47","Sahl ibn Saʿd رضي الله عنه said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""I have been commanded to fight the people until they say: 'There is no deity worthy of worship except Allah.' When they say: 'There is no deity worthy of worship except Allah,' their blood and wealth are protected from me, except by its rightful due, and their reckoning is with Allah.""**"
"48","Ibn ʿAbbās رضي الله عنهما said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""I have been commanded to fight the people until they say: 'There is no deity worthy of worship except Allah.' When they say it, their blood and wealth are protected from me, except by its rightful due, and their reckoning is with Allah, Mighty and Majestic.""**"
"49","Abū Bakr al-Ṣiddīq رضي الله عنه said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""I have been commanded to fight the people until they say: 'There is no deity worthy of worship except Allah.' When they say it, they shield their blood and wealth from me, except by its rightful due, and their reckoning is with Allah.""**"
"50","ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd رضي الله عنه said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""When one of you aims a spear at a man, even if its tip is at the hollow of his throat, and he says: 'There is no deity worthy of worship except Allah,' let him lower the spear away from him.""**"
"51","Abū Mālik al-Ashjaʿī reported from his father رضي الله عنه that he said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""I have been commanded to fight the people until they say: 'There is no deity worthy of worship except Allah.' When they say it, their blood and wealth are protected from me, except by its rightful due, and their reckoning is with Allah, Mighty and Majestic.""**"
"52","Abū Bakrah رضي الله عنه said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""I have been commanded to fight the people until they say: 'There is no deity worthy of worship except Allah.' When they say it, their blood and wealth are protected from me, except by its rightful due, and their reckoning is with Allah, Mighty and Majestic.""**"
"53","Samurah ibn Jundub رضي الله عنه said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""I have been commanded to fight the people until they say: 'There is no deity worthy of worship except Allah.' When they say it, their blood and wealth are protected from me, except by its rightful due, and their reckoning is with Allah.""**"
"54","Anas ibn Mālik رضي الله عنه said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""I have been commanded to fight the people until they say: 'There is no deity worthy of worship except Allah.' When they say it, their blood and wealth are protected from me, except by its rightful due.""** It was asked, ""And what is its rightful due?"" He ﷺ said: > **""Adultery after marriage, disbelief after accepting Islam, or unlawfully taking a life, for which one is executed in return.""**"
"55","ʿIyāḍ al-Anṣārī رضي الله عنه reported in a marfūʿ narration that the Prophet ﷺ said: > **""Indeed, 'There is no deity worthy of worship except Allah' is a word noble in the sight of Allah, holding an exalted status before Him. It is a word such that whoever says it sincerely, Allah will admit him into Paradise thereby; and whoever says it deceitfully, it protects his blood and secures his wealth in this life, and when he meets Allah tomorrow, He will call him to account.""**"
"56","Ḥumayd ibn Hilāl said: ʿUmārah ibn Qard al-Laythī went out on a military campaign, remaining there for as long as Allah willed, and then returned. When he drew near al-Ahwāz, he heard the call to prayer (adhān) and said, ""By Allah, it has been three days since I last prayed in congregation with Muslims."" So he headed toward the sound of the adhān intending to pray, only to find that they were Azāriqah [Khārijites]. They said to him, ""What has brought you, O enemy of Allah?"" He said, ""Are you not my brothers?"" They said, ""You are the brother of Satan! We will surely kill you."" He said, ""Will you not be pleased with me for that which the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was pleased with from me?"" They asked, ""What did he accept from you?"" He replied, ""I came to him while I was a disbeliever, and I testified that there is no deity worthy of worship except Allah and that he is the Messenger of Allah, so he spared me."" Yet they seized him and martyred him."
"57","Al-Nuʿmān ibn Bashīr رضي الله عنه reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: > **""I have been commanded to fight the people until they say: 'There is no deity worthy of worship except Allah.' When they say it, their blood and wealth are protected from me, except by its rightful due.""**"
"58","Muslim al-Tamīmī رضي الله عنه said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent us on an expedition. When we raided the enemy, I rode ahead of my companions on horseback, and the women and children came out screaming. I said to them, ""Do you wish to secure your lives?"" They said, ""Yes."" I said, ""Say: 'We testify that there is no deity worthy of worship except Allah alone, without partner, and that Muḥammad is His servant and His Messenger.'"" So they said it. My companions then caught up, reproached me, and said, ""We were on the verge of taking spoils of war, and you prevented us!"" When we returned to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he said to them: > **""Do you know what he has achieved? Allah has written for him such-and-such immense reward for every single soul.""** Then he ﷺ drew me close to him."
"59","ʿUqbah ibn Mālik al-Laythī رضي الله عنه said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ dispatched an expedition, and they raided a tribe. A man from that tribe broke away, and a man from the expedition pursued him with an unsheathed sword. The fleeing man shouted, ""I am a Muslim!"" but the pursuer paid no attention to his words, struck him, and killed him. News of this reached the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he spoke very sternly about it until word reached the killer. While the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was delivering a sermon, the killer stood up and said, ""By Allah, O Messenger of Allah, he only said what he said to seek refuge from being killed!"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ turned away from him and from the people in his direction, continuing his sermon. The man said a second time, ""By Allah, he only said what he said to seek refuge from being killed!"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ turned away from him again and continued his sermon. The man could not contain himself and said a third time, ""By Allah, he only said what he said to seek refuge from being killed!"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ then turned toward him, distress and displeasure clearly visible upon his face, and said: > **""Indeed, Allah has refused to accept any excuse from me regarding someone who kills a believer.""** He ﷺ repeated this three times."
"60","Jundub ibn Sufyān رضي الله عنه—a man from Bajīlah—said: I was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when a bearer of glad tidings arrived from one of his military detachments, informing him of the victory and conquest that Allah had granted them. The man said, ""O Messenger of Allah, while we were pursuing the enemy after Allah had routed them, I caught up with a man with my sword. As I fell upon him, he ran saying: 'I am a Muslim! I am a Muslim!'"" The Prophet ﷺ asked: > **""And did you kill him?""** The man said, ""O Messenger of Allah, he only said it to seek refuge."" He ﷺ said: > **""Why did you not tear open his heart to see whether he was truthful or lying?!""** The man said, ""Even if I had torn open his heart, what would I have known? Is his heart anything more than a lump of flesh?"" He ﷺ said: > **""You could not know what was in his heart, nor did you believe what his tongue declared!""** The man pleaded, ""O Messenger of Allah, pray for my forgiveness!"" He ﷺ said: > **""I will not pray for your forgiveness.""** When that man died, they buried him, but the next morning his body was found cast out upon the surface of the earth. They buried him again, but the next morning he was again found on the surface of the earth. This occurred three times. When they saw that, they felt disgraced and ashamed at what had befallen him, so they carried him and cast him into one of those mountain ravines."
"61","ʿImrān ibn Ḥuṣayn رضي الله عنه said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""For what else do I fight the people except for Islam?! By Allah, I will not pray for your forgiveness!""** —or as he ﷺ said."
"62","Quṭbah ibn Qatādah al-Sadūsī رضي الله عنه said: I said, ""O Messenger of Allah, stretch out your hand so that I may pledge allegiance to you on behalf of myself and my daughter Al-Ḥuwayṣilah; for if I were to lie against Allah, I would be deceiving you."" He said: And Khālid ibn al-Walīd attacked us with his cavalry, so we said, ""We are Muslims!"" and he spared us. Then we participated with him in the battle of Al-Ubullah; it was conquered, and our hands were filled [with spoils of war]."
"63","Saʿd ibn Abī Dhiyāb رضي الله عنه said: I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and embraced Islam. I said, ""O Messenger of Allah, allow my people to keep the property and wealth they held upon embracing Islam."" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did so, and appointed me as governor over them. Subsequently, Abū Bakr appointed me after him, and then ʿUmar appointed me after him."
"64","ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd رضي الله عنه said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ wrote to Al-Mundhir ibn Sāwā: > **""Whoever prays our prayer and eats our slaughtered meat, then that is the Muslim; he possesses the covenant of protection from Allah and the covenant of protection from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.""**"
"65","Jundub رضي الله عنه said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Whoever prays our prayer, faces our Qiblah, and eats our slaughtered meat, that is the Muslim; he has the covenant of protection from Allah and the covenant of protection from His Messenger.""**"
"66","ʿAbdullāh ibn Māʿiz رضي الله عنه said: He came to the Prophet ﷺ, and he ﷺ said: > **""Indeed, Māʿiz embraced Islam and thereby secured his wealth, and no crime shall be held against him except what his own hand commits.""** So I pledged allegiance to him upon that."
"67","Mālik ibn Aḥmar رضي الله عنه said: When news of the arrival of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ reached him, he traveled to him as part of a delegation. The Prophet ﷺ accepted his Islam, and Mālik requested that he write a document for him with which he could invite his people to Islam. So he ﷺ had written for him on a piece of leather: > **""In the name of Allah, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful. This is a document from Muḥammad, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, for Mālik ibn Aḥmar and for those who follow him among the Muslims: safety and protection for them as long as they establish the prayer, pay the zakāh, align with the Muslims, keep apart from the polytheists, and pay the fifth (khumus) of the war booty, the share of the indebted, and such-and-such share—then they are secure under the protection of Allah and the protection of Muḥammad, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.""**"
"68","Abū Shaddād رضي الله عنه—a man from the people of Dhimār, a town in Oman—said: The letter of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to the people of Oman: > **""Peace be upon you. To proceed: Affirm the testimony that there is no deity worthy of worship except Allah and that I am the Messenger of Allah, and pay the zakāh; otherwise, I will wage war against you.""** Abū Shaddād said: We could find no one to read the letter to us until we found a young black boy, and he read the letter to us. The sub-narrator asked Abū Shaddād, ""Who was governing the affairs of the people of Oman at that time?"" He replied, ""An Aswār [commander] from among the commanders of Chosroes (Kisrā) who was called Subayḥibān."""
"69","ʿAmr ibn al-Ḥamiq رضي الله عنه said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was dispatching an expedition, and they said, ""O Messenger of Allah, you are sending us out while we have neither provisions nor food, nor do we know the road."" He ﷺ said: > **""You will surely pass by a man of radiant countenance who will feed you with food, give you drink, and guide you along the road; and he is from the people of Paradise.""** When the troop halted at my dwelling, they began gesturing to one another and looking at me. I said, ""Why are you gesturing to one another and looking at me?"" They said, ""Rejoice in glad tidings from Allah and His Messenger, for we recognize in you the description given by the Messenger of Allah ﷺ!"" They informed me of what he had said, so I fed them, gave them drink, provided them with provisions, and went out with them until I guided them along the road. Then I returned to my family and entrusted my camels to them. Thereafter, I traveled to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and asked, ""What is it that you call to?"" He ﷺ said: > **""I call to the testimony that there is no deity worthy of worship except Allah and that I am the Messenger of Allah, the establishment of prayer, the payment of zakāh, the Pilgrimage to the House, and fasting during Ramaḍān.""** I asked, ""If we respond to you in this, will our families, our wealth, and our blood be safe?"" He ﷺ said: > **""Yes.""** So I embraced Islam and returned to my people, informing them of my Islam, and a large number of them accepted Islam at my hands."
"70","ʿUmayr رضي الله عنه said: The letter of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to us: > **""In the name of Allah, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful. From Muḥammad, the Messenger of Allah, to ʿUmayr Dhū Marrān and whoever has embraced Islam from Hamdān. Peace be upon you. I praise Allah before you, beside Whom there is no deity worthy of worship.** > > **To proceed: News of your Islam reached us upon our return from the land of the Byzantines (al-Rūm). So rejoice, for Allah has guided you with His guidance. When you testify that there is no deity worthy of worship except Allah and that Muḥammad is the Messenger of Allah, establish prayer, and pay zakāh, then you have the covenant of protection from Allah and the covenant of protection from His Messenger over your lives, your wealth, and the land of the Byzantine upon which you accepted Islam—its plains, its lowlands, and its pastures—neither being wronged nor placed under hardship.** > > **Indeed, charity (ṣadaqah) is not lawful for Muḥammad nor for the members of his household. And Mālik ibn Murārah al-Rahāwī has faithfully guarded what was entrusted to him, discharged the trust, and conveyed the message; so I command you, O Dhū Marrān, to treat him well, for he is held in high esteem among his people. And may your Lord love you.""**"
"71","Abū Nuʿaym said: ʿAbd al-Malik ibn ʿAṭāʾ al-ʿĀmirī brought out to us a letter from the Prophet ﷺ and said, ""Transcribe it,"" though he did not dictate it to us. He stated that his ancestor Al-Fujayʿ رضي الله عنه had narrated it to him: > **""This is a letter from Muḥammad, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, to Al-Fujayʿ and those with him: Whoever embraces Islam, establishes prayer, pays zakāh, obeys Allah and His Messenger, gives the fifth belonging to Allah from the war booty, aids the Prophet of Allah, bears witness to his Islam, and parts from the polytheists—he is safe under the protection of Allah and Muḥammad ﷺ.""**"
"72","ʿUmārah ibn Aḥmar al-Māzinī رضي الله عنه said: In the pre-Islamic days of ignorance (Jāhiliyyah), I was grazing my camels when the cavalry of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ raided us. I rounded up my camels and mounted the stud camel, but it halted and spread its legs to urinate. So I dismounted and mounted a she-camel, escaping upon it, while they drove away the camels. I then came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and embraced Islam, whereupon he returned the camels to me, as they had not yet distributed them as spoils. Jawwāb ibn ʿUmārah said: ""My brother and I lived to see the very she-camel upon which ʿUmārah rode that day to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."""
"73","Nuʿaym ibn Qaʿnab al-Riyāḥī said: I came seeking Abū Dharr رضي الله عنه but did not find him. I saw a woman and asked her about him, and she said, ""He is over there tending to some land of his."" Then Abū Dharr arrived leading—or driving—two camels tied nose to tail, each bearing a water-skin around its neck. He put down the two water-skins. I said, ""O Abū Dharr, there was no one among all people whom I desired more to meet than you, nor anyone whom I dreaded more to meet than you!"" He said, ""May Allah bless your father! How can both of these feelings be united in you?"" I said, ""I buried a daughter alive during the days of ignorance (Jāhiliyyah). In meeting you, I hoped you would tell me that there is repentance and a way out for me; yet I also feared in meeting you that you would tell me that there is no repentance for me."" Abū Dharr asked: ""Was that during the Jāhiliyyah?"" I said, ""Yes."" Abū Dharr رضي الله عنه said: > **""Allah has pardoned what occurred in the past.""**"
"74","Abū al-Dardāʾ رضي الله عنه said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Exalt Allah, and He will forgive you.""** Ibn Thawbān said: ""Meaning: embrace Islam."""
"75","Salamah ibn Nufayl رضي الله عنه said: A young man came and sat before the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, calling out at the top of his voice: ""O Messenger of Allah, what do you say of a person who has committed every evil deed, perpetrated every sin, and seized everything that came within his grasp—one whose sins, if divided among the people of Madīnah, would overwhelm them all?!"" The Prophet ﷺ said to him: > **""Have you embraced Islam?""** — or **""Are you a Muslim?""** He said, ""As for me, I testify that there is no deity worthy of worship except Allah and that Muḥammad is the Messenger of Allah!"" He ﷺ said: > **""Go, for your evil deeds have been replaced with good deeds.""** The man asked, ""O Messenger of Allah, even my betrayals and wicked deeds?!"" He ﷺ said: > **""Even your betrayals and wicked deeds.""** — repeating it three times. The young man turned away saying: ""Allāhu Akbar, Allāhu Akbar (Allah is the Greatest, Allah is the Greatest)!"" I continued to hear him proclaiming the takbīr until he disappeared from my view."
"76","Abū Ṭawīl Shaṭb al-Mamdūd رضي الله عنه said: He came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, ""What do you say of a man who committed all sins, leaving none out, and during that time left no craving or impulse unfulfilled—is there any repentance for such a person?"" He ﷺ asked: > **""Have you embraced Islam?""** He said, ""As for me, I bear witness that there is no deity worthy of worship except Allah alone, without partner, and that you are the Messenger of Allah."" He ﷺ said: > **""Yes. You must perform good deeds and abandon evil deeds, and Allah will turn all of them into good deeds for you.""** The man asked, ""Even my betrayals and wicked deeds?!"" He ﷺ said: > **""Yes.""** The man cried out, ""Allāhu Akbar (Allah is the Greatest)!"" and continued proclaiming the takbīr until he vanished from sight."
"77","ʿAmr ibn ʿAbasah رضي الله عنه said: An old man leaning upon a staff approached until he stood before the Prophet ﷺ and said, ""O Prophet of Allah, I have committed acts of betrayal and wickedness. Can I be forgiven?"" He ﷺ asked: > **""Do you not testify that there is no deity worthy of worship except Allah?""** The man said, ""Yes, and I testify that Muḥammad is the Messenger of Allah."" He ﷺ said: > **""Your acts of betrayal and wickedness have been forgiven.""**"
"78","Al-Jārūd al-ʿAbdī رضي الله عنه said: I came to the Prophet ﷺ to pledge allegiance to him, and I said to him, ""On condition that if I abandon my religion and enter into your religion, Allah will not punish me in the Hereafter."" He ﷺ said: > **""Yes.""**"
"79","ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb رضي الله عنه reported that he heard the Prophet ﷺ say: > **""Whoever dies believing in Allah and the Last Day, it will be said to him: 'Enter through whichever of the eight gates of Paradise you wish.'""**"
"80","ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān رضي الله عنه said: I wished that I had asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: ""What can save us from that which Satan casts into our souls?"" Abū Bakr رضي الله عنه said, ""I asked him about that, and he ﷺ said: > **'What will save you from that is to say the words which I commanded my uncle to say, but he did not say them.'""**"
"81","Khuzaymah ibn Thābit رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Satan comes to a person and asks: 'Who created the heavens?' and he replies: 'Allah.' Then he asks: 'Who created the earth?' and he replies: 'Allah.' Until he asks: 'Who created Allah?' When any of you encounters that, let him say: 'I believe in Allah and His Messengers (Āmantu billāhi wa rusulih).'""**"
"82","ʿĀʾishah رضي الله عنها reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Indeed, Satan comes to one of you and says: 'Who created you?' and he replies: 'Allah.' Then he says: 'Who created Allah?' When any of you encounters that, let him say: 'I believe in Allah and His Messenger (Āmantu billāhi wa rasūlih),' for indeed that will dispel it from him.""**"
"83","ʿĀʾishah رضي الله عنها said: They complained to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about the whispers they experienced within themselves, saying, ""O Messenger of Allah, we find thoughts within ourselves such that falling from the sky would be more beloved to any of us than uttering them!"" The Prophet ﷺ said: > **""That is pure faith.""**"
"84","Muḥammad ibn Jubayr reported: ʿUmar passed by ʿUthmān while he was sitting in the mosque and greeted him with salām, but ʿUthmān did not return the greeting. ʿUmar went to Abū Bakr and complained to him, saying, ""I passed by ʿUthmān and greeted him with salām, but he did not return my greeting."" Abū Bakr asked, ""Where is he?"" He replied, ""He is sitting in the mosque."" So both of them went to him, and Abū Bakr said to him, ""What prevented you from returning the salām to your brother when he greeted you?"" ʿUthmān said, ""By Allah, I did not realize that he had passed by me. I was absorbed in my thoughts, so I did not notice him greeting me."" Abū Bakr asked, ""What were you pondering?"" He said, ""Satan isolated me and began casting thoughts into my mind such that I would rather possess nothing upon the earth than utter them. When Satan cast that into my mind, I said to myself: 'How I wish I had asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ what can save us from these thoughts that Satan casts into our souls!'"" Abū Bakr said, ""By Allah, I complained of that very matter to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and asked him: 'What can save us from these thoughts that Satan casts into our souls?' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **'What will save you from that is to say the like of what I commanded my uncle to say at the time of death, but he did not do so.'""**"
"85","Anas ibn Mālik رضي الله عنه said: They said, ""O Messenger of Allah, what do you say about one of us who experiences thoughts within himself such that falling from the sky and being dashed to pieces would be more beloved to him than speaking of them?"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""That is pure faith.""**"
"86","Anas رضي الله عنه said: They said, ""O Messenger of Allah, when we are in your presence, we are in a certain spiritual state; but when we depart from you, our state changes."" He ﷺ asked: > **""How are you with your Prophet?""** They said, ""You are our Prophet in secret and in public."" He ﷺ said: > **""That is not hypocrisy.""**"
"87","ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr رضي الله عنهما said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Indeed, Satan comes to one of you and says: 'Who created the heaven?' and he says: 'Allah.' Then he says: 'Who created the earth?' and he says: 'Allah.' Then he says: 'Who created Allah?' When any of you encounters that, let him say: 'I believe in Allah and His Messengers (Āmantu billāhi wa rusulih).'""**"
"88","Ibn ʿAbbās رضي الله عنهما said: A man said to the Prophet ﷺ, ""I find thoughts within myself such that turning into charcoal would be more beloved to me than speaking of them."" He ﷺ said: > **""That is plain, genuine faith.""**"
"89","Umm Salamah رضي الله عنها reported that she heard the Prophet ﷺ when a man asked him, saying, ""I experience thoughts within myself such that if I spoke of them, I would ruin my Hereafter!"" He ﷺ said: > **""None encounters such distress except a believer.""**"
"90","ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd رضي الله عنه said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about whispers (waswasah). He ﷺ said: > **""That is pure faith.""**"
"91","Muʿādh ibn Jabal رضي الله عنه said: I said, ""O Messenger of Allah, by the One Who sent you with the truth, a thought occurs in my mind such that burning until I become charcoal would be more beloved to me than speaking of it!"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Praise be to Allah that Satan has despaired of ever being worshipped in this land of mine; but he has become content with the petty shortcomings among your deeds.""**"
"92","ʿUmārah ibn Abī al-Ḥasan (or Ibn al-Ḥasan) reported from his uncle: People asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about the whispers that one of them finds within himself, such that falling from the Pleiades (al-Thurayyā) would be more beloved to him than speaking of them. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""That is plain, genuine faith. Indeed, Satan comes to the servant with matters less than that; and when he is protected against him, Satan resorts to that extreme.""**"
"93","Abū Hurayrah رضي الله عنه said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""People will continue to say: 'Allah existed before everything, so what existed before Him?'""**"
"94","Ibn ʿUmar رضي الله عنهما said: We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when there came a man who had the ugliest of faces, the foulest of garments, and the most putrid odor, rough and crude, stepping over the necks of the people until he sat directly before the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He asked, ""Who created you?"" He ﷺ said: > **""Allah.""** He asked, ""Then who created the heaven?"" He ﷺ said: > **""Allah.""** He asked, ""Then who created the earth?"" He ﷺ said: > **""Allah.""** He asked, ""Then who created Allah?"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Subḥān Allāh (Glory be to Allah)!""** — twice, and he grasped his forehead. Then the man stood up and departed. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Bring the man back to me!""** So we searched for him, but it was as though he had never existed. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""That was Iblīs; he came to cast doubt into your religion.""**"
"95","Ibn ʿUmar رضي الله عنهما said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Faith is not accepted without deeds, nor are deeds accepted without faith.""**"
"96","ʿAmr ibn ʿAwf ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Muzanī رضي الله عنه said: ""I learned and memorized twelve fundamental principles of the religion from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."""
"97","Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī رضي الله عنه said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Indeed, before the Most Merciful (al-Raḥmān) is a Tablet containing three hundred and fifteen pathways of divine law (sharīʿah). The Most Merciful, Mighty and Majestic is He, says: 'By My Might and My Majesty! No servant among My servants comes to Me, associating nothing with Me and having fulfilled even one of them, except that he enters Paradise.'""**"
"98","ʿUbayd رضي الله عنه—who had the honor of companionship with the Prophet ﷺ—reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: > **""Faith comprises three hundred and thirty pathways of divine law; whoever fulfills any single pathway among them shall enter Paradise.""**"
"99","ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān رضي الله عنه said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Indeed, to Allah, Mighty and Majestic is He, belong one hundred and sixteen noble character traits; whoever comes to Him having embodied even one of them shall enter Paradise.""**"
"100","Anas ibn Mālik رضي الله عنه said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Indeed, to Allah, Mighty and Majestic is He, belongs a Tablet of green chrysolite beneath the Throne, upon which He has inscribed: 'I am Allah, there is no deity worthy of worship except Me, the Most Merciful of the merciful. I have created over three hundred and ten noble character traits; whoever comes with even one of them along with the testimony that there is no deity worthy of worship except Allah shall be admitted into Paradise.'""**"
"101","Ibn ʿAbbās رضي الله عنهما narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Islam consists of three hundred and thirteen pathways; there is not a single pathway among them with which a person meets Allah except that he will enter Paradise.""**"
"102","ʿUbayd رضي الله عنه — who was honored with companionship of the Prophet ﷺ — said that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Faith consists of three hundred and thirty pathways; whoever fulfills any one of them shall enter Paradise.""**"
"103","Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī رضي الله عنه narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: > **""Faith has seventy-odd branches: the highest of them is [the declaration that] there is no deity worthy of worship except Allah, and the lowest of them is removing a harmful object from the path.""**"
"104","Ibn ʿAbbās رضي الله عنهما said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Islam consists of ten shares — and ruined is he who has no share in it: testifying that there is no deity worthy of worship except Allah, which is the foundational creed; the second is prayer, which is the innate nature; the third is zakāh, which is purification; the fourth is fasting, which is a protective shield; the fifth is Ḥajj, which is the divine ordinance; the sixth is jihād, which is fortitude and strength; the seventh is enjoining good, which is loyalty and fulfillment; the eighth is forbidding wrong, which is the conclusive proof; the ninth is the unified community, which is harmony and affection; and the tenth is obedience, which is protection and inviolability.""**"
"105","ʿĀʾishah رضي الله عنها narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""There are three matters concerning which I swear: Allah will never treat one who has a share in Islam like one who has no share — and the foundational shares of Islam are three: prayer, fasting, and zakāh; no servant takes Allah as his Protector in this world and then Allah entrusts him to another on the Day of Resurrection; and no person loves a people except that Allah joins him with them. And as for the fourth, were I to swear upon it, I hope I would not sin: Allah does not conceal the faults of a servant in this world except that He will conceal them on the Day of Resurrection.""**"
"106","ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd رضي الله عنه narrated similar from the Prophet ﷺ: > **""There are three matters concerning which I swear: Allah will never treat one who has a share in Islam like one who has no share; no servant takes Allah as his Protector in this world and then Allah entrusts him to another on the Day of Resurrection; and no servant loves a people except that Allah joins him with them. And as for the fourth, were I to swear upon it, I hope I would not sin: Allah does not conceal the faults of a servant in this world except that He will conceal them on the Day of Resurrection.""**"
"107","Abū Umāmah رضي الله عنه said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""There are three matters concerning which, if I were to swear, I would certainly be truthful; and as for the fourth, if I were to swear upon it, I hope I would not sin: Allah will never treat one who has a share in Islam like one who has no share; Allah will never be the Protector of His servant in this world and then entrust him to another in the Hereafter; no servant loves a people except that Allah will resurrect him alongside them [and among them]; and the fourth: Allah does not conceal the faults of a servant in this world except that Allah will conceal them on the Day of Return.""**"
"108","ʿAlī رضي الله عنه narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: > **""Islam consists of eight shares: Islam [the testimony of faith] is a share, prayer is a share, zakāh is a share, Ḥajj is a share, jihād is a share, the fast of Ramadan is a share, enjoining good is a share, and forbidding wrong is a share. And ruined indeed is he who has no share in it.""**"
"109","Ḥudhayfah رضي الله عنه narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: > **""Islam consists of eight shares: Islam [the testimony of faith] is a share, prayer is a share, zakāh is a share, pilgrimage to the House is a share, fasting is a share, enjoining good is a share, forbidding wrong is a share, and jihād in the cause of Allah is a share. And ruined indeed is he who has no share in it.""**"
"110","ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd رضي الله عنه said: > **""There are three matters concerning which, if I were to swear, I would certainly be truthful: Allah will not treat one who has a share in Islam like one who has no share; Allah will not protect a servant in this world and then entrust him to another in the Hereafter; and no servant loves a people except that Allah will join him with them on the Day of Resurrection.""**"
"111","Abū al-Dardāʾ رضي الله عنه narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: > **""Indeed, Islam possesses radiance and landmarks like guiding beacons along the road. Its apex and its comprehensive essence are testifying that there is no deity worthy of worship except Allah and that Muḥammad is His slave and Messenger, establishing the prayer, paying zakāh, and performing ablution thoroughly.""**"
"112","Ibn ʿAbbās رضي الله عنهما said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was sitting in a gathering when Gabriel عليه السلام came to him and sat down before the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, placing the palms of his hands upon the knees of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said, ""O Messenger of Allah, tell me about Islam."" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Islam is that you surrender your face [your entire being] to Allah, Mighty and Majestic, and testify that there is no deity worthy of worship except Allah alone, without partner, and that Muḥammad is His slave and His Messenger.""** He asked, ""If I do that, have I embraced Islam?"" He ﷺ said: > **""If you do that, you have embraced Islam.""** He asked, ""O Messenger of Allah, tell me about faith (Īmān)."" He ﷺ said: > **""Faith is that you believe in Allah, the Last Day, the angels, the Scripture, the Prophets, death, life after death, and that you believe in Paradise, the Fire, the Reckoning, the Scale, and that you believe in the divine decree entirely, both the good of it and the evil of it.""** He asked, ""If I do that, have I believed?"" He ﷺ said: > **""If you do that, you have believed.""** He asked, ""O Messenger of Allah, tell me: what is excellence (Iḥsān)?"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Excellence is that you act for Allah as though you see Him, for even if you do not see Him, He surely sees you.""** He asked, ""O Messenger of Allah, tell me: when is the Hour?"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Glory be to Allah! Five matters belong to the unseen, which none knows except Allah: {Indeed, with Allah alone is knowledge of the Hour; He sends down the rain, and He knows what is in the wombs. No soul knows what it will earn tomorrow, and no soul knows in what land it will die. Indeed, Allah is All-Knowing, All-Aware} [Luqmān: 34]. However, if you wish, I can inform you of signs that will occur before it.""** He said, ""Yes, O Messenger of Allah, tell me."" He ﷺ said: > **""When you see the female slave give birth to her mistress — or her master — and you see the builders competing in constructing lofty buildings, and you see the barefoot, hungry, impoverished destitute become the leaders of the people — then those are among the signs of the Hour and its portents.""** He asked, ""O Messenger of Allah, who are the barefoot, hungry, impoverished destitute builders?"" He ﷺ said: > **""The Arab bedouins.""**"
"113","Ibn ʿĀmir — or Abū ʿĀmir, or Abū Mālik — narrated: While the Prophet ﷺ was sitting in a gathering with his Companions, Gabriel عليه السلام came to him in an unfamiliar form, appearing like a man from among the Muslims. He gave the greeting of salām, and the Prophet ﷺ returned it. Then Gabriel placed his hand upon the knees of the Prophet ﷺ and said, ""O Messenger of Allah, what is Islam?"" He ﷺ said: > **""That you surrender your face to Allah, testify that there is no deity worthy of worship except Allah and that Muḥammad is His slave and Messenger, establish prayer, and pay zakāh.""** He asked, ""If I do that, have I embraced Islam?"" He ﷺ said: > **""Yes.""** Then he asked, ""What is faith?"" He ﷺ said: > **""That you believe in Allah, the Last Day, the angels, the Scripture, the Prophets, death, life after death, Paradise, the Fire, the Reckoning, the Scale, and the divine decree entirely, both the good of it and the evil of it.""** He asked, ""If I do that, have I believed?"" He ﷺ said: > **""Yes.""** Then he asked, ""What is excellence, O Messenger of Allah?"" He ﷺ said: > **""That you worship Allah as though you see Him, for if you do not see Him, He surely sees you.""** He asked, ""If I do that, have I attained excellence?"" He ﷺ said: > **""Yes.""** The narrator said: We could hear the reply of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, but we could neither see the one speaking to him nor hear his words. He asked, ""When is the Hour, O Messenger of Allah?"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Glory be to Allah! Five matters belong to the unseen, which none knows except Allah: {Indeed, with Allah alone is knowledge of the Hour; He sends down the rain, and He knows what is in the wombs. No soul knows what it will earn tomorrow, and no soul knows in what land it will die. Indeed, Allah is All-Knowing, All-Aware} [Luqmān: 34]. However, if you wish, I can tell you of two signs that will occur before it.""** He said, ""Tell me."" He ﷺ said: > **""When you see the female slave give birth to her master, and the builders construct increasingly lofty buildings, and the impoverished, barefoot destitute become the leaders of the people.""** He asked, ""And who are they, O Messenger of Allah?"" He ﷺ said: > **""The Arab bedouins.""** The narrator said: Then the man turned and departed. When we could no longer see his path, the Prophet ﷺ said: > **""Glory be to Allah! That was Gabriel; he came to teach the people their religion. By the One in Whose Hand is the soul of Muḥammad, he never came to me previously without me recognizing him, except on this occasion.""**"
"114","Anas رضي الله عنه said: While the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was sitting with his Companions, a man wearing travel garments arrived, making his way through the people until he sat directly before the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He placed his hand upon the knee of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, ""O Muḥammad, what is Islam?"" He ﷺ said: > **""Testifying that there is no deity worthy of worship except Allah alone, without partner, and that Muḥammad is His slave and Messenger, establishing prayer, paying zakāh, fasting the month of Ramadan, and performing pilgrimage to the House if you are able to find a way to it.""** He asked, ""If I do that, am I a Muslim?"" He ﷺ said: > **""Yes.""** He said, ""You have spoken the truth."" The Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ remarked, ""Look at him: he asks him and then confirms his truthfulness, as though he knows better than him!"" Yet they did not know the man. Then he asked, ""O Muḥammad, what is faith?"" He ﷺ said: > **""Faith is that you believe in Allah, the Last Day, the angels, the Scripture, the Prophets, death, the Resurrection, the Reckoning, Paradise, the Fire, and the divine decree entirely.""** He asked, ""If I do that, am I a believer?"" He ﷺ said: > **""Yes.""** He said, ""You have spoken the truth. O Muḥammad, what is excellence?"" He ﷺ said: > **""That you fear Allah as though you see Him, for if you do not see Him, He surely sees you.""** He asked, ""If I do that, am I a person of excellence?"" He ﷺ said: > **""Yes.""** He said, ""You have spoken the truth. O Muḥammad, when is the Hour?"" He ﷺ said: > **""The one questioned about it knows no more than the questioner.""** The man then turned away and departed. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Bring the man back to me!""** They went after him to seek him, but they saw nothing. They returned to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, ""O Messenger of Allah, we went after the man and sought him, but we found nothing."" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""That was Gabriel; he came to you to teach you your religion.""**"
"115","Ibn ʿUmar رضي الله عنهما narrated: A man came to Ibn ʿUmar and said, ""O Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, we travel and encounter people who claim: 'There is no divine decree (qadar).'"" Ibn ʿUmar said, ""When you meet those people, inform them that Ibn ʿUmar is free of them. We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when a man with a handsome face, pleasant scent, and clean white garments approached. He said, 'Peace be upon you, O Messenger of Allah. May I come close to you?' He ﷺ said: > **'Come close.'** So he drew closer. He repeated this several times until his knees touched the knees of the Prophet ﷺ. He said, 'O Messenger of Allah, what is Islam?' He ﷺ said: > **'Testifying that there is no deity worthy of worship except Allah and that Muḥammad is the Messenger of Allah, establishing prayer, paying zakāh, performing pilgrimage to the House, fasting Ramadan, and performing the ritual bath after sexual impurity (janābah).'** He asked, 'If I do that, am I a Muslim?' He ﷺ said: > **'Yes.'** He said, 'You have spoken the truth. Then what is faith?' He ﷺ said: > **'Faith is that you believe in Allah, His angels, His Scriptures, His Messengers, Paradise, the Fire, and the divine decree — both its good and its evil, its sweet and its bitter — as being from Allah.'** He asked, 'If I do that, am I a believer?' He ﷺ said: > **'Yes.'** He said, 'You have spoken the truth. Then what is excellence?' He ﷺ said: > **'That you worship Allah as though you see Him, for even if you do not see Him, He surely sees you.'** He asked, 'If I do that, am I a person of excellence?' He ﷺ said: > **'Yes.'** He said, 'You have spoken the truth.' We thought: We have never seen a man more handsome of face, sweeter in scent, or showing greater reverence to the Prophet ﷺ, and yet saying to the Prophet ﷺ: 'You have spoken the truth!' Then the Prophet ﷺ said: > **'Bring the man back to me!'** We stood up, and I went out toward one of the roads of Medina, but we saw nothing. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **'Do you know who this was?'** They said, 'Allah and His Messenger know best.' He ﷺ said: > **'This was Gabriel, teaching you the rituals of your religion. He never came to me in any form without me recognizing him, except in this form.'**"""
"116","Jarīr ibn ʿAbdillāh رضي الله عنه said: We set out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. When we emerged from Medina, behold, a rider was spurring his mount toward us. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""It is as though this rider is heading toward you""** — meaning he intends to come to us. The man reached us and gave salām, and we returned his greeting. The Prophet ﷺ said to him: > **""From where have you come?""** He said, ""From my family, my children, and my clan."" He ﷺ asked: > **""And where do you intend to go?""** He said, ""I intend to reach the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."" He ﷺ said: > **""You have indeed reached him.""** The man said, ""O Messenger of Allah, teach me: what is faith?"" He ﷺ said: > **""You must testify that there is no deity worthy of worship except Allah and that Muḥammad is the Messenger of Allah, establish prayer, pay zakāh, fast Ramadan, and perform pilgrimage to the House.""** The man said, ""I affirm this."" Then suddenly, the foot of his camel stepped into a rodent's burrow, throwing the mount and throwing the man. He landed on the crown of his head and died. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Bring the man to me!""** ʿAmmār ibn Yāsir and Ḥudhayfah ibn al-Yamān leaped toward him, sat him up, and said, ""O Messenger of Allah, the man has passed away."" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ turned his face away from them both. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to them: > **""Did you not see me turning away from the man? Indeed, I saw two angels placing the fruits of Paradise into his mouth, so I knew that he died hungry.""** Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""This man, by Allah, is among those about whom Allah, Mighty and Majestic, said: {Those who have believed and not mixed their belief with injustice - those will have security, and they are [rightly] guided} [Al-Anʿām: 82].""** Then he ﷺ said: > **""Attend to your brother.""** We carried him to water, washed him, scented him, shrouded him, and carried him to the grave. He ﷺ said: > **""Dig a laḥd (niche grave) and do not dig a shaqq (open trench).""** And in another narration: > **""This is one who worked little and was rewarded immensely.""**"
"117","Jarīr رضي الله عنه said: When the Prophet ﷺ was sent, I came to him to pledge allegiance. He ﷺ said: > **""For what reason have you come to us, O Jarīr?""** I said, ""I have come to embrace Islam at your hands."" So he called me to testify that there is no deity worthy of worship except Allah and that I am the Messenger of Allah, to establish the prescribed prayer, to pay the obligatory zakāh, and to believe in the divine decree, both its good and its evil. Jarīr said: He ﷺ then cast his cloak to me, turned to his Companions, and said: > **""When the noble person of a people comes to you, honor him.""**"
"118","Bashīr ibn al-Khaṣāṣiyyah al-Sadūsī رضي الله عنه said: I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to pledge allegiance to him. He stipulated upon me: > **""Testify that there is no deity worthy of worship except Allah and that Muḥammad is His slave and Messenger, pray the five daily prayers, fast Ramadan, pay zakāh, perform pilgrimage to the House, and strive in the cause of Allah (jihād).""** I said, ""O Messenger of Allah, as for two of these, I cannot endure them: zakāh, for by Allah, I possess only ten camels which provide the milk and transport for my household; and as for jihād, people claim that whoever turns his back incurs the wrath of Allah, and I fear that if battle confronts me, my soul may quail and I will dread death."" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ grasped his hand, shook it, and said: > **""No charity and no jihād — by what means then will you enter Paradise?!""** So I pledged allegiance to him upon all of them."
"119","Anas ibn Mālik رضي الله عنه narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Whoever testifies that there is no deity worthy of worship except Allah and that I am the Messenger of Allah, being sincere in both, and prays, fasts, pays zakāh, and performs pilgrimage to the House — Allah Almighty has forbidden him to the Fire.""**"
"120","A man from Banū ʿĀmir asked permission to enter upon the Prophet ﷺ, saying, ""May I enter?"" using an improper expression. The Prophet ﷺ said to his servant girl: > **""Go out to him, for he does not know how to seek permission properly. Tell him to say: 'Peace be upon you (al-salāmu ʿalaykum), may I enter?'""** The man said: I heard him saying that, so I said, ""Peace be upon you, may I enter?"" The Prophet ﷺ granted permission, and I entered. I asked, ""With what message have you come to us?"" He ﷺ said: > **""I have not brought you anything except good. I have brought you [the command] that you worship Allah alone without partner — Shuʿbah said: I believe he said: alone without partner — that you abandon al-Lāt and al-ʿUzzā, that you pray five prayers by night and day, that you fast one month of the year, that you perform pilgrimage to the House, and that you take from the wealth of your rich and return it to your poor.""** The man asked, ""Does there remain anything of the unseen that you do not know?"" He ﷺ said: > **""Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has known abundant good, and indeed of the unseen is that which none knows except Allah, Mighty and Majestic — the five: {Indeed, with Allah alone is knowledge of the Hour; He sends down the rain, and He knows what is in the wombs. No soul knows what it will earn tomorrow, and no soul knows in what land it will die. Indeed, Allah is All-Knowing, All-Aware} [Luqmān: 34].""**"
"121","A man from Qays known as Ibn al-Muntafiq رضي الله عنه said: The description of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was given to me, so I sought him in Mecca. I was told: ""He is in Minā."" I sought him in Minā and was told: ""He is at ʿArafāt."" I reached him and pressed through the crowd until I reached his side. I took hold of the halter of the riding camel of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ — or he said: its rein — until the necks of our mounts intertwined. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not rebuke me nor reprimand me. I said, ""There are two questions I ask of you: What will save me from the Fire, and what will admit me into Paradise?"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ looked up toward the sky, then lowered his head, and then turned his face toward me. He said: > **""Though you were brief in your question, you have asked a momentous and profound matter! Comprehend from me then: Worship Allah and do not associate anything with Him, establish the prescribed prayer, pay the obligatory zakāh, fast Ramadan, and whatever you love for people to do to you, do it to them; and whatever you hate that people should do to you, spare people from it.""** Then he ﷺ said: > **""Release the path of the riding camel.""**"
"122","Al-Mughīrah ibn Saʿd reported from his father or his uncle رضي الله عنه: I came to the Prophet ﷺ at ʿArafah and took hold of the rein or halter of his she-camel. People began pushing me away from him, but the Prophet ﷺ said: > **""Leave him, for he has come with a genuine need.""** I said, ""Inform me of a deed that will draw me near to Paradise and distance me from the Fire."" He lifted his head toward the sky and then said: > **""Though you were concise, you have asked something momentous and profound: Worship Allah without associating anything with Him, establish prayer, pay zakāh, perform pilgrimage to the House, fast Ramadan, treat people as you would love to be treated by them, and whatever you dislike for yourself, spare people from it. Release the rein of the she-camel.""**"
"123","Ḥujayr narrated from his father, whose kunyah was Abū al-Muntafiq رضي الله عنه: I came to Mecca and asked about the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. They said, ""He is at ʿArafah."" So I went to him and drew close until the neck of my mount intertwined with the neck of his mount. I said, ""O Messenger of Allah, inform me of that which will save me from the punishment of Allah and admit me into His Paradise."" He ﷺ said: > **""Worship Allah without associating anything with Him, establish the prescribed prayer, pay the obligatory zakāh, perform Ḥajj and ʿUmrah, fast Ramadan, and observe what you love for people to do to you and do it to them; and whatever you dislike for them to do to you, spare them from it.""**"
"124","ʿAlī رضي الله عنه narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Allah sent Yaḥyā ibn Zakariyyā عليهما السلام to the Children of Israel with five commandments. When Allah sent ʿĪsā عليه السلام, Allah, Blessed and Exalted is He, said: 'O ʿĪsā, say to Yaḥyā ibn Zakariyyā: Either you convey that with which you were sent to the Children of Israel, or I shall convey it to them.' So Yaḥyā went forth until he came to the Children of Israel and said: > 'Indeed, Allah, Blessed and Exalted is He, commands you to worship Him and not associate anything with Him. The parable of that is like a man who freed a slave, treated him kindly, and gave him wealth; yet the slave departed, was ungrateful for his favor, and gave his allegiance to someone else. > And indeed, Allah commands you to establish prayer. The parable of that is like a man captured by the enemy who intended to execute him, so he pleaded: ""Do not kill me, for I possess a treasure and I will ransom myself."" Thus he gave them his treasure and saved himself. > And indeed, Allah, Blessed and Exalted is He, commands you to give charity. The parable of that is like a man marching toward his enemy who has taken a shield for battle, so he cares not from which side he is attacked. > And indeed, Allah commands you to recite the Scripture. The parable of that is like a group of people inside their fortress toward whom their enemy advances; they stationed defenders at every corner of the fortress, so the enemy cannot approach from any corner without defenders repelling them from the fortress. Such is the parable of the one who recites the Qur'an: he remains continuously within the most impregnable fortress.'""**"
"125","Suwayd ibn Ḥujayr said: My maternal uncle رضي الله عنه narrated to me: I met the Prophet ﷺ between ʿArafah and al-Muzdalifah and took hold of the halter of his she-camel. I said, ""O Messenger of Allah, what will bring me close to Paradise and distance me from the Fire?"" He ﷺ said: > **""By Allah, though you were brief in your question, you have asked something momentous and profound: Establish the prescribed prayer, pay the obligatory zakāh, perform pilgrimage to the House, and whatever you love that people should do to you, do it to them; and whatever you dislike that people should do to you, spare people from it. Release the rein of the she-camel.""**"
"126","Abū al-Dardāʾ رضي الله عنه narrated: A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, ""O Messenger of Allah, what is the safeguard of this matter [religion], its firm handhold, and its secure bond?"" He ﷺ said: > **""Devote your worship purely to Allah Almighty, establish your five daily prayers, pay the zakāh on your wealth with a cheerful soul, and fast your month; you shall enter the Paradise of your Lord.""**"
"127","ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr رضي الله عنهما reported that he heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: > **""Whoever meets Allah Almighty on the Day of Resurrection with the five daily prayers, the fast of Ramadan, and performing the ritual bath from sexual impurity (janābah) is truly a servant of Allah; and whoever acts treacherously regarding any of them is truly an enemy of Allah.""**"
"128","Jarīr رضي الله عنه said: A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and asked him about Islam. He ﷺ said: > **""That you testify that there is no deity worthy of worship except Allah and that Muḥammad is the Messenger of Allah, establish prayer, pay zakāh, fast Ramadan, love for people what you love for yourself, and dislike for them what you dislike for yourself.""**"
"129","Abū Mālik al-Ashʿarī رضي الله عنه narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Whoever does not associate anything with Allah after having believed in Him, establishes prayer, pays the obligatory zakāh, fasts Ramadan, and listens and obeys, and dies upon that state — Paradise becomes obligatory for him.""**"
"130","Ḥakīm ibn Muʿāwiyah رضي الله عنه came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, ""O Messenger of Allah, with what has our Lord sent you?"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""That you worship Allah and associate nothing with Him, establish prayer, and pay zakāh; and every Muslim is sacred to another Muslim. O Ḥakīm ibn Muʿāwiyah, this is your religion: wherever you may be, it will suffice you.""**"
"131","Ibn ʿAbbās رضي الله عنهما said: The Prophet ﷺ said: > **""Whoever establishes prayer, pays zakāh, performs pilgrimage to the House, fasts Ramadan, and honors the guest shall enter Paradise.""**"
"132","Samurah رضي الله عنه said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Establish prayer, pay zakāh, perform Ḥajj and ʿUmrah, and remain upright, and matters will remain upright for you.""**"
"133","Abū Umāmah رضي الله عنه said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""There are six deeds: whoever arrives with any one of them will come possessing a covenant on the Day of Resurrection, with each one of them declaring: 'He used to act upon me!' — zakāh, prayer, Ḥajj, fasting, fulfilling trusts, and maintaining ties of kinship.""**"
"134","Abū Umāmah رضي الله عنه narrated: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded his Companions at the time of the night prayer (ʿIshāʾ): ""Assemble for prayer tomorrow morning, for I have a need to address to you."" A group among them said to one another, ""O so-and-so, you take responsibility for the first statement spoken by the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and you take responsibility for the one that follows it,"" so that nothing of the words of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ would escape them. When they finished their morning prayer, he ﷺ said: > **""Have you assembled as I commanded you?""** They said, ""Yes, O Messenger of Allah."" He ﷺ said: > **""Worship your Lord and do not associate anything with Him! Have you understood this? Have you understood this? Have you understood this?""** They said, ""Yes."" He ﷺ said: > **""Establish prayer and pay zakāh! Establish prayer and pay zakāh! Establish prayer and pay zakāh! Have you understood this? Have you understood this? Have you understood this?""** They said, ""Yes."" He ﷺ said: > **""Listen and obey! Listen and obey! Listen and obey! Have you understood this? Have you understood this? Have you understood this?""** They said, ""Yes."" The narrator said: We had anticipated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ would deliver a lengthy address, but when we examined his speech, behold, he had gathered for us the entirety of religion."
"135","ʿAmr ibn Murrah al-Juhanī رضي الله عنه said: A man from Quḍāʿah came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, ""I bear witness that there is no deity worthy of worship except Allah and that you are the Messenger of Allah, I pray the five daily prayers, I fast Ramadan during its appointed time, and I pay zakāh."" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Whoever dies upon this is among the affirmers of truth (al-Ṣiddīqīn) and the martyrs (al-Shuhadāʾ).""**"
"136","Muʿādh ibn Jabal رضي الله عنه narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: > **""Whoever fasts Ramadan, prays the five daily prayers, and performs pilgrimage to the House""** — the narrator said: I do not know whether he mentioned zakāh or not — **""it is an established right upon Allah to forgive him.""** I said, ""Shall I inform the people of this?"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Leave the people to strive in deeds! For indeed, Paradise has one hundred levels, between every two levels is a distance like that between heaven and earth; and al-Firdaws is its highest and most central level, above which is the Throne of the Most Merciful, and from it gush forth the rivers of Paradise. So when you ask Allah, ask Him for al-Firdaws.""**"
"137","Jarīr رضي الله عنه said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Islam is built upon five: testifying that there is no deity worthy of worship except Allah, establishing prayer, paying zakāh, performing pilgrimage to the House, and fasting Ramadan.""**"
"138","ʿUmārah ibn Ḥazm رضي الله عنه said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""There are four obligations which Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has ordained in Islam; whoever comes with three of them, they will not avail him anything until he brings them all together: prayer, zakāh, the fast of Ramadan, and pilgrimage to the House.""**"
"139","Abū al-Dardāʾ رضي الله عنه said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""There are five deeds: whoever comes with them accompanied by faith shall enter Paradise: whoever diligently observes the five daily prayers — with their ablutions, their bowings, their prostrations, and their appointed times — fasts Ramadan, performs pilgrimage to the House if he is able to find a way, pays zakāh with a cheerful soul, and fulfills the trust.""** It was said, ""O Prophet of Allah, what is the fulfillment of the trust?"" He ﷺ said: > **""Performing the ritual bath from sexual impurity (janābah), for indeed Allah has not entrusted the son of Adam with any aspect of his religion other than it.""**"
"140","Ibn ʿAbbās رضي الله عنهما narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: > **""The firm bonds of Islam and the foundations of religion upon which Islam is established are three; whoever abandons any one of them is an unbeliever regarding it, whose blood is lawful: testifying that there is no deity worthy of worship except Allah, the prescribed prayer, and fasting Ramadan.""** Then Ibn ʿAbbās said: ""You may find a person possessing abundant wealth who does not pay zakāh; he does not thereby become a disbeliever whose blood is lawful. And you may find a person possessing abundant wealth who does not perform Ḥajj; he does not thereby become a disbeliever whose blood is lawful."""
"141","Maʿn ibn Yazīd رضي الله عنه said: A bedouin came and took hold of the halter of the she-camel of the Prophet ﷺ and said, ""O Prophet of Allah, direct me to an action that will bring me near to Paradise and distance me from the Fire."" He ﷺ said: > **""You have asked concisely, yet you have addressed something momentous: Worship Allah and associate nothing with Him, pray the five daily prayers, fast Ramadan, and whatever you dislike for people to do to you, dislike it for them.""**"
"142","ʿUbaydullāh ibn ʿUmayr al-Laythī reported from his father رضي الله عنه that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said during the Farewell Pilgrimage: > **""Indeed, the allies of Allah are those who pray — whoever establishes the five daily prayers which Allah has ordained upon him, fasts Ramadan seeking Allah's reward, pays zakāh seeking reward with a cheerful soul, and avoids the major destructive sins which Allah has forbidden.""** A man among his Companions asked, ""O Messenger of Allah, how many are the major sins?"" He ﷺ said: > **""They are nine, the greatest of which are: associating partners with Allah, killing a believer without right, fleeing from the battlefield, slandering chaste women, practicing sorcery, consuming the property of an orphan, consuming usury (ribā), disobedience to Muslim parents, and violating the sanctity of the Ancient Inviolable House — your qiblah in life and death. No man dies having avoided these major sins, while establishing prayer and paying zakāh, except that he will accompany Muḥammad ﷺ in the heart of Paradise, whose gates have leaves of pure gold.""**"
"143","ʿAbdullāh ibn Shaqīq reported from a man from the Balqayn tribe رضي الله عنه: I came to the Prophet ﷺ while he was in Wādī al-Qurā and asked, ""O Messenger of Allah, what have you been commanded with?"" He ﷺ said: > **""I have been commanded that you worship Allah and associate nothing with Him, establish prayer, and pay zakāh.""** I asked, ""O Messenger of Allah, who are those who incurred divine wrath?"" He ﷺ said: > **""The Jews.""** I asked, ""Who are the misguided?"" He ﷺ said: > **""The Christians.""** I asked, ""To whom do the spoils of war belong, O Messenger of Allah?"" He ﷺ said: > **""One share belongs to Allah, Mighty and Majestic, and four shares belong to these [soldiers].""** I asked, ""Is anyone more entitled to the spoils than another?"" He ﷺ said: > **""No, not even an arrow that one of you retrieves from his side; he has no greater right to it than anyone else.""**"
"144","ʿItbān ibn Mālik رضي الله عنه said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Whoever testifies that there is no deity worthy of worship except Allah and that I am the Messenger of Allah, being sincere in both, and prays the five daily prayers, Allah will forbid his face to the Fire.""**"
"145","Zayd Abū Sallām reported from a freed slave of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""How excellent! How excellent are five things — how heavy they are on the Scale: 'Lā ilāha illallāh' (There is no deity worthy of worship except Allah), 'Allāhu Akbar' (Allah is the Greatest), 'Subḥānallāh' (Glory be to Allah), 'Al-ḥamdu lillāh' (All praise is due to Allah), and a righteous child who dies and whose parent patiently anticipates reward from Allah.""** And he ﷺ said: > **""How excellent! How excellent are five things: whoever meets Allah possessing firm conviction in them shall enter Paradise: believing in Allah, the Last Day, Paradise, the Fire, the Resurrection after death, and the Reckoning.""**"
"146","ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb رضي الله عنه reported that he heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: > **""Whoever dies believing in Allah and the Last Day, it will be said to him: 'Enter through whichever of the eight gates of Paradise you wish.'""**"
"147","Ḥudhayfah رضي الله عنه said: I came to the Prophet ﷺ while al-ʿAbbās was sitting on his right and Fāṭimah رضي الله عنها was sitting on his left. He ﷺ said: > **""O Fāṭimah, daughter of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, do good deeds for Allah, for I cannot avail you anything before Allah on the Day of Resurrection!""** He repeated that three times. Then he ﷺ said: > **""O ʿAbbās ibn ʿAbd al-Muṭṭalib, uncle of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, do good deeds for Allah, for I cannot avail you anything before Allah on the Day of Resurrection!""** He repeated that three times. Then he ﷺ said: > **""O Ḥudhayfah, come near.""** So I drew near. Then he said: > **""O Ḥudhayfah, come near.""** So I drew near. Then he said: > **""O Ḥudhayfah, whoever testifies that there is no deity worthy of worship except Allah and that I am the Messenger of Allah, and believes in that which I have brought, Allah has forbidden him to the Fire and Paradise has become obligatory for him.""** I said, ""O Messenger of Allah, shall I keep this confidential or proclaim it?"" He ﷺ said: > **""Proclaim it.""**"
"148","Abū Hurayrah رضي الله عنه said: I was walking with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in a date-palm orchard belonging to one of the people of Medina, when he said: > **""O Abū Hurayrah, the possessors of abundant wealth are ruined, except for the one who spends like this, and like this, and like this""** — repeating it three times, gesturing with his cupped hands to his right, to his left, and before him — **""and how few they are!""** Then he walked for a while and said: > **""O Abū Hurayrah, shall I not direct you to a treasure from the treasures of Paradise?""** I said, ""Certainly, O Messenger of Allah."" He ﷺ said: > **""Lā ḥawla wa lā quwwata illā billāh, wa lā malja'a min Allāhi illā ilayh (There is no power nor might except with Allah, and there is no refuge from Allah except in Him).""** Then he walked for a while and asked: > **""Do you know what is the right of Allah upon people?""** I said, ""Allah and His Messenger know best."" He ﷺ said: > **""The right of Allah upon people is that they worship Him and associate nothing with Him; and when they do that, it is a duty upon Allah not to punish them.""**"
"149","Abū Hurayrah رضي الله عنه said: Muʿādh ibn Jabal was riding behind the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, when the Prophet ﷺ asked: > **""What is the right of Allah upon the servants?""** Muʿādh said, ""Allah and His Messenger know best."" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""His right upon them is that they worship Him and associate nothing with Him.""** The Prophet ﷺ then asked: > **""Do you know what is the right of the servants upon Allah when they worship Him and do not associate anything with Him?""** Muʿādh said, ""Allah and His Messenger know best."" He ﷺ said: > **""Their right upon Him is that He admits them into Paradise.""** Muʿādh said, ""O Messenger of Allah, shall I not go to the people and give them glad tidings?!"" The Prophet ﷺ said: > **""No, leave them to strive in good deeds.""**"
"150","Ḥudhayfah رضي الله عنه said: I was riding behind the Prophet ﷺ when he said: > **""O Ḥudhayfah, do you know what is the right of Allah upon the servants?""** I said, ""Allah and His Messenger know best."" He ﷺ said: > **""That they worship Him and associate nothing with Him.""** Then he said: > **""O Ḥudhayfah!""** I said, ""At your service, O Messenger of Allah."" He ﷺ said: > **""Do you know what is the right of the servants upon Allah Almighty when they do that?""** I said, ""Allah and His Messenger know best."" He ﷺ said: > **""That He forgives them.""**"
"151","Anas ibn Mālik رضي الله عنه narrated from the Prophet ﷺ, who related from his Lord: > **""There are four characteristics: one of them is for Me, one is for you, one is between Me and you, and one is between you and My servants. As for the one that is for Me: you worship Me without associating anything with Me. As for the one that is for you: whatever good deed you perform, I shall reward you for it. As for the one that is between Me and you: from you is supplication and upon Me is the response. And as for the one between you and My servants: be pleased for them with that which you are pleased with for yourself.""**"
"152","Salmān رضي الله عنه said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Allah says: 'O son of Adam, there are three characteristics: one is for Me, one is for you, and one is between Me and you. As for the one that is for Me: you worship Me without associating anything with Me. As for the one that is for you: whatever deed you perform, I shall reward you for it, and if I forgive, then I am the Most Forgiving, the Most Merciful. And as for the one between Me and you: upon you is supplication, and upon Me is response and granting.'""**"
"153","Ibn ʿAbbās رضي الله عنهما said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Allah, Mighty and Majestic, says: 'I do not consider the right of My servant until My servant considers My right.'""**"
"154","ʿUtbah ibn ʿAbd رضي الله عنه narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""If a man were to fall upon his face in prostration from the day he was born until the day he dies, seeking the pleasure of Allah, Mighty and Majestic, he would surely consider it insignificant on the Day of Resurrection.""**"
"155","Muḥammad ibn Abī ʿAmrah رضي الله عنه — who was among the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ — said: > **""If a man were to be dragged upon his face in obedience to Allah, Mighty and Majestic, from the day he was born until the day he dies of old age, he would surely deem it insignificant on that Day, and he would desperately wish to be returned to the world so that he might increase in reward and recompense.""**"
"156","Jābir ibn ʿAbdillāh رضي الله عنهما said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""There is not in the seven heavens the space of a footstep, nor a handspan, nor a palm, except that therein is an angel standing or an angel prostrating. When the Day of Resurrection arrives, they will all say: 'Glory be to You! We have not worshipped You as You truly deserve to be worshipped, except that we have never associated anything with You.'""**"
"157","Buraydah رضي الله عنه said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""There is nothing in existence except that it is more obedient to Allah Almighty than the son of Adam.""**"
"158","ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr رضي الله عنهما said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Indeed, faith wears out in the chest of one of you just as a garment wears out; so ask Allah Almighty to renew faith in your hearts.""**"
"159","Abū Hurayrah رضي الله عنه said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Renew your faith!""** It was said, ""O Messenger of Allah, how do we renew our faith?"" He ﷺ said: > **""Say abundantly: 'Lā ilāha illallāh' (There is no deity worthy of worship except Allah).""**"
"160","Anas رضي الله عنه said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to say: > **""Islam is outward, while faith is in the heart.""** Then he would point with his hand to his chest three times and say: > **""Taqwā (God-consciousness) is here! Taqwā is here!""**"
"161","Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī رضي الله عنه narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""The believers in the world are of three categories: those who believe in Allah and His Messenger, then never doubt, and strive with their wealth and their lives in the cause of Allah; the one whom people trust with their wealth and their lives; and the one who, when greed presents itself to him, abandons it for the sake of Allah, Mighty and Majestic.""**"
"162","Ibn ʿAbbās رضي الله عنهما said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""It is sufficient faith for a person that he says: 'I am pleased with Allah as my Lord, with Muḥammad as my Messenger, and with Islam as my religion.'""**"
"163","Jābir رضي الله عنه said: The Prophet ﷺ commanded Suḥaym to proclaim among the people: > **""None shall enter Paradise except a believer.""**"
"164","ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd رضي الله عنه said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Indeed, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has distributed your character among you just as He has distributed your provision among you. And indeed, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, gives worldly wealth to whom He loves and to whom He does not love, but He does not grant religion except to whom He loves. So whoever has been granted religion by Him, He has loved him. By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, no servant has truly embraced Islam until his heart and tongue submit, and he does not truly believe until his neighbor is safe from his harmful conduct (bawāʾiq).""** I asked, ""And what is his harmful conduct, O Prophet of Allah?"" He ﷺ said: > **""His deceit and his oppression. A person does not acquire wealth from unlawful means and spend from it and have it blessed for him; nor does he give charity from it and have it accepted from him; nor does he leave it behind his back except that it will be his provision heading to the Fire. Indeed, Allah does not erase evil with evil, but rather He erases evil with good; indeed, the foul does not erase the foul.""**"
"165","Anas ibn Mālik رضي الله عنه narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""The faith of a servant will not become upright until his heart becomes upright, and his heart will not become upright until his tongue becomes upright; and a servant will not enter Paradise until his neighbor is safe from his harmful conduct.""**"
"166","Abū Razīn al-ʿUqaylī رضي الله عنه said: I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and asked, ""O Messenger of Allah, how does Allah bring the dead to life?"" He ﷺ said: > **""Have you ever passed by a barren valley in your land, and then passed by it later when it was lush and fertile?""** He said, ""Yes."" He ﷺ said: > **""Thus is the Resurrection.""** He asked, ""O Messenger of Allah, what is faith?"" He ﷺ said: > **""That you testify that there is no deity worthy of worship except Allah alone, without partner, and that Muḥammad is His slave and Messenger; that Allah and His Messenger are more beloved to you than anything else; that being burned in the fire is more beloved to you than associating partners with Allah; and that you love an unrelated person loving him solely for the sake of Allah. When you are like that, the love of faith will have entered your heart just as the love of water enters the thirsty person on a scorching day.""** I asked, ""O Messenger of Allah, how can I know that I am a believer?"" He ﷺ said: > **""There is no servant from my nation — or this nation — who performs a good deed and knows that it is good and that Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will reward him for it with good, nor does he commit an evil deed and seeks forgiveness from Allah, Mighty and Majestic, knowing that He forgives — except that he is indeed a believer.""**"
"167","ʿAmr ibn ʿAbasah رضي الله عنه said: I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and asked, ""O Messenger of Allah, who is with you in this matter?"" He ﷺ said: > **""A free man and a slave.""** I asked, ""What is Islam?"" He ﷺ said: > **""Pleasant speech and providing food.""** I asked, ""What is faith?"" He ﷺ said: > **""Patience and generosity.""** I asked, ""Which Islam is best?"" He ﷺ said: > **""The one from whose tongue and hand Muslims are safe.""** I asked, ""Which faith is best?"" He ﷺ said: > **""Noble character.""** I asked, ""Which prayer is best?"" He ﷺ said: > **""Lengthy standing in devotion.""** I asked, ""Which emigration (hijrah) is best?"" He ﷺ said: > **""That you abandon what your Lord dislikes.""**"
"168","Anas رضي الله عنه said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""The believer is the one whom people trust, the Muslim is the one from whose tongue and hand Muslims are safe, and the emigrant (muhājir) is the one who abandons evil. By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, no servant will enter Paradise whose neighbor is not safe from his harmful conduct.""**"
"169","Sahl ibn Muʿādh narrated from his father رضي الله عنه that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Indeed, the one who attains safety [or the true Muslim] is he from whose tongue and hand people are safe.""**"
"170","Anas رضي الله عنه said: The Prophet ﷺ was asked about the believer, and he said: > **""The one whose neighbor is safe from him and does not fear his harmful conduct.""**"
"171","Ibn ʿAbbās رضي الله عنهما said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon ʿUmar while several of his Companions were with him. He ﷺ asked: > **""Are you believers?""** They remained silent. He repeated it three times. At the end, ʿUmar said, ""Yes, we believe in that which you have brought to us, we praise Allah in prosperity, we show patience in adversity, and we believe in the divine decree."" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""You are believers, by the Lord of the Kaʿbah!""**"
"172","ʿAbdullāh ibn Zayd al-Anṣārī رضي الله عنه said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""When one of you is asked: 'Are you a believer?' let him not express doubt.""**"
"173","ʿAlqamah reported: A man said in the presence of ʿAbdullāh [ibn Masʿūd رضي الله عنه], ""Indeed, I am a believer."" ʿAbdullāh said: > **""Why do you not also say: 'Indeed, I am in Paradise'? Rather, we say: 'We have believed in Allah, His angels, His Scriptures, and His Messengers.'""**"
"174","ʿUthmān ibn Suhayl ibn Ḥunayf رضي الله عنه said: Before the Messenger of Allah ﷺ arrived from Mecca, he used to call the people to faith in Allah and belief in Him as a statement without stipulated actions, while the qiblah was toward Bayt al-Maqdis (Jerusalem). When he migrated to us, the religious obligations were revealed; Medina abrogated Mecca and the previous condition of mere verbal affirmation, and the Sacred House (the Kaʿbah) abrogated Bayt al-Maqdis. Thus faith became both statement and action."
"175","Abū Umāmah رضي الله عنه said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""There are three qualities: whoever possesses them will taste the sweetness of faith: that Allah and His Messenger are more beloved to him than anything else, that he loves a person loving him solely for the sake of Allah, and that he hates returning to disbelief after Allah has rescued him from it just as he hates being cast into the Fire.""**"
"176","Qatādah reported that Ibn Masʿūd رضي الله عنه said: > **""There are three qualities; whoever possesses them will find through them the sweetness of faith: abandoning arguing even when one is in the right, abandoning lying even in jest, and knowing that whatever has befallen him could never have missed him, and whatever has missed him could never have befallen him.""**"
"177","Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd reported from Nawfal ibn Masʿūd, who said: We entered upon Anas ibn Mālik رضي الله عنه and said, ""Narrate to us what you heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."" He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: > **""There are three qualities; whoever possesses them is forbidden to the Fire and the Fire is forbidden to him: faith in Allah, love for Allah Blessed and Exalted, and that being cast into the fire and burnt is more beloved to him than returning to disbelief.""**"
"178","Anas ibn Mālik رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""There are three qualities; whoever possesses them has tasted the flavor of faith: he to whom nothing is more beloved than Allah and His Messenger; he to whom being burned in the fire is more beloved than apostatizing from his religion; and he who loves for the sake of Allah and hates for the sake of Allah.""**"
"179","Abū Umāmah رضي الله عنه reported: A man asked, ""O Messenger of Allah, who is the Muslim?"" He ﷺ said: > **""The one from whose tongue and hand the Muslims are safe.""**"
"180","Bilāl ibn al-Ḥārith al-Muzanī رضي الله عنه reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: > **""The Muslim is the one from whose tongue and hand the Muslims are safe.""**"
"181","Faḍālah ibn ʿUbayd رضي الله عنه said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said on the day of the Farewell Pilgrimage: > **""And the Muslim is the one from whose tongue and hand the Muslims are safe.""**"
"182","Ibn ʿUmar رضي الله عنهما reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: > **""Five qualities are of faith; whoever possesses none of them has no faith: submission to the command of Allah, contentment with the decree of Allah, consigning affairs to the command of Allah, reliance upon Allah, and patience at the first stroke of calamity. And no person tastes the reality of Islam until people feel safe from him regarding their blood and their wealth.""** A man asked, ""O Messenger of Allah, which aspect of Islam is best?"" He ﷺ replied: > **""The one from whose tongue and hand the Muslims are safe. Its signs are like guideposts along the road: testifying that there is no deity worthy of worship except Allah, establishing prayer, paying zakāh, judging by the Book of Allah, obeying the Unlettered Prophet, and greeting the children of Adam whenever you meet them.""**"
"183","ʿAmmār رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Three things are from faith: spending despite scarcity, extending greetings of peace to all people, and observing fairness against one's own self.""**"
"184","ʿAmmār ibn Yāsir رضي الله عنه said: ""Whoever combines three traits has combined the characteristics of faith."" One of his companions asked him, ""O Abū al-Yaqẓān, what are these traits about which you stated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Whoever combines them has combined faith'?"" ʿAmmār replied, ""I heard him ﷺ say: > **""Spending despite scarcity, observing fairness against one's own self, and extending greetings of peace to all people.""**"
"185","Anas رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""There are three qualities; whoever possesses them has merited the reward and perfected faith: noble character by which he lives among people, piety that restrains him from the prohibitions of Allah, and forbearance that turns him away from the foolishness of the ignorant.""**"
"186","Anas ibn Mālik رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""The faith of a servant will not be upright until his heart is upright, and his heart will not be upright until his tongue is upright, and he will not enter Paradise until his neighbor is safe from his evil conduct.""**"
"187","ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""He who cannot be trusted has no faith, and he who does not keep his covenant has no religion. By the One in Whose Hand is the soul of Muḥammad, the religion of a servant will not be upright until his tongue is upright, and his tongue will not be upright until his heart is upright, and he will not enter Paradise whose neighbor is not safe from his evil conduct.""** It was asked, ""What is his evil conduct (*al-bawāʾiq*), O Messenger of Allah?"" He ﷺ replied: > **""His deceit and his injustice. And whichever man acquires wealth through unlawful means and spends from it, no blessing is placed in it for him; if he gives it in charity, it is not accepted; and whatever remains of it is his provision toward the Fire. Verily, evil does not expiate evil, but good expiates evil.""**"
"188","ʿAlqamah reported that ʿUbaydullāh said: > **""Patience is half of faith, and certainty is the whole of faith.""**"
"189","Al-Ḥārith ibn Mālik al-Anṣārī رضي الله عنه reported that he passed by the Prophet ﷺ, who asked him, ""How are you this morning, O Ḥārithah?"" He replied, ""I have entered the morning as a true believer."" The Prophet ﷺ said, ""Consider well what you say, for every statement has a reality. What is the reality of your faith?"" He said, ""My soul has detached itself from the worldly life, so I stay awake through my night in worship and keep thirsty through my day in fasting. It is as though I am gazing at the Throne of my Lord openly, as though I am looking at the people of Paradise visiting one another therein, and as though I am looking at the people of the Fire clamoring and howling therein."" The Prophet ﷺ said: > **""O Ḥārithah, you have attained true knowledge, so remain steadfast upon it.""**"
"190","Anas رضي الله عنه reported that the Prophet ﷺ met a man named Ḥārithah in one of the alleyways of Medina and said, ""How are you this morning, O Ḥārithah?"" He replied, ""I have entered the morning as a true believer."" The Prophet ﷺ said, ""Indeed, for every faith there is a reality; so what is the reality of your faith?"" He said, ""My soul has turned away from the worldly life, so I keep my day thirsty and my night awake. It is as though I see the Throne of my Lord visibly, as though I see the people of Paradise rejoicing in their bliss therein, and as though I see the people of the Fire being tormented in the Fire."" The Prophet ﷺ said: > **""You have spoken rightly, so hold firmly to it—a believer whose heart Allah has illuminated.""**"
"191","Abū al-Dardāʾ رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""A servant does not attain the reality of faith until he knows that whatever has befallen him could never have missed him, and whatever has missed him could never have befallen him.""**"
"192","ʿAmr ibn al-Ḥamiq رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""A servant does not genuinely realize the reality of faith until he becomes angry for the sake of Allah and is pleased for the sake of Allah. When he does that, he becomes deserving of the reality of faith. And indeed, My beloved ones and My close allies are those who are remembered when I am remembered, and I am remembered when they are remembered.""**"
"193","ʿUmayr ibn Qatādah reported: A man asked, ""O Messenger of Allah, which prayer is best?"" He ﷺ replied, ""The one with prolonged standing (*ṭūl al-qunūt*)."" He asked, ""Which charity is best?"" He ﷺ replied, ""The effort of one of little means."" He asked, ""Which of the believers is most complete in faith?"" The Prophet ﷺ said: > **""Those of them who are best in character.""**"
"194","Jābir رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""The most complete of the believers in faith are those best in character.""**"
"195","Anas رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Indeed, the most complete of people in faith are those best in character; and indeed, good character reaches the rank of fasting and prayer.""**"
"196","Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""The most complete of the believers in faith are those best in character, who are accommodating and gentle, who show affection and are shown affection; and there is no good in one who neither shows affection nor is shown affection.""**"
"197","Anas ibn Mālik رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Three qualities are of the ethics of faith: one whose anger does not lead him into falsehood, whose pleasure does not lead him away from the truth, and who, when capable, does not take what is not rightfully his.""**"
"198","Jābir رضي الله عنه said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about faith, and he said: > **""Patience and generosity.""**"
"199","ʿAmr ibn ʿAbasah رضي الله عنه said: A man asked, ""O Messenger of Allah, what is Islam?"" He ﷺ replied, ""That your heart surrenders to Allah, and that the Muslims are safe from your tongue and hand."" The man asked, ""Then which Islam is best?"" He ﷺ said, ""Faith."" The man asked, ""And what is faith?"" He ﷺ said, ""That you believe in Allah, His angels, His Books, His Messengers, and the resurrection after death."" The man asked, ""Then which faith is best?"" He ﷺ said, ""Migration (*hijrah*)."" The man asked, ""What is migration?"" He ﷺ said, ""That you abandon evil."" The man asked, ""Then which migration is best?"" He ﷺ said, ""Jihād."" The man asked, ""And what is Jihād?"" He ﷺ said, ""That you fight the disbelievers when you encounter them."" The man asked, ""Then which Jihād is best?"" The Prophet ﷺ said: > **""The one whose horse is slain and whose blood is shed.""**"
"200","ʿAbdullāh ibn Salām رضي الله عنه said: While we were journeying with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he heard the people asking, ""Which deeds are best, O Messenger of Allah?"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, ""Faith in Allah, striving in the cause of Allah, and an accepted pilgrimage (*ḥajj mabrūr*)."" Then he heard a caller in the valley proclaiming: ""I testify that there is no deity worthy of worship except Allah, and that Muḥammad is the Messenger of Allah."" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""And I testify, and I testify that no one bears witness to it except that he is free from polytheism (*shirk*).""**"
"201","ʿUbādah ibn al-Ṣāmit رضي الله عنه reported: A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and asked, ""O Prophet of Allah, which deed is best?"" He ﷺ replied, ""Faith in Allah, affirming Him as true, striving in His cause, and an accepted pilgrimage."" The man said, ""I desire something easier than that, O Messenger of Allah."" He ﷺ said, ""Generosity and patience."" The man said, ""I desire something easier than that, O Messenger of Allah."" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Do not accuse Allah, Blessed and Exalted, concerning anything He has decreed for you.""**"
"202","ʿAmr ibn al-ʿĀṣ رضي الله عنه said: A man asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, ""Which deed is best?"" He ﷺ replied, ""Faith in Allah and affirming Him as true, striving in His cause, and an accepted pilgrimage."" The man said, ""You have given me many things, O Messenger of Allah."" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, ""Then gentle speech, providing food, leniency, and noble character."" The man said, ""I desire just a single word."" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: > **""Go, and do not accuse Allah, Mighty and Majestic, concerning yourself.""**"
"203","Ibn ʿAbbās رضي الله عنهما said: It was said to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, ""Which religion is most beloved to Allah?"" He ﷺ said: > **""The upright, tolerant monotheism (*al-Ḥanīfiyyah al-Samḥah*).""**"
"204","ʿUbādah ibn al-Ṣāmit رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Indeed, the most virtuous faith is to know that Allah is with you wherever you may be.""**"
"205","Abū Hurayrah رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Indeed, the religion most beloved to Allah is the upright, tolerant monotheism (*al-Ḥanīfiyyah al-Samḥah*).""**"
"206","ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz reported from his father, who believed he mentioned his grandfather, that: The Prophet ﷺ was asked, ""Which Islam is best?"" He ﷺ said: > **""The upright, tolerant monotheism (*al-Ḥanīfiyyah al-Samḥah*).""**"
"207","Ibn ʿUmar رضي الله عنهما reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""The noblest faith is that people feel secure from you; the noblest Islam is that people are safe from your tongue and your hand; the noblest migration is that you abandon evil deeds; and the noblest Jihād is that you are slain and your horse is felled.""**"
"208","Anas رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""The best of your religion is that which is easiest.""**"
"209","Abū Mūsā al-Ashʿarī رضي الله عنه reported from the Prophet ﷺ that: He was asked, ""Which Islam is best?"" He ﷺ said, ""The one from whose tongue and hand people are safe."" It was asked, ""Then which Jihād is best?"" He ﷺ said, ""The one whose horse is slain and whose blood is shed."" It was asked, ""Then which prayer is best?"" The Prophet ﷺ said: > **""Prolonged standing in devotion (*ṭūl al-qunūt*).""**"
"210","ʿAmr ibn ʿAbasah رضي الله عنه said: I came to the Prophet ﷺ and asked, ""O Messenger of Allah, who followed you in this matter?"" He ﷺ replied, ""A free man and a slave."" I asked, ""O Messenger of Allah, what is Islam?"" He ﷺ said, ""Pleasant speech and feeding others."" I asked, ""O Messenger of Allah, what is faith?"" He ﷺ said, ""Patience and tolerance."" I asked, ""Which Islam is best?"" He ﷺ said, ""The one from whose tongue and hand Muslims are safe."" I asked, ""Which faith is best?"" He ﷺ said, ""Good character."" I asked, ""Which prayer is best?"" He ﷺ said, ""Prolonged standing in devotion (*ṭūl al-qunūt*)."" I asked, ""Which migration is best?"" He ﷺ said, ""That you abandon evil."" I asked, ""Which Jihād is best?"" The Prophet ﷺ said: > **""The one whose horse is slain and whose blood is shed.""**"
"211","Muʿādh ibn Anas رضي الله عنه reported that he asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about the most virtuous faith. He ﷺ said: > **""That you love for the sake of Allah, hate for His sake, and keep your tongue employed in the remembrance of Allah.""** He asked, ""And what else, O Messenger of Allah?"" The Prophet ﷺ said: > **""And that you love for people what you love for yourself, and dislike for them what you dislike for yourself, and that you speak good or remain silent.""**"
"212","Sahl ibn Saʿd al-Sāʿidī رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""The intention of the believer is better than his deed, and the deed of the hypocrite is better than his intention; and each person acts according to his intention. Thus, when a believer performs a deed, a radiant light shines forth in his heart.""**"
"213","Anas رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Make things easy and do not make them difficult; bring tranquility and do not drive people away.""**"
"214","An unnamed Bedouin who heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: > **""The best of your religion is that which is easiest.""**"
"215","ʿUrwah al-Fuqaymī رضي الله عنه said: We were waiting for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when a man came out whose head was dripping with water from ablution or ritual bath. He led the prayer, and when he finished the prayer, the people began asking him, ""O Messenger of Allah, is there any blame upon us if we do such-and-such?"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said three times: > **""O people, indeed the religion of Allah is founded on ease.""**"
"216","Anas رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Indeed, this religion is firm and profound, so penetrate into it with gentleness.""**"
"217","Jābir رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Indeed, this religion is firm, so penetrate into it with gentleness. For verily, the traveler who exhausts his mount neither covers the terrain nor preserves his mount.""**"
"218","Buraydah al-Aslamī رضي الله عنه said: I went out one day on an errand, and behold, the Prophet ﷺ was walking ahead of me. He took my hand and we walked together. We came across a man praying who was excessively performing bowing and prostration. The Prophet ﷺ said, ""Do you think he is showing off?"" I said, ""Allah and His Messenger know best."" He let go of my hand, clasped his two hands together, lowering and raising them, and said: > **""Hold fast to a moderate course! Hold fast to a moderate course! Hold fast to a moderate course! For whoever tries to make this religion rigid and harsh, it will certainly overpower him.""**"
"219","Abū Dharr رضي الله عنه reported from the Prophet ﷺ: > **""Islam is submissive and yielding; it is not mounted except by one who is compliant.""**"
"220","Sahl ibn Ḥunayf رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Do not impose severe restrictions upon yourselves, for those who came before you perished only because of the harsh burdens they imposed upon themselves; and you will find their remnants in hermitages and monasteries.""**"
"221","Samurah ibn Jundub رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Beware of extremism! For many among the Children of Israel fell into exaggeration, to the point that a short woman would make two wooden pattens, pad them, and insert her feet into them, then stand beside a tall woman and walk with her so that she appeared equal to her or taller than her.""**"
"222","ʿAbdullāh ibn Busr رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Adhere to the correct course and receive glad tidings, for Allah the Exalted is not hasty to punish you. And soon there will come a people who possess no valid argument.""**"
"223","ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr رضي الله عنهما said: A man came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, ""O Messenger of Allah, I recite the Qurʾān but I do not find my heart grasping it."" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Verily, your heart is filled with faith, and indeed, faith is granted to a servant before the Qurʾān.""**"
"224","Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Hearts are of four types: an unblemished heart in which shines a blazing lamp; an encased heart bound tightly within its sheath; an inverted heart; and a divided heart.** > > **As for the unblemished heart, it is the heart of the believer wherein lies his lamp and radiance. As for the encased heart, it is the heart of the disbeliever. As for the inverted heart, it is the heart of the hypocrite who recognized the truth and then denied it. And as for the divided heart, it is a heart containing both faith and hypocrisy: the likeness of faith within it is like an herb nourished by pure water, while the likeness of hypocrisy within it is like an ulcer fed by pus and blood; whichever of the two nourishments prevails over the other will dominate it.""**"
"225","Abū Umāmah al-Bāhilī رضي الله عنه said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ took me by the hand and said: > **""O Abū Umāmah, indeed among the believers are those whose hearts soften with love and reverence for me.""**"
"226","Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""The believers in this world are in three categories: those who believe in Allah and His Messenger, then harbour no doubt, and strive with their wealth and their lives in the cause of Allah; the one from whom people feel secure regarding their wealth and their lives; and the one who, whenever an object of greed presents itself to him, renounces it for the sake of Allah, Mighty and Majestic.""**"
"227","Ibn ʿUmar رضي الله عنهما reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""We know of nothing that is better than a hundred of its own kind, except for the believing man.""**"
"228","ʿĀʾishah رضي الله عنها said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would never approve or allow it to be said: > **""That anyone possesses the level of faith of Jibrīl and Mīkāʾīl, peace be upon them both.""**"
"229","Ibn ʿAbbās رضي الله عنهما reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""When the night in which I was taken on the journey occurred and I awoke in Mecca, the gravity of what occurred weighed heavily upon me, and I knew that the people would accuse me of lying, so I sat apart in grief.""** The enemy of Allah, Abū Jahl, passed by him, came over, and sat beside him, saying mockingly, ""Has anything happened?"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ replied, ""Yes."" He asked, ""What is it?"" He ﷺ said, ""I was taken on a journey by night."" He asked, ""To where?"" He ﷺ said, ""To Bayt al-Maqdis."" He asked, ""And then by morning you were back among us?"" He ﷺ said, ""Yes."" Abū Jahl did not show him that he disbelieved him, fearing that he might retract the statement if he called his people to him. He said, ""What do you think, if I call your people, will you tell them what you have told me?"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, ""Yes."" Abū Jahl cried out, ""O congregation of Banū Kaʿb ibn Luʾayy, come here!"" The assemblies gathered and came until they sat around both of them. He said, ""Tell your people what you told me."" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""I was taken on a journey by night.""** They asked, ""To where?"" He ﷺ said: > **""To Bayt al-Maqdis.""** They said, ""And then by morning you were back among us?"" He ﷺ said, ""Yes."" Thereupon, some began clapping in disbelief, while others placed their hands upon their heads in astonishment at what they deemed a lie. They asked, ""Can you describe the Sanctuary to us?"" For among the people were those who had traveled to that land and seen the Mosque. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""I began describing it, and I continued describing it until some details became indistinct to me. Then the Sanctuary was brought before me while I was looking at it, until it was placed near the house of ʿUqayl—or ʿIqāl—so I described it while looking directly at it.""** The narrator said: Along with this were specific details of the description that I did not memorize. The people said, ""As for the description, by Allah, he has described it precisely!"""
"230","Ibn ʿAbbās رضي الله عنهما reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""On the night I was taken on the journey, I came upon a delightful, fragrant aroma, so I said, 'O Jibrīl, what is this wonderful fragrance?' He said, 'This is the fragrance of the hairdresser of Pharaoh's daughter and her children.'** > > **I asked, 'What is her story?' He said, 'While she was combing the hair of Pharaoh's daughter one day, the comb fell from her hand, and she said: In the name of Allah! Pharaoh's daughter said to her: My father? She replied: No, rather my Lord and the Lord of your father is Allah. The daughter said: Shall I inform him of this? She replied: Yes. So she informed him, and Pharaoh summoned her and said: O so-and-so, do you have a lord other than me? She said: Yes, my Lord and your Lord is Allah.** > > **Pharaoh commanded that a copper vat be heated until it was boiling hot, and ordered that she and her children be thrown into it. She said to him: I have a request of you. He asked: What is your request? She said: I wish that you gather my bones and the bones of my children in a single cloth and bury us together. He said: That is an obligation upon us.** > > **He ordered that her children be thrown into it before her eyes, one by one, until they reached a suckling infant of hers. She seemed to hesitate because of him, but the infant said: O mother, plunge forward, for the punishment of this world is lighter than the punishment of the Hereafter! So she plunged forward.'""** Ibn ʿAbbās added: Four individuals spoke while in their infancy: ʿĪsā ibn Maryam عليه السلام, the companion of Jurayj, the witness of Yūsuf, and the infant son of the hairdresser of Pharaoh's daughter."
"231","Ubayy ibn Kaʿb رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""The roof of my house was opened while I was in Mecca, and Jibrīl ﷺ descended and opened my chest, then washed it with the water of Zamzam. He then brought a golden basin filled with wisdom and faith, emptied it into my chest, and closed it up.** > > **He then took me by the hand and ascended with me to the lowest heaven. When he reached the lowest heaven, he asked for the gate to be opened. It was asked, 'Who is this?' He replied, 'Jibrīl.' It was asked, 'Is anyone with you?' He replied, 'Yes, Muḥammad is with me.' It was asked, 'Has he been sent for?' He replied, 'Yes, open.'** > > **When we ascended above the lowest heaven, behold, there was a man with vast multitudes of souls to his right and vast multitudes of souls to his left. Whenever he looked toward his right, he smiled, and whenever he looked toward his left, he wept. He said, 'Welcome to the righteous Prophet and the righteous son!' I asked Jibrīl, 'Who is this?' He replied, 'This is Adam, and these multitudes to his right and left are the souls of his offspring; those on the right are the dwellers of Paradise, and the multitudes to his left are the dwellers of the Fire. When he looks toward his right he laughs with joy, and when he looks toward his left he weeps with grief.'** > > **Then Jibrīl ascended with me until he reached the second heaven, and said to its gatekeeper, 'Open.' The gatekeeper said to him the same as the gatekeeper of the lowest heaven had said, and opened for him.""**"
"232","Abū Hurayrah رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""On the night I was taken on the journey, when we reached the seventh heaven, I looked above me and saw thunder, lightning, and thunderbolts. Then I came upon people whose bellies were like houses, filled with snakes that could be seen from outside their bellies. I said: 'Who are these, O Jibrīl?' He said: 'These are the consumers of usury (*ribā*).'** > > **When I descended to the lowest heaven, I looked beneath me and saw wind, clamorous voices, and smoke. I said: 'What is this, O Jibrīl?' He replied: 'These are the devils who hover over the eyes of the children of Adam so that they do not reflect upon the wondrous dominion of the heavens and the earth; were it not for that, they would have seen marvels.'""**"
"233","Abū Hurayrah رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""On the night I was taken on the journey, I saw that I placed my feet where the feet of the Prophets were placed in Bayt al-Maqdis. Then ʿĪsā ibn Maryam ﷺ was shown to me, and the person who resembles him most among people is ʿUrwah ibn Masʿūd. And Mūsā ﷺ was shown to me, and he was a man of athletic build, as though he were from the men of Shanūʾah. And Ibrāhīm ﷺ was shown to me, and the person who resembles him most among people is your companion (meaning the Prophet ﷺ himself).""**"
"234","Ibn ʿAbbās رضي الله عنهما said: The Prophet ﷺ was taken on a night journey to Bayt al-Maqdis, and returned that very night. He told them of his journey, the landmarks of Bayt al-Maqdis, and of their trade caravans. Some people said, ""We believe whatever Muḥammad says,"" but others apostatized into disbelief, and Allah caused their necks to be struck alongside Abū Jahl. Abū Jahl had mockingly said, ""Muḥammad frightens us with the tree of Zaqqūm! Bring dates and butter, and swallow it down!"" The Prophet ﷺ saw the Dajjāl with his own eyes in his true appearance—not in a dream—and he saw ʿĪsā ibn Maryam and Ibrāhīm. The Prophet ﷺ was asked about the Dajjāl, and he said: > **""I saw him as a heavily-built man, fair-skinned and pale, with one prominent eye that appeared like a shining star, and his hair was like the tangled branches of a tree. And I saw ʿĪsā as a youthful, fair man with wavy hair, sharp vision, and a slender, firm build. And I saw Mūsā as dark-skinned, of deep brown complexion, with abundant hair and a powerful physique. And I saw Ibrāhīm, and whenever I looked at any limb of his limbs, it was as if I were looking at your companion. Jibrīl عليه السلام said to me: 'Greet your forefather with peace,' so I greeted him with peace.""**"
"235","Abū Hurayrah رضي الله عنه reported: A steed was brought to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ whose stride reached as far as its eye could see. He set out, and Jibrīl ﷺ traveled alongside him. He came upon a people who were sowing crops in a single day and harvesting them on that same day; whenever they harvested, the crops returned as they had been. He said, ""O Jibrīl, who are these?"" Jibrīl replied, ""These are the warriors in the cause of Allah; their good deeds are multiplied seven-hundredfold, and whatever they spend, He replaces it."" Then he came upon a people whose heads were being crushed with boulders; whenever they were crushed, they returned to their former state without any reprieve. He asked, ""O Jibrīl, who are these?"" Jibrīl replied, ""These are the ones whose heads grew too heavy to perform the prescribed prayers."" Then he came upon a people who had patches of cloth on their fronts and backs, wandering like livestock to graze upon thorny shrubs (*ḍarīʿ*), the bitter Zaqqūm tree, and the burning stones of Hell. He asked, ""What are these, O Jibrīl?"" Jibrīl said, ""These are the ones who did not pay the prescribed alms on their wealth; Allah did not wrong them, and Allah is never unjust to His servants."" Then he came upon a people who had before them cooked, succulent meat in a cauldron, and raw, putrid meat alongside it, yet they were eating the foul, raw meat and leaving the wholesome cooked meat. He asked, ""O Jibrīl, who are these?"" Jibrīl said, ""This is a man from your nation who leaves his lawful wife and goes to an immoral woman, spending the night with her until morning; and a woman who leaves her lawful husband and goes to an immoral man, spending the night with him until morning."" Then he came upon a man who had gathered a massive bundle of wood which he was unable to lift, yet he sought to add more onto it. He asked, ""O Jibrīl, who is this?"" Jibrīl said, ""This is a man from your nation who bears people's trusts which he cannot fulfill, yet he keeps taking on more."" Then he came upon a people whose lips and tongues were being clipped with shears of iron; whenever they were cut, they returned as they were without any reprieve. He asked, ""O Jibrīl, who are these?"" Jibrīl said, ""These are the preachers of discord (*khuṭabāʾ al-fitnah*)."" Then he came upon a tiny hole from which a huge bull emerged; the bull then tried to re-enter where it had come out from, but could not. He asked, ""What is this, O Jibrīl?"" Jibrīl said, ""This is the man who speaks a grave, destructive word and regrets it, desiring to take it back, but he cannot."" Then he came upon a valley from which emanated a delightful fragrance and the scent of musk, accompanied by a voice. He asked, ""What is this?"" Jibrīl said, ""This is the voice of Paradise saying: 'O my Lord, bring me my inhabitants and that which You promised me, for my plantings, my silk, my fine brocade, my heavy silk, my rich carpets, my corals, my pearls, my gold, my goblets, my bowls, my pitchers, my fruits, my honey, my garments, my milk, and my pure wine have multiplied; fulfill for me what You promised me!' Allah said: 'Yours is every Muslim man and Muslim woman, every believing man and believing woman; whoever believes in Me and My Messengers, acts righteously, associates nothing with Me, and sets up no rivals beside Me is safe. Whoever asks of Me, I shall grant him; whoever lends to Me, I shall reward him; and whoever relies upon Me, I shall suffice him. Truly, I am Allah, there is no deity worthy of worship except Me; I never break My promise. Indeed, the believers have attained success; blessed is Allah, the Best of Creators.' Paradise said: 'I am well-pleased!'"" Then he came upon a valley and heard a horrifying, hideous sound. He asked, ""O Jibrīl, what is this sound?"" Jibrīl said, ""This is the voice of Hell saying: 'O my Lord, bring me my inhabitants and that which You promised me, for my chains, my shackles, my blazing fire, my boiling water, my murky discharge, and my foul pus have multiplied; my pit is deep and my heat is intense; bring me what You promised me!' Allah said: 'Yours is every polytheist man and polytheist woman, every foul man and foul woman, and every haughty tyrant who disbelieved in the Day of Reckoning.' Hell said: 'I am well-pleased!'"" He continued until he reached Bayt al-Maqdis, where he dismounted, tethered his mount to a rock, and prayed alongside the angels. When the prayer concluded, the angels asked, ""O Jibrīl, who is this with you?"" He said, ""This is Muḥammad, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, the Seal of the Prophets."" They asked, ""Has he been sent for?"" He said, ""Yes."" They said, ""May Allah greet him as a brother and vicegerent; what an excellent brother, what an excellent vicegerent, and what an excellent arrival!"" Then he met the souls of the Prophets, who all praised their Lord, the Exalted. Ibrāhīm ﷺ praised his Lord, saying: ""Praise be to Allah Who took me as an intimate friend, granted me a magnificent dominion, made me a submissive leader, chose me for His messages, delivered me from the fire, and made it cool and peaceful for me."" Then Mūsā عليه السلام praised his Lord, saying: ""Praise be to Allah Who spoke directly to me, chose me, revealed the Torah to me, brought about Pharaoh's destruction at my hands, and granted deliverance to the Children of Israel through me."" Then Dāwūd ﷺ praised his Lord, saying: ""Praise be to Allah Who granted me a kingdom, revealed the Psalms to me, softened iron for me, subjugated the mountains and birds to glorify Him along with me, and granted me wisdom and decisive speech."" Then Sulaymān عليه السلام praised his Lord, saying: ""Praise be to Allah Who subjugated the winds, the jinn, and mankind for me, and subjugated the devils who fashioned whatever I wished—sanctuaries, statues, basins like reservoirs, and immovable cooking cauldrons; Who taught me the speech of birds, made a spring of molten copper flow for me, and granted me a kingdom not granted to anyone after me."" Then ʿĪsā ﷺ praised his Lord, saying: ""Praise be to Allah Who taught me the Torah and the Gospel, made me cure the blind and the leper, and raise the dead by His leave; Who raised me up, purified me from those who disbelieve, and protected me and my mother from the accursed Satan so that Satan had no way over us."" Then Muḥammad ﷺ praised his Lord, saying: ""Each of you has praised his Lord, and I praise my Lord: Praise be to Allah Who sent me as a mercy to the worlds and to all mankind as a bearer of glad tidings and a warner; Who revealed upon me the Criterion (*al-Furqān*) containing a clear exposition of all things; Who made my nation the best nation brought forth for mankind; Who made my nation a justly balanced nation, making them the first and the last; Who expanded my chest for me, removed my burden, exalted my fame, and made me the opener and the seal."" Ibrāhīm ﷺ said: ""By this has Muḥammad ﷺ surpassed you all!"" Then three covered vessels were brought to him. A vessel containing water was offered to him, and it was said, ""Drink."" Then another vessel containing milk was offered to him, and he drank until his thirst was quenched. Then another vessel containing wine was offered to him, and he said, ""I have quenched my thirst; I will not taste it."" It was said to him, ""You have chosen rightly; indeed, it will soon be forbidden to your nation, and had you drunk it, only a few of your nation would have followed you."" Then he was ascended to the heavens. Jibrīl sought entry at the lowest heaven, and it was asked, ""Who is this?"" He said, ""Jibrīl."" It was asked, ""Who is with you?"" He said, ""Muḥammad ﷺ."" They asked, ""Has he been sent for?"" He said, ""Yes."" They said, ""May Allah greet him as a brother and vicegerent; what an excellent brother, what an excellent vicegerent, and what an excellent arrival!"" He entered, and behold, there was an elder of complete, perfect stature, lacking nothing in his creation as human creation lacks. To his right was a gate from which a delightful scent emanated, and to his left was a gate from which a foul odor emanated. When he looked to the gate on his right, he smiled, and when he looked to the gate on his left, he wept in sorrow. The Prophet ﷺ asked, ""O Jibrīl, who is this elder, and what are these two gates?"" Jibrīl said, ""This is your forefather Adam; the gate on his right is the gate of Paradise: when he sees those of his offspring who enter it, he smiles and rejoices; and when he looks to the gate on his left, the gate of Hell: when he sees those of his offspring who enter it, he weeps and grieves."" Then he ascended to the second heaven and Jibrīl sought entry. The gatekeeper asked, ""Who is this?"" He said, ""Jibrīl."" They asked, ""Who is with you?"" He said, ""Muḥammad, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."" They asked, ""Has he been sent for?"" He said, ""Yes."" They said, ""May Allah greet him as a brother and vicegerent; what an excellent brother, what an excellent vicegerent, and what an excellent arrival!"" He entered, and behold, there were two young men. He asked, ""O Jibrīl, who are these two youths?"" Jibrīl said, ""These are ʿĪsā and Yaḥyā, maternal cousins."" Then he ascended to the third heaven and Jibrīl sought entry. They asked, ""Who is with you?"" He said, ""Muḥammad."" They asked, ""Has he been sent for?"" He said, ""Yes."" They welcomed him, and he entered. Behold, there sat a man endowed with beauty surpassing all people, just as the full moon surpasses all other stars. He asked, ""Who is this, O Jibrīl?"" Jibrīl said, ""This is your brother Yūsuf ﷺ."" Then he ascended to the fourth heaven and Jibrīl sought entry. He entered, and behold, there sat a man. The Prophet ﷺ asked, ""O Jibrīl, who is this man sitting here?"" Jibrīl said, ""This is your brother Idrīs, whom Allah raised to a high station."" Then he ascended to the fifth heaven and Jibrīl sought entry. He entered, and behold, there sat an elder narrating to the people. He asked, ""O Jibrīl, who is this, and who are these surrounding him?"" Jibrīl said, ""This is Hārūn ﷺ, appointed over his people, and these around him are his people from the Children of Israel."" Then he ascended to the sixth heaven and Jibrīl sought entry. He entered, and behold, there sat a man. As the Prophet ﷺ passed beyond him, the man wept. He asked, ""O Jibrīl, who is this?"" Jibrīl said, ""Mūsā ﷺ."" The Prophet ﷺ asked, ""What makes him weep?"" Jibrīl said, ""The Children of Israel claim that I was the most favored of creation, yet this one has succeeded me; were he alone it would be one thing, but with him is his entire nation!"" Then Jibrīl ascended with us to the seventh heaven and sought entry. He entered, and behold, there sat a gray-haired elder upon a throne near the gate of Paradise. Beside him sat a group of people whose complexions had some blemish. These people rose and entered a river called *Niʿmatullāh* (The Grace of Allah) and washed therein; they emerged with their complexions noticeably cleansed. Then they entered another river called *Raḥmatullāh* (The Mercy of Allah) and washed therein; they emerged with their complexions further cleansed. Then they entered yet another river—fulfilling Allah's word: {And their Lord will give them a pure drink}—and emerged with their complexions completely radiant and pure like those of their companions, and they sat beside them. The Prophet ﷺ asked, ""O Jibrīl, who is this gray-haired elder sitting here? And who are these white-faced people? And who are those whose complexions had a blemish, who entered these rivers and bathed, and then emerged with their complexions purified?"" Jibrīl said, ""This is your forefather Ibrāhīm ﷺ, the first person whose hair grayed on earth. As for those white-faced people, they are a people who did not obscure their faith with wrongdoing. And as for those whose complexions had a blemish, they mixed a righteous deed with another that was evil; they repented, and Allah accepted their repentance."" Then he proceeded to the Lote Tree (*al-Sidrah*). It was said to him, ""This is the Lote Tree of the Utmost Boundary (*Sidrat al-Muntahā*); at it terminates the soul of every one of your nation who passes upon your path. From its base flow rivers of water incorruptible, rivers of milk whose taste never changes, rivers of wine delicious to those who drink, and rivers of clarified honey. It is a tree in whose shade a rider could travel for seventy years, and a single leaf of it provides shade for creation."" A divine light enveloped it and angels enveloped it—which is the meaning of: {When there covered the Lote Tree that which covered it}. Allah, Blessed and Exalted, said to him: ""Ask!"" The Prophet ﷺ said: ""You took Ibrāhīm as an intimate friend and granted him a magnificent dominion; You spoke directly to Mūsā; You granted Dāwūd a magnificent dominion, softened iron for him, and subjugated the mountains for him; You granted Sulaymān a magnificent dominion, subjugating for him jinn, men, devils, and winds, and granting him a kingdom not fitting for anyone after him; You taught ʿĪsā the Torah and the Gospel, caused him to heal the blind and leper, and protected him and his mother from the accursed Satan so that Satan had no way over them."" His Lord, Blessed and Exalted, said to him: > **""I have taken you as an intimate friend—and it is written in the Torah: 'Muḥammad is the Beloved of the Most Merciful'—and I have sent you to all mankind entirely. I have made your nation the first and the last; I have ordained that no sermon is valid for them until they bear witness that you are My servant and My Messenger; I have made you the first of the Prophets in creation and the last of them in being sent; I have granted you the Seven Oft-Repeated verses (*al-Sabʿ al-Mathānī*), which I never gave to any Prophet before you; I have granted you the concluding verses of Sūrat al-Baqarah from a treasure beneath the Throne, which I never gave to any Prophet before you; and I have made you an opener and a seal.""** The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""My Lord, Blessed and Exalted, favored me with six honors: He cast dread into the hearts of my enemies from a distance of a month's journey; spoils of war were made lawful for me, whereas they were never made lawful for anyone before me; the earth was made for me a place of prayer and a means of purification; I was granted the openings of concise, comprehensive speech (*jawāmiʿ al-kalim*); my nation was displayed before me, such that neither the follower nor the followed was hidden from me—and I saw them coming upon a people wearing footwear made of hair, and I saw them coming upon a people with broad faces and small eyes, and I recognized who they were; and I was commanded with fifty prayers.""** The Prophet ﷺ returned to Mūsā, who asked him, ""How many prayers were you commanded with?"" He replied, ""Fifty prayers."" Mūsā said, ""Return to your Lord and ask Him for a reduction, for your nation is the weakest of nations, and I have tested the Children of Israel with great severity."" So Muḥammad ﷺ returned and asked Allah for a reduction, and He reduced them by ten. He returned to Mūsā, who said, ""How many were you commanded with?"" He said, ""Forty prayers."" Mūsā said, ""Return to your Lord and ask Him for a reduction for your nation, for your nation is the weakest of nations, and I have experienced severity from the Children of Israel."" Muḥammad ﷺ returned and asked Him for a reduction, and He reduced them by ten. He returned to Mūsā, who asked, ""How many were you commanded with?"" He said, ""Thirty."" Mūsā said, ""Return to your Lord and ask Him for a reduction for your nation, for your nation is the weakest of nations, and I experienced severity from the Children of Israel."" Muḥammad ﷺ returned and asked his Lord for a reduction, and He reduced them by ten. He returned to Mūsā, who asked, ""How many were you commanded with?"" He said, ""Twenty."" Mūsā said, ""Return to your Lord and ask Him for a reduction for your nation, for your nation is the weakest of nations, and I experienced severity from the Children of Israel."" Muḥammad ﷺ returned and asked his Lord for a reduction, and He reduced them by ten. He returned to Mūsā, who asked, ""How many were you commanded with?"" He said, ""Ten."" Mūsā said, ""Return to your Lord and ask Him for a reduction for your nation, for your nation is the weakest of nations, and I experienced severity from the Children of Israel."" Muḥammad ﷺ returned and asked his Lord for a reduction, and He reduced them by five. He returned to Mūsā, who asked, ""How many were you commanded with?"" He said, ""Five."" Mūsā said, ""Return to your Lord and ask Him for a reduction, for your nation is the weakest of nations, and I experienced severity from the Children of Israel."" The Prophet ﷺ said: > **""I have returned to my Lord until I feel ashamed before Him, and I will not return to Him again.""** Thereupon, it was said to him: > **""Just as you have resigned yourself to five, they shall suffice for you as fifty; every good deed will be rewarded tenfold for you.""** The Prophet ﷺ said: > **""Mūsā ﷺ was the strictest of them upon me at first, and the best of them for me in the end.""**"
"236","Shaddād ibn Aws رضي الله عنه said: We asked, ""O Messenger of Allah, how was the night journey in which you were taken?"" He ﷺ said: > **""I prayed the night prayer with my companions in Mecca in late evening. Then Jibrīl came to me with a white beast, larger than a donkey and smaller than a mule. It proved difficult for me, so Jibrīl turned it by its ear until he mounted me upon it. It dashed forward with us, placing its hoof at the furthest point its eye could see, until we reached a land filled with date palms.** > > **Jibrīl said: 'Dismount,' so I dismounted. He said: 'Pray,' so I prayed. Then we mounted again. He said to me: 'Do you know where you prayed?' I said: 'Allah knows best.' He said: 'You prayed in Yathrib; you prayed in Ṭaybah.'** > > **Then it dashed forward, placing its hoof at the furthest point its eye could see, until we reached a white land. He said to me: 'Dismount,' so I dismounted. Then he said: 'Pray,' so I prayed. Then we mounted. He said: 'Do you know where you prayed?' I said: 'Allah and His Messenger know best.' He said: 'You prayed in Madyan; you prayed by the tree of Mūsā.'** > > **Then it dashed forward with us, placing its hoof at the furthest point its eye could see, until we ascended. He said: 'Dismount,' so I dismounted. He said: 'Pray,' so I prayed. Then we mounted. He said: 'Do you know where you prayed?' I said: 'Allah knows best.' He said: 'You prayed in Bethlehem, where ʿĪsā the Messiah, son of Maryam, was born.'** > > **Then he proceeded with me until we entered the city from its eighth gate. He came to the Qiblah side of the Mosque and tethered his mount, and we entered the Mosque through a gate wherein the sun and moon are depicted. I prayed in the Mosque wherever Allah willed.** > > **Then two vessels were brought to me; in one was milk and in the other was honey. Both were presented to me, and I looked between the two, then Allah guided me and I took the milk. I drank until milk moistened my forehead. Before me was an elder reclining, who said: 'Your companion has chosen the primordial nature (*al-fiṭrah*)'—or he said: 'taken to the fiṭrah.'** > > **Then he traveled with me until I came to the valley in the city, and behold, Hell was exposed like spread carpets.""** We said, ""O Messenger of Allah, how did you find it?"" He ﷺ said, ""Like...""—and he mentioned something that escaped my memory. He ﷺ continued: > **""Then I passed by a trade caravan of Quraysh at such-and-such place who had lost a camel of theirs, so I greeted them with peace, and some of them said to each other: 'This is the voice of Muḥammad ﷺ!'** > > **Then I returned to my companions in Mecca before morning. Abū Bakr came to me and said, 'O Messenger of Allah, where were you tonight? I looked for you in your place and did not find you.' I said: 'I traveled to Bayt al-Maqdis tonight.' He said: 'O Messenger of Allah, it is a journey of a month! Describe it for me.'** > > **So an aperture was opened for me as though I were looking directly at it; they did not ask me about a single thing except that I informed them of it.** > > **Abū Bakr said: 'I bear witness that you are indeed the Messenger of Allah!'** > > **The polytheists said: 'Look at the son of Abū Kabshah claiming that he traveled to Bayt al-Maqdis tonight!' The Prophet ﷺ said: 'Yes, and I passed by a caravan of yours at such-and-such place; they had lost a camel of theirs at such-and-such place, and I am describing their journey for you: they will encamp at such-and-such place, and then arrive before you on such-and-such day, led by a brownish-grey camel wearing a black woolen cloth and two black saddlebags.'** > > **When that day arrived, the people went out watching eagerly until, close to midday, the caravan appeared, led by that exact camel just as the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had described.""**"
"237","ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""The Burāq was brought to me and I mounted it. Whenever it climbed an ascent, its hind legs elongated, and whenever it descended, its front legs elongated. It traveled with us through a murky, foul-smelling land, and then we came out into a vast, fragrant land.** > > **I asked, 'O Jibrīl, we were traveling in a murky, putrid land, then we emerged into a vast, sweet land?' He replied, 'That was the land of the Fire, and this is the land of Paradise.'** > > **Then I came upon a man standing, who asked, 'Who is this with you, O Jibrīl?' He said, 'Your brother Muḥammad ﷺ.' He welcomed me and prayed for blessings upon me. I asked, 'Who is this, O Jibrīl?' He said, 'This is your brother ʿĪsā ibn Maryam ﷺ.'** > > **We traveled on, and I heard a voice, then we came upon a man who asked, 'Who is this with you?' Jibrīl said, 'This is your brother Muḥammad ﷺ.' He greeted me with peace, prayed for blessings upon me, and said, 'Ask for ease for your nation.' I asked, 'Who is this, O Jibrīl?' He said, 'This is your brother Mūsā ﷺ.' I asked, 'Toward whom was his vehement tone directed?' He said, 'Toward his Lord.' I said, 'Toward his Lord?' He said, 'Yes, He knows his fiery nature.'** > > **Then we traveled on and I saw something. I asked, 'What is this, O Jibrīl?' He said, 'This is the tree of your forefather Ibrāhīm; draw near to it.' We drew near to it, and he welcomed me and prayed for blessings upon me.** > > **Then we proceeded until we reached Bayt al-Maqdis. I tethered the beast to the ring to which the Prophets tethered their mounts, then we entered the Mosque, and the Prophets were gathered for me—both those Allah named and those He did not name—and I led them in prayer.""**"
"238","Anas ibn Mālik رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""While I was sitting, Jibrīl ﷺ came and tapped me between my shoulders. I rose and went to a tree containing what looked like two birds' nests; he sat in one of them and I sat in the other.** > > **It then grew and ascended until it spanned the horizons, while I turned my gaze; and had I wished to touch the heaven, I could have touched it. Jibrīl then looked at me as if he were a worn, flattened mat out of awe of Allah, so I recognized the superiority of his knowledge of Allah over mine.** > > **A gate of the gates of heaven was opened, and I beheld the Greatest Light, and behold, beneath the veil were shimmering drapes of pearls and rubies; then Allah revealed to me whatever He willed to reveal.""**"
"239","Umm Hāniʾ رضي الله عنها said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ spent the night in which he was taken on the journey in my house. I missed him during the night and sleep was kept from me out of fear that some harm had befallen him from Quraysh. When he returned, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Jibrīl عليه السلام came to me, took me by the hand, and led me out. Outside the house was a beast smaller than a mule and larger than a donkey. He mounted me upon it and journeyed until we reached Bayt al-Maqdis.** > > **He showed me Ibrāhīm, whose appearance resembles mine and whose character resembles mine. He showed me Mūsā, a tall man of brownish complexion with straight hair, resembling the men of Azd Shanūʾah. He showed me ʿĪsā ibn Maryam, of medium height, fair-skinned with a reddish tint, whom I found resembling ʿUrwah ibn Masʿūd al-Thaqafī. And he showed me the Dajjāl, blind in his right eye, whom I found resembling Qaṭan ibn ʿAbd al-ʿUzzā. Now I intend to go out to Quraysh and inform them of what I have seen.""** I took hold of his garment and said, ""I adjure you by Allah! You are going to a people who will call you a liar and reject your word, and I fear that they will assault you."" He freed his garment from my hand and went out to them while they were sitting in their assembly, and informed them of what he had told me. Jubayr ibn Muṭʿim stood up and said, ""O Muḥammad, had you still been the young man you were, you would not have spoken what you just said while you are living among us!"" A man among them asked, ""O Muḥammad, did you pass by camels belonging to us at such-and-such place?"" He ﷺ said: > **""Yes, by Allah, I found them; they had lost a camel of theirs and were searching for it.""** The man asked, ""Did you pass by the camels of Banū so-and-so?"" He ﷺ said: > **""Yes, I found them at such-and-such place; a red she-camel of theirs had broken its leg, and I found them with a bowl of water, so I drank what was in it.""** They said, ""Tell us their exact number and the herdsmen among them."" He said: > **""I was occupied with other matters than counting them.""** Then he stood, and the caravan was brought before his vision, so he counted them and knew their herdsmen. He then returned to Quraysh and said to them: > **""You asked me about the camels of Banū so-and-so: they are such-and-such number, and their herdsmen are so-and-so and so-and-so. And you asked me about the camels of Banū so-and-so: they are such-and-such number, and their herdsmen are Ibn Abī Quḥāfah and so-and-so and so-and-so; and they will arrive before you tomorrow morning at the mountain pass.""** The people sat waiting at the pass to see if he had spoken the truth. When the camels appeared, they asked them, ""Did you lose a camel?"" They replied, ""Yes."" They asked the others, ""Did a red she-camel of yours break its leg?"" They replied, ""Yes."" They asked, ""Did you have a bowl of water?"" Abū Bakr said, ""By Allah, I myself placed it, and no one drank from it, nor was it spilled upon the ground!"" Abū Bakr believed in him and affirmed his truthfulness, and on that day he was named *al-Ṣiddīq* (the Affirmer of Truth)."
"240","Abū Umāmah al-Bāhilī رضي الله عنه said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out to us after the morning prayer and said: > **""Indeed, I saw a vision that is absolute truth, so comprehend it well:** > > **A man came to me, took me by the hand, and had me follow him until he brought me to a lofty, rugged mountain. He said to me: 'Climb it.' I said: 'I am unable to.' He said: 'I shall make it easy for you.' So whenever I lifted my foot, I placed it upon a step, until we stood level upon the summit of the mountain.** > > **We proceeded, and behold, we came upon men and women whose cheeks were torn open. I asked: 'Who are these?' He said: 'These are the ones who speak of things they do not know.'** > > **Then we proceeded, and behold, we came upon men and women whose eyes and ears were pierced and sealed. I asked: 'Who are these?' He said: 'These are the ones who claim to show their eyes what they never saw, and make their ears hear what they never heard.'** > > **Then we proceeded, and behold, we came upon women suspended by their Achilles tendons, their heads hanging downward, with serpents tearing at their breasts. I asked: 'Who are these?' He said: 'These are the women who withheld their milk from their children.'** > > **Then we proceeded, and behold, we came upon men and women suspended by their Achilles tendons, their heads hanging downward, licking small traces of muddy, foul water. I asked: 'Who are these?' He said: 'These are the ones who fast and then break their fast before the lawful time of their fast.'** > > **Then we proceeded, and behold, we came upon men and women of the most hideous appearance, the foulest clothing, and the most putrid stench, as though their odor were that of latrines. I asked: 'Who are these?' He said: 'These are the male and female fornicators.'** > > **Then we proceeded, and behold, we came upon corpses that were severely bloated and intensely foul-smelling. I asked: 'Who are these?' He said: 'These are the deceased of the disbelievers.'** > > **Then we proceeded, and behold, we saw smoke and heard howling. I asked: 'What is this?' He said: 'This is Hell, so leave it.'** > > **Then we proceeded, and behold, we came upon men sleeping peacefully beneath the shade of trees. I asked: 'Who are these?' He said: 'These are the deceased of the Muslims.'** > > **Then we proceeded, and behold, we came upon young girls and boys playing between two rivers. I asked: 'Who are these?' He said: 'These are the deceased offspring of the believers.'** > > **Then we proceeded, and behold, we came upon men possessing the most handsome faces, the finest clothing, and the sweetest fragrance, as though their faces were sheets of pure parchment. I asked: 'Who are these?' He said: 'These are the truthful (*al-Ṣiddīqūn*), the martyrs (*al-Shuhadāʾ*), and the righteous (*al-Ṣāliḥūn*).'** > > **Then we proceeded, and behold, we came upon three persons drinking wine and chanting. I asked: 'Who are these?' He said: 'That is Zayd ibn Ḥārithah, Jaʿfar, and Ibn Rawāḥah.' I inclined toward them, and they said: 'We are prepared for you, we are prepared for you!'** > > **Then I raised my head, and behold, there were three persons beneath the Throne. I asked: 'Who are these?' He said: 'That is your forefather Ibrāhīm, Mūsā, and ʿĪsā, and they are awaiting you'—may the peace and blessings of Allah be upon them all.""**"
"241","ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Laylā reported: Jibrīl brought the Burāq to the Prophet ﷺ and carried him before him. Whenever it reached a low place, its front legs lengthened and its hind legs shortened so that he remained level; and whenever it reached an incline, its front legs shortened and its hind legs lengthened until it leveled out. Then a man appeared on the right of the path and called out twice, ""O Muḥammad, come to the path!"" Jibrīl said to him, ""Proceed and do not speak."" Then a man appeared on the left of the path and called out, ""To the path, O Muḥammad!"" Jibrīl said to him, ""Proceed and do not speak to anyone."" Then an exquisite, beautiful woman appeared before him. Jibrīl said, ""Do you know who that man was on the right of the path?"" The Prophet ﷺ said, ""No."" Jibrīl said, ""That was Judaism calling you to their religion."" Then he asked, ""Do you know who called you on the left of the path?"" He said, ""No."" Jibrīl said, ""That was Christianity calling you to their religion. Do you know who that beautiful woman was?"" He said, ""That was the worldly life (*al-Dunyā*) calling you to itself."" Then they proceeded until they arrived at Bayt al-Maqdis. Behold, there sat a gathering who said, ""Welcome to the Unlettered Prophet!"" Among them sat an elder. Muḥammad ﷺ asked, ""Who is this?"" Jibrīl said, ""This is your forefather Ibrāhīm."" Then he asked, ""Who is this?"" Jibrīl said, ""This is Mūsā."" Then he asked, ""Who is this?"" Jibrīl said, ""This is ʿĪsā ibn Maryam."" The prayer was established and they stepped back, bringing Muḥammad ﷺ forward to lead. Drinks were brought, and Muḥammad ﷺ chose milk. Jibrīl said to him, ""You have chosen the primordial nature (*al-fiṭrah*)."" Then it was said to him, ""Stand before your Lord."" He entered, and when he returned, he was asked, ""What happened?"" He said, ""Fifty prayers were enjoined upon my nation."" Mūsā said to him, ""Return to your Lord and ask Him for a reduction for your nation, for your nation cannot bear this."" He returned and came back. Mūsā asked, ""What happened?"" He said, ""He reduced them to twenty-five."" Mūsā said, ""Return to your Lord and ask Him for a reduction."" He returned and came back until He reduced them to five. Mūsā said, ""Return to your Lord and ask Him for a reduction."" The Prophet ﷺ said: > **""I feel ashamed before my Lord from repeatedly returning to Him, especially since He has said to me: 'For every return you made, you have an answered petition that I shall grant you.'""**"
"242","Ṣuhayb ibn Sinān رضي الله عنه said: When water, then wine, and then milk were presented to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he took the milk. Jibrīl said to him: > **""You have attained the primordial nature (*al-fiṭrah*) by which every creature is nourished. Had you taken the wine, you would have gone astray and your nation would have gone astray, and you would have been of the dwellers of this""—and he pointed toward the valley known as the Valley of Hell; I looked toward it and behold, it was blazing with fire.**"
"243","ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Qurṭ رضي الله عنه reported: On the night the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was taken on the journey to al-Masjid al-Aqṣā, when he returned he was between the Maqām of Ibrāhīm and Zamzam, with Jibrīl on his right and Mīkāʾīl on his left. They flew with him until he reached the seven heavens. When he returned, he ﷺ said: > **""I heard glorification in the highest heavens amidst many hymns of praise: 'The highest heavens glorify the Possessor of Awe, in fearful reverence of the Possessor of Sublimity by virtue of His supreme transcendence; glorified and exalted is He!'""**"
"244","Ibn ʿAbbās رضي الله عنهما said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: > **""When I was taken on the night journey, I reached the Lote Tree of the Utmost Boundary (*Sidrat al-Muntahā*), and behold, its lote-fruits were like large water jars (*al-qilāl*).""**"
"245","ʿAbdullāh ibn Asʿad ibn Zurārah رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""On the night I was taken on the journey, I reached a palace of pearl glistening with light, and I was granted three honors: 'Indeed, you are the Master of the Messengers, the Leader of the God-fearing, the Messenger of the Lord of the worlds, and the Leader of those with radiant faces, hands, and feet from ablution.'""**"
"246","Jābir رضي الله عنه reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: > **""On the night I was taken on the journey, I passed by the Exalted Assembly (*al-Malaʾ al-Aʿlā*), and Jibrīl was like a worn, flattened mat out of the fear and awe of Allah.""**"
"247","Ibn ʿAbbās رضي الله عنهما reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""I saw my Lord, Mighty and Majestic.""**"
"248","ʿIkrimah said regarding the verse: *{And We made not the vision which We showed you except as a test for people}* [al-Isrāʾ: 60]: > **""It was something shown to the Prophet ﷺ in a wakeful state, which he saw with his own eyes when he was taken to Bayt al-Maqdis.""**"
"249","Ibn ʿAbbās رضي الله عنهما used to say: > **""Indeed, Muḥammad ﷺ saw his Lord twice: once with his physical eyes, and once with his heart.""**"
"250","Ibn ʿAbbās رضي الله عنهما said: ""Muḥammad ﷺ gazed upon his Lord, Blessed and Exalted."" ʿIkrimah said: I asked Ibn ʿAbbās, ""Did Muḥammad gaze upon his Lord?"" He replied: > **""Yes. Allah granted direct speech to Mūsā, intimate friendship (*al-khullah*) to Ibrāhīm, and the direct vision to Muḥammad ﷺ.""**"
"251","Anas ibn Mālik رضي الله عنه reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: > **""I asked Gabriel: 'Do you see your Lord?' He replied: 'Indeed, between Him and me are seventy veils of light; were I to see the nearest of them, I would be incinerated.'""**"
"252","ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr and Sahl ibn Saʿd رضي الله عنهما reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Before Allah are seventy thousand veils of light and darkness; no soul hears anything of the murmur of those veils without its soul departing.""**"
"253","Abū Hurayrah رضي الله عنه narrated: A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and asked, ""O Muḥammad, has Allah, Mighty and Majestic is He, veiled Himself from His creation with anything other than the heavens and the earth?"" The Prophet ﷺ said: > **""Yes, between Him and the angels who are around the Throne are seventy veils of light, seventy veils of fire, seventy veils of darkness, seventy veils of brocade hangings (istabraq), seventy veils of fine silk hangings (sundus), seventy veils of white pearls, seventy veils of red pearls, seventy veils of yellow pearls, seventy veils of green pearls, seventy veils of luminescence illuminated by the radiance of fire and light, seventy veils of snow, seventy veils of water, seventy veils of clouds, seventy veils of hail, and seventy veils of Allah's indescribable Majesty.""** The man said, ""Then inform me of the angel closest to Him."" The Prophet ﷺ said: > **""Have I spoken the truth in what I informed you, O Jewish man?""** The man replied, ""Yes."" The Prophet ﷺ said: > **""The angel closest to Him is Isrāfīl, then Gabriel, then Michael, then the Angel of Death—may Allah bless them all.""**"
"254","ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbbās رضي الله عنهما said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: > **""Indeed, Allah has an angel who, if it were said to him, 'Swallow the seven heavens and the seven earths in a single morsel,' he would do so. His glorification is: 'Glory be to You wherever You are.'""**"
"255","Anas ibn Mālik رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""I have been permitted to speak about one of the angels carrying the Throne: his two feet are in the lowest earth, the Throne rests upon his horn, and between his earlobe and his shoulder is the distance flown by a bird in seven hundred years. That angel says: 'Glory be to You wherever You are.'""**"
"256","Jābir رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""I have been permitted to speak about an angel from among the angels of Allah who bear the Throne: between his earlobe and his shoulder is the journey of seventy years.""**"
"257","Abū Hurayrah رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""I have been permitted to speak about an angel whose feet have penetrated the seventh earth, while the Throne rests upon his shoulders, and he says: 'Glory be to You wherever You were and wherever You are.'""**"
"258","Abū Hurayrah رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""An angel came to me who had never descended to the earth before, bearing a message from my Lord; he placed one foot above the lowest heaven and his other foot in the earth, barely contained by it.""**"
"259","Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Indeed, in the heaven there is an angel called Ismāʿīl, commanding seventy thousand angels, each of whom commands seventy thousand angels.""**"
"260","ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar رضي الله عنهما reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Contemplate the blessings and bounties of Allah, and do not contemplate the essence of Allah.""**"
"261","Abū Hurayrah رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""The Hour will not be established until Allah is openly disbelieved in, and that will occur when people dispute speculatively concerning their Lord.""**"
"262","ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr رضي الله عنهما reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""There is nothing more noble and honored in the sight of Allah, Mighty and Majestic is He, than the believer.""**"
"263","ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr رضي الله عنهما reported: The Prophet ﷺ looked at the Kaʿbah and said: > **""Allah has indeed ennobled you, honored you, and magnified you, yet the sanctity of the believer is greater than yours.""**"
"264","Jābir رضي الله عنه said: When the Prophet ﷺ conquered Makkah, he turned to face it and said: > **""You are sacred; how magnificent is your sanctity and how delightful is your fragrance! Yet greater in sanctity with Allah than you is the believer.""**"
"265","ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr رضي الله عنهما reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: > **""The angels said: 'O our Lord, You gave the Children of Adam the world where they eat, drink, and clothe themselves, while we glorify You with Your praise, neither eating nor engaging in amusement; so just as You made the world for them, grant us the Hereafter.' He said: 'I will not make the righteous offspring of the one I created with My Hand like those to whom I said: ""Be,"" and they were.'""**"
"266","ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr رضي الله عنهما reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""There is nothing more noble in the sight of Allah, Exalted is His mention, on the Day of Resurrection than the Children of Adam.""** It was said, ""O Messenger of Allah, not even the angels?"" The Prophet ﷺ said: > **""Not even the angels; indeed, the angels are compelled to obedience, in the manner of the sun and the moon.""**"
"267","Abū Hurayrah رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Allah says: 'My believing servant is more beloved to Me than some of My angels.'""**"
"268","ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr رضي الله عنهما reported that the Prophet ﷺ used to say: > **""Indeed, Allah, Blessed and Exalted is He, is more reluctant concerning the death of His believing servant than any one of you is with his most prized possession, until He takes his soul upon his bed.""**"
"269","Kaʿb ibn Mālik رضي الله عنه reported: The Prophet ﷺ was asked, ""Which of the people is most excellent?"" He ﷺ said: > **""A believer between two noble parents.""**"
"270","Kaʿb ibn Mālik رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""The believer is unsuspecting and noble, while the wicked transgressor is deceitful and vile.""**"
"271","ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar رضي الله عنهما reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""The likeness of the believer is that of a perfume seller: if you sit with him he benefits you, if you walk with him he benefits you, and if you partner with him he benefits you.""**"
"272","ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar رضي الله عنهما reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""The likeness of the believer is that of a date palm: whatever comes to you from it benefits you.""**"
"273","Abū Hurayrah رضي الله عنه said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ upon the minbar speaking about Moses عليه السلام, saying: > **""It crossed his mind: 'Does Allah sleep?' So Allah sent an angel to him who kept him awake for three nights. Then he gave him two glass bottles, one in each hand, and commanded him to safeguard them. He began to doze off, and his two hands almost collided, so he would awaken and hold one away from the other, until he dozed off heavily, his hands struck together, and both bottles shattered.""** The Prophet ﷺ said: > **""Allah struck a parable for him that if Allah were to sleep, the heavens and the earth would not hold together.""**"
"274","ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb رضي الله عنه reported: A woman came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, ""Supplicate to Allah that He admits me to Paradise."" The Prophet ﷺ magnified the Lord, Blessed and Exalted is He, and said: > **""Indeed, His Kursī encompasses the heavens and the earth, and indeed it groans like the groaning of a new camel saddle when mounted due to the heaviness.""**"
"275","ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr ibn al-ʿĀṣ رضي الله عنهما said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: > **""The Compeller will take His heavens and His earth in His Hand—and the Prophet clenched his hand, opening and closing it—then He will say: 'I am the Compeller! I am the King! Where are the tyrants? Where are the arrogant?'""** ʿAbdullāh said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ swayed to his right and to his left until I looked at the minbar shaking from its very base, to the point that I wondered: ""Will it collapse with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?"""
"276","ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar رضي الله عنهما reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Allah will roll up the heavens and take them in His Right Hand, and He will roll up the earth and take it in His other Hand, then He will say: 'I am the Sovereign! Where are the kings?'""**"
"277","Nuʿaym ibn Hammār رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""The Scale is in the Hand of the Most Merciful; He raises some peoples and lowers others.""**"
"278","ʿĀʾishah رضي الله عنها said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: > **""Indeed, Allah laughs at the despair and hopelessness of His servants, while His mercy is so near to them.""** I said, ""May my father and mother be sacrificed for you, O Messenger of Allah! Does our Lord laugh?"" He ﷺ said: > **""Yes, by the One in Whose Hand is my soul, He indeed laughs!""** I said, ""Then He will never deprive us of good when He laughs."""
"279","Muʿāwiyah ibn Abī Sufyān رضي الله عنه said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: > **""Indeed, Allah the Exalted cannot be overcome, nor can He be deceived, nor can He be informed of anything He does not already know.""**"
"280","ʿUqbah ibn ʿĀmir رضي الله عنه said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: > **""Our Lord is All-Hearing, All-Seeing.""** And he pointed with his hand toward his eyes."
"281","Abū Razīn رضي الله عنه said: I said, ""O Messenger of Allah, how does Allah bring the dead back to life?"" The Prophet ﷺ said: > **""Have you not passed by the valley of your people when it was barren and drought-stricken, then passed by it when it was lush and green, then passed by it when it was barren, and then passed by it when it was lush and green?""** I said, ""Yes, indeed."" He ﷺ said: > **""In such a manner does Allah bring the dead back to life.""**"
"282","ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd رضي الله عنه said: > **""Indeed, with your Lord the Exalted there is neither night nor day; the light of the heavens and the earth is from the light of His Face. The measure of a day of your days with Him is twelve hours. Your deeds of yesterday are presented before Him at the start of today; He examines them for three hours, and when He sees what He dislikes, it angers Him. The first to realize His anger are the bearers of the Throne, as they find it becoming heavy upon them. Then the bearers of the Throne, the canopies of the Throne, the proximate angels, and all other angels fall down in prostration. Gabriel then blows into the Horn such that everything hears his voice, and they glorify the Most Merciful, Mighty and Majestic is He, for three hours until the Most Merciful is filled with mercy—that makes six hours. Then the wombs are brought and He examines them for three hours; that is His saying in His Book: 'It is He who forms you in the wombs however He wills' (3:6), and 'He grants to whom He wills females and He grants to whom He wills males, or He makes them both males and females, and He renders whom He wills barren; indeed, He is Knowing and Competent' (42:49-50)—that makes nine hours. Then the provisions are brought and He examines them for three hours; that is His saying: 'Allah extends provision for whom He wills and restricts it' (13:26), and 'Every day He is bringing about a matter' (55:29). This is from your affairs and the affairs of your Lord, Mighty and Majestic is He.""**"
"283","Abū Hurayrah رضي الله عنه said: While we were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, a cloud passed by, so he asked: > **""Do you know what this is?""** We said, ""Allah and His Messenger know best."" He ﷺ said: > **""This is the ʿanān (clouds); these are the water-bearers of the earth that Allah drives to those among His servants who neither thank Him nor supplicate to Him. Do you know what is above you?""** We said, ""Allah and His Messenger know best."" He ﷺ said: > **""The raqīʿ (firmament): a held-back wave and a protected ceiling. Do you know how much distance is between you and it?""** We said, ""Allah and His Messenger know best."" He ﷺ said: > **""A journey of five hundred years. Do you know what is above that?""** We said, ""Allah and His Messenger know best."" He ﷺ said: > **""Another heaven. Do you know how much distance is between you and it?""** We said, ""Allah and His Messenger know best."" He ﷺ said: > **""A journey of five hundred years""**—until he counted seven heavens. Then he asked: > **""Do you know what is above that?""** We said, ""Allah and His Messenger know best."" He ﷺ said: > **""The Throne. Do you know how much distance is between it and the seventh heaven?""** We said, ""Allah and His Messenger know best."" He ﷺ said: > **""A journey of five hundred years.""** Then he asked: > **""Do you know what is beneath you?""** We said, ""Allah and His Messenger know best."" He ﷺ said: > **""An earth. Do you know what is beneath it?""** We said, ""Allah knows best."" He ﷺ said: > **""Another earth. Do you know how much distance is between the two?""** We said, ""Allah and His Messenger know best."" He ﷺ said: > **""A journey of seven hundred years""**—until he counted seven earths. Then he ﷺ said: > **""By Allah, if you were to lower a rope, it would descend,""** and then he recited: > **""'He is the First and the Last, the Ascendant and the Intimate, and He is Knowing of all things' (57:3).""**"
"284","ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd رضي الله عنه said: > **""Between the lowest heaven and the one that follows it is the journey of five hundred years, and between every two heavens is five hundred years. Between the seventh heaven and the Kursī is the journey of five hundred years, and between the Kursī and the water is five hundred years. The Throne is upon the water, and Allah, Exalted is His mention, is above the Throne, knowing that which you are upon.""**"
"285","Abū Mūsā al-Ashʿarī رضي الله عنه said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: > **""Whoever performs a good deed and is pleased by it, or commits an evil deed and is grieved by it, then he is a believer.""**"
"286","Abū Umāmah رضي الله عنه reported: A man asked, ""O Messenger of Allah, what is faith?"" The Prophet ﷺ said: > **""If your good deed brings you joy and your evil deed brings you grief, then you are a believer.""**"
"287","Abū Umāmah رضي الله عنه narrated: A man asked, ""What is sin, O Messenger of Allah?"" He ﷺ said: > **""Whatever wavers in your chest, leave it.""** The man asked, ""Then what is faith?"" He ﷺ said: > **""Whoever is grieved by his bad deed and pleased by his good deed, he is a believer.""**"
"288","ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Whoever is grieved by his evil deed is a believer.""**"
"289","Abū Umāmah رضي الله عنه reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: > **""Allah, Mighty and Majestic is He, says: 'The most beloved thing with which My servant worships Me is sincere devotion (nuṣḥ) to Me.'""**"
"290","ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbbās رضي الله عنهما reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""The religion is sincerity.""** They asked, ""To whom?"" He ﷺ said: > **""To Allah, to His Messenger, and to the leaders of the believers.""**"
"291","Abū Hurayrah رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Gabriel عليه السلام commanded me to maintain sincerity.""**"
"292","ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar رضي الله عنهما reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: > **""The religion is sincerity.""**"
"293","Thawbān رضي الله عنه reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: > **""The pinnacle of religion is sincerity.""** They asked, ""To whom, O Messenger of Allah?"" He ﷺ said: > **""To Allah, Mighty and Majestic is He, to His religion, to the leaders of the Muslims, and to the generality of the Muslims.""**"
"294","Ḥudhayfah ibn al-Yamān رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Whoever does not concern himself with the affairs of the Muslims is not of them, and whoever does not begin and end his day being sincere to Allah, to His Messenger, to His Book, to his leader, and to the generality of the Muslims, is not of them.""**"
"295","Jarīr ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Bajalī رضي الله عنه said: I pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and then turned to leave, but he called me back and said: > **""I will not accept it from you until you pledge allegiance to show sincerity to every Muslim.""** So I pledged allegiance to him upon that."
"296","ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Laylā reported from his father رضي الله عنه that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""No servant truly believes until I am more beloved to him than his own self, my family is more beloved to him than his own family, my lineage is more beloved to him than his own lineage, and my person is more beloved to him than his own person.""**"
"297","Anas ibn Mālik رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""A person does not truly believe until I am more beloved to him than his child, his parent, and all mankind.""**"
"298","ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar رضي الله عنه said: Al-ʿAbbās ibn ʿAbd al-Muṭṭalib came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, ""O Messenger of Allah, I approached some people who were conversing, but when they saw me, they fell silent; and that was only because they found my presence burdensome."" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Have they done so? By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, none of them truly believes until he loves you for the sake of my love! Do you hope to enter Paradise through my intercession while the Banū ʿAbd al-Muṭṭalib do not hope for it?""**"
"299","Al-Miqdād ibn al-Aswad رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Whoever loves Allah and His Messenger truthfully without falsehood, meets the believers and loves them, and regards the state of pre-Islamic ignorance as being cast into the Fire, has tasted the flavor of faith""**—or he said: **""has reached the pinnacle of faith.""**"
"300","Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Indeed, Allah, Mighty and Majestic is He, has three sacred sanctities: whoever safeguards them, Allah will safeguard for him his religion and his worldly affairs; and whoever does not safeguard them, Allah will not safeguard anything for him: the sanctity of Islam, my sanctity, and the sanctity of my kinship.""**"
"301","Abū Umāmah رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Whoever possesses three qualities will taste the sweetness of faith: that Allah and His Messenger are more beloved to him than anything else, that he loves a person solely for the sake of Allah, and that being cast into the Fire is more beloved to him than returning to disbelief after Allah has rescued him from it.""**"
"302","Anas ibn Mālik رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Love for Quraysh is faith, and hatred for them is disbelief. Love for the Arabs is faith; so whoever loves the Arabs has loved me, and whoever hates the Arabs has hated me.""**"
"303","ʿAmr ibn al-Jamūḥ رضي الله عنه heard the Prophet ﷺ say: > **""A servant does not realize pure, unadulterated faith until he loves for the sake of Allah and hates for the sake of Allah. When he loves for the sake of Allah, Blessed and Exalted is He, and hates for the sake of Allah, he becomes deserving of the alliance of Allah. Indeed, My allies among My servants and My beloved among My creation are those who are remembered when I am remembered, and I am remembered when they are remembered.""**"
"304","ʿAmr ibn al-Ḥamiq رضي الله عنه heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: > **""A servant does not find pure faith until he loves for the sake of Allah and hates for the sake of Allah. When he loves for the sake of Allah and hates for the sake of Allah, he becomes deserving of the divine alliance. Indeed, My allies among My servants and My beloved among My creation are those who are remembered when I am remembered, and I am remembered when they are remembered.""**"
"305","Muʿādh ibn Anas رضي الله عنه reported that he asked the Prophet ﷺ about the most excellent faith. He ﷺ said: > **""That you love for the sake of Allah, hate for the sake of Allah, and employ your tongue in the remembrance of Allah.""** Muʿādh asked, ""And what else, O Messenger of Allah?"" He ﷺ said: > **""And that you love for people what you love for yourself, and dislike for them what you dislike for yourself.""** In another narration, he added: > **""And that you speak good or remain silent.""**"
"306","Al-Barāʾ ibn ʿĀzib رضي الله عنه said: We were sitting with the Prophet ﷺ when he asked: > **""Which handhold of Islam is the firmest?""** They said, ""The prayer."" He ﷺ said: > **""It is good, but it is not that.""** They said, ""Fasting Ramadan."" He ﷺ said: > **""It is good, but it is not that.""** They said, ""Jihād."" He ﷺ said: > **""It is good, but it is not that.""** Then he ﷺ said: > **""Indeed, the firmest handhold of faith is that you love for the sake of Allah and hate for the sake of Allah.""**"
"307","Abū Dharr رضي الله عنه said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out to us and asked: > **""Do you know which deed is most beloved to Allah?""** Someone said, ""The prayer and zakāh."" Another said, ""Jihād."" He ﷺ said: > **""Indeed, the most beloved of deeds to Allah, Mighty and Majestic is He, is loving for the sake of Allah and hating for the sake of Allah.""**"
"308","Abū Hurayrah رضي الله عنه reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: > **""Whoever loves for the sake of Allah...""** And in another narration: > **""Whoever is pleased to taste the sweetness of faith, let him love a person loving him for nothing other than Allah, Mighty and Majestic is He.""**"
"309","ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd رضي الله عنه said: I entered upon the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: > **""O Ibn Masʿūd, which handhold of faith is the firmest?""** I said, ""Allah and His Messenger know best."" He ﷺ said: > **""The firmest handhold of Islam is loyalty and allegiance for the sake of Allah, love for the sake of Allah, and hatred for the sake of Allah.""**"
"310","Abū Umāmah رضي الله عنه reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: > **""Whoever loves for the sake of Allah, hates for the sake of Allah, gives for the sake of Allah, and withholds for the sake of Allah, has perfected faith.""**"
"311","ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd رضي الله عنه said: > **""Indeed, it is part of faith that a man loves his brother, loving him for nothing other than for the sake of Allah.""**"
"312","Mujāhid reported that ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar رضي الله عنهما said to him: > **""Love for the sake of Allah, hate for the sake of Allah, ally for the sake of Allah, and show enmity for the sake of Allah; for indeed, the alliance of Allah cannot be attained except through that. A man will never taste the sweetness of faith—even if his prayers and fasting are abundant—until he is like that; yet the brotherhood of the people has become based upon worldly affairs.""**"
"313","ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar رضي الله عنهما reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Three things are destructive, three things are salvific, three things are expiations, and three things raise ranks. As for the destructive things: obeyed greed, followed whims, and a person's self-admiration. As for the salvific things: justice in anger and pleasure, moderation in poverty and wealth, and fear of Allah in secret and in public. As for the expiations: waiting for the next prayer after prayer, performing ablution thoroughly in severe cold, and walking to congregate prayers. As for what raises ranks: feeding others, spreading peace (salām), and praying at night while the people are asleep.""**"
"314","Anas ibn Mālik رضي الله عنه reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: > **""Three things are expiations, three things raise ranks, three things are salvific, and three things are destructive. As for the expiations: performing ablution thoroughly in severe cold, waiting for prayers after prayers, and walking to Friday prayers. As for what raises ranks: feeding others, spreading peace (salām), and praying at night while the people are asleep. As for the salvific things: justice in anger and pleasure, moderation in poverty and wealth, and fear of Allah in secret and in public. As for the destructive things: obeyed greed, followed whims, and a person's self-admiration.""**"
"315","ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbbās رضي الله عنهما reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""The destructive things are three: a person's self-admiration, obeyed greed, and followed whims.""**"
"316","ʿAbdullāh ibn Abī Awfā رضي الله عنه reported that the Prophet ﷺ said something similar: > **""The destructive things are three: a person's self-admiration, obeyed greed, and followed whims.""**"
"317","Abū Hurayrah رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Modesty (ḥayāʾ) is from faith, and faith leads to Paradise. Vulgarity (badhāʾ) is from harshness, and harshness leads to the Fire.""**"
"318","ʿAbdullāh ibn Salām رضي الله عنه reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: > **""Modesty is part of faith.""**"
"319","Abū Bakrah and ʿImrān ibn Ḥuṣayn رضي الله عنهما reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Modesty is from faith, and faith leads to Paradise. Vulgarity is from harshness, and harshness leads to the Fire.""**"
"320","ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd رضي الله عنه said: Some people brought their companion to the Prophet of Allah ﷺ and said, ""O Prophet of Allah, this companion of ours has been ruined by modesty."" The Prophet of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Indeed, modesty is among the precepts of Islam, while vulgarity is from a person's vileness.""**"
"321","Abū Umāmah رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Indeed, modesty (ḥayāʾ) and reticence in speech (ʿiyy) are from faith, and they draw one near to Paradise and distance one from the Fire. Indecency and vulgarity are from Satan, and they draw one near to the Fire and distance one from Paradise.""** A Bedouin said, ""In rajaz poetry we say that reticence is part of foolishness."" Abū Umāmah said: ""I say to you: 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said,' and you recite to me foul rajaz poetry?"""
"322","Abū Mūsā al-Ashʿarī رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Modesty and faith are tied together; they are never separated except together.""**"
"323","ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbbās رضي الله عنهما reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: > **""Modesty and faith are bound together; when one of them is stripped away, the other follows it.""**"
"324","ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr رضي الله عنهما reported: A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and asked, ""O Messenger of Allah, what is the deed that leads to Paradise?"" He ﷺ said: > **""Truthfulness. For when a servant speaks the truth, he acts righteously; when he acts righteously, he believes; and when he believes, he enters Paradise.""**"
"325","Abū Hurayrah رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""A servant does not attain complete faith until he abandons lying even in jest, and abandons disputing even when he is truthful.""**"
"326","ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""A servant does not attain the pure reality of faith until he abandons jesting and falsehood, and abandons disputing even when he is in the right.""**"
"327","Abū Umāmah رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""A believer may be naturally disposed to every trait, except treachery and lying.""**"
"328","Saʿd ibn Abī Waqqāṣ رضي الله عنه reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: > **""A believer may be naturally disposed to every characteristic, except treachery and lying.""**"
"329","ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar رضي الله عنهما reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""A believer may adopt every character trait, but not treachery and lying.""**"
"330","Abū Hurayrah رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Disbelief and faith can never coexist in the heart of a person, nor can truthfulness and falsehood ever coexist together, nor can treachery and trustworthiness ever coexist together.""**"
"331","ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd رضي الله عنه said: > **""A believer may be molded upon every characteristic except treachery and lying.""**"
"332","Muʿāwiyah ibn Abī Sufyān رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Adhere strictly to truthfulness, for it guides to righteousness, and both of them lead to Paradise. And beware of lying, for it guides to wickedness, and both of them lead to the Fire.""**"
"333","Māzin ibn al-Ghaḍūbah رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Adhere strictly to truthfulness, for it guides to Paradise.""**"
"334","Abū Umāmah رضي الله عنه said: On the Day of the Conquest of Makkah, I was beneath the riding camel of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he spoke fine and beautiful words. Among what he said was: > **""Whoever embraces Islam from among the People of the Book will have his reward twice; he shall have the same rights as we have and bear the same obligations as we bear. And whoever embraces Islam from among the polytheists will have his reward; he shall have the same rights as we have and bear the same obligations as we bear.""**"
"335","Al-Zubayr ibn Bakkār reported: Al-Qāsim was born to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he was the eldest of his children, followed by Zaynab. Zaynab, the daughter of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, was married to Abū al-ʿĀṣ ibn al-Rabīʿ ibn ʿAbd Shams, and she bore him ʿAlī and Umāmah. ʿAlī was being nursed among Banū Ghāḍirah, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ weaned him while his father was still a polytheist at that time. The Prophet ﷺ said: > **""Whoever shares with me in anything, I have more right to it; and whichever disbeliever shares with a Muslim in anything, the Muslim has more right to it than him.""**"
"336","ʿUqbah ibn ʿĀmir al-Juhanī رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Whoever has a person embrace Islam at his hands, Paradise becomes obligatory for him.""**"
"337","Al-Sāʾib ibn Abī al-Sāʾib رضي الله عنه reported that he used to be a business partner of the Prophet ﷺ before Islam. On the Day of the Conquest of Makkah, he came to him, and the Prophet ﷺ said: > **""Welcome to my brother and partner, who neither defrauded nor disputed. O Sāʾib, you used to perform deeds during the pre-Islamic days of ignorance that were not accepted from you, but today they are accepted from you.""** Al-Sāʾib was known for advancing loans generously and upholding family ties."
"338","Ṣaʿṣaʿah ibn Nājiyah al-Mujāshiʿī رضي الله عنه—the grandfather of the poet al-Farazdaq—said: I came to the Prophet ﷺ, and he presented Islam to me, so I embraced Islam, and he taught me verses from the Qurʾān. I said, ""O Messenger of Allah, I performed good deeds during the pre-Islamic days of ignorance; will I have any reward for them?"" He ﷺ asked: > **""And what did you do?""** I said, ""Two of my pregnant she-camels went astray, so I went out searching for them riding my camel. Two tents appeared in an open plain, so I headed toward them. In one of them, I found an elderly man, so I asked, 'Have you noticed two pregnant she-camels?' He asked, 'What is their brand mark?' I replied, 'The brand of Banū Dārim.' He said, 'We found your two she-camels, helped deliver their young, and fostered them. Through them, Allah brought relief to a household among your people of the Arabs from Muḍar.' While he was speaking with me, a woman called out from the other tent, 'She has given birth!' The man asked, 'What has she given birth to? If it is a boy, he will share with us among our people—and in al-Bazzār's narration: he will bring blessing to our people—but if it is a girl, bury her!' The woman said, 'It is a girl.' I asked, 'Who is this infant to be buried alive?' He replied, 'My daughter.' I said, 'I will buy her from you.' He said, 'O brother of Banū Tamīm, do you say: ""Will you sell your daughter?"" when I have told you that I am an Arab of Muḍar?' I said, 'I am not buying her person from you; I am only buying her life, so that you do not kill her.' He asked, 'With what will you buy her?' I said, 'With these two she-camels of mine and their two calves.' He asked, 'And will you add this camel of yours?' I said, 'Yes, provided you send a messenger with me, and when I reach my family, I will return the camel to you.' He agreed. When I reached my family, I returned the camel to him. Later that night, I thought to myself: 'This is a noble deed that no one among the Arabs has preceded me in.' By the time Islam appeared, I had saved three hundred and sixty infant girls from being buried alive, buying each of them with two pregnant she-camels and a camel. Will I have any reward for that?"" The Prophet ﷺ said: > **""You have your reward, for Allah has blessed you with Islam.""**"
"339","Jābir ibn ʿAbdillāh رضي الله عنهما reported that a man asked: ""O Messenger of Allah, will we be taken to account for what we did during the pre-Islamic days of ignorance?"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Whoever excels in good conduct in Islam will not be taken to account for what he did in the days of ignorance; but whoever behaves evilly in Islam will be taken to account for what he did in both the days of ignorance and in Islam.""**"
"340","Anas ibn Mālik رضي الله عنه reported: I was sitting with another man in the company of the Prophet ﷺ, when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""A servant does not truly believe until he loves for his Muslim brother what he loves for himself.""** Anas said: Then that man and I went out to the market, and there was an item being sold. I bargained for it, and the seller said, ""For thirty."" The man examined it and said, ""I will take it for forty."" The seller said, ""What makes you do this when I am offering it to you for less than this?"" Then the man examined it again and said, ""I will take it for fifty."" The seller said, ""What makes you do this when I am offering it to you for less than this?"" The man said, ""I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying: 'A servant does not truly believe until he loves for his brother what he loves for himself,' and in my judgment, this item is worth fifty."""
"341","Anas ibn Mālik رضي الله عنه said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ never addressed us in a sermon except that he said: > **""There is no faith for the one who has no trustworthiness, and there is no religion for the one who upholds no covenant.""**"
"342","Abū Umāmah رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""There is no faith for the one who has no trustworthiness. And by the One in Whose hand is my soul, you shall not enter Paradise until you believe.""**"
"343","ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""There is no faith for the one who has no trustworthiness, and there is no religion for the one who upholds no covenant.""**"
"344","Al-Ḥasan al-Baṣrī reported: A man came to al-Zubayr ibn al-ʿAwwām رضي الله عنه and said, ""Shall I not kill ʿAlī for you?"" Al-Zubayr said, ""No. How could you kill him when he is accompanied by troops?"" The man said, ""I will join his ranks and assassinate him by stealth."" Al-Zubayr said, ""No, for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **'Indeed, faith is a shackle against treacherous assassination; a believer never assassinates by stealth.'""**"
"345","Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyab reported: Muʿāwiyah رضي الله عنه entered upon ʿĀʾishah رضي الله عنها, and she said to him, ""Did you not fear that I might have hidden a man for you to kill you?"" He replied, ""You would never do that while I am in a house of safety, and I have heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying: > **'Faith is a shackle against treacherous assassination.'** How have I been regarding the matters between me and you, and in fulfilling your needs?"" She said, ""Good."" He said, ""Then leave us and them until we meet our Lord, the Mighty and Majestic."""
"346","ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbbās رضي الله عنهما reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""He is not a believer with complete faith who does not consider affliction to be a blessing and ease to be a misfortune.""** They asked, ""How is that, O Messenger of Allah?"" He ﷺ said: > **""Because affliction is followed by nothing except ease, and likewise ease is followed by nothing except affliction and misfortune. And he is not a believer with complete faith who does not find tranquility in his prayer.""** They asked, ""And why is that, O Messenger of Allah?"" He ﷺ said: > **""Because the one who prays is conversing privately with his Lord, whereas when he is not in prayer, he only converses with the children of Adam.""**"
"347","ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""A believer is neither a defamer, nor a curser, nor obscene, nor vulgar.""**"
"348","ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr رضي الله عنهما reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""It is an act of disbelief to disown one's lineage, however subtle it may be, and to claim a lineage that is not known.""**"
"349","Jābir ibn ʿAbdillāh رضي الله عنهما reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: > **""Whoever claims clientage to other than his rightful patrons has cast off the loop of faith from his neck.""**"
"350","Abū Bakr al-Ṣiddīq رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Whoever claims a lineage that is unknown has committed disbelief in Allah; and disowning a lineage—even if distant—is disbelief in Allah.""**"
"351","Ayyūb ibn ʿUdayy ibn ʿUdayy narrated from his father—or his uncle—that: There was an enslaved man named Kaysān who renamed himself Qays, claimed lineage to his master, and moved to Kūfah. His father rode to ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb رضي الله عنه and said, ""O Commander of the Believers, my son was born in my bed, but now he has turned away from me and claimed to be the son of my master and his master."" ʿUmar said to Zayd ibn Thābit رضي الله عنه, ""Do you not know that we used to recite: > **'Do not turn away from your fathers, for indeed it is disbelief on your part'?""** Zayd said, ""Yes."" Thereupon ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb said to the father, ""Go, bind your son to your camel, then proceed, striking your camel with a whip and your son with a whip until you bring him back to your family."""
"352","ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr رضي الله عنهما reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Whoever attributes himself to someone other than his father shall not smell the fragrance of Paradise, even though its fragrance is detected from a distance of seventy years—or a journey of seventy years.""**"
"353","Abū Salamah ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAwf reported: ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar رضي الله عنهما and ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr ibn al-ʿĀṣ رضي الله عنهما met upon Mount al-Marwah and spoke together. Then ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr moved on while ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar remained behind weeping. A man said to him, ""What makes you weep, O Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān?"" He replied, ""This one—meaning ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr—stated that he heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying: > **'Whoever has in his heart even the weight of a seed of arrogance, Allah will cast him down upon his face into the Fire.'""**"
"354","ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr رضي الله عنهما reported: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: > **""No person shall enter Paradise who has in his heart a mustard seed's weight of arrogance.""**"
"355","ʿUqbah ibn ʿĀmir رضي الله عنه reported that he heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: > **""There is no man who dies while having in his heart a mustard seed's weight of arrogance for whom Paradise is lawful, so that he may neither smell its fragrance nor see it.""** A man from Quraysh named Abū Rayḥānah said, ""O Messenger of Allah, I love beauty and desire it, so much so that I love it in the strap of my whip and the thong of my sandal."" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""That is not arrogance. Indeed, Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, is Beautiful and loves beauty. Rather, arrogance is to reject the truth and look down upon people with contempt.""**"
"356","ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar رضي الله عنهما reported: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: > **""Whoever exalts himself or struts haughtily in his walk will meet Allah, Blessed and Exalted, while He is angry with him.""**"
"357","ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbbās رضي الله عنهما reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: > **""He shall not enter Paradise who has in his heart a mustard seed's weight of arrogance, and he shall not enter the Fire who has in his heart a mustard seed's weight of faith.""**"
"358","Al-Sāʾib ibn Yazīd رضي الله عنه reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: > **""He shall not enter Paradise who has in his heart a seed's weight of arrogance.""** The people said, ""O Messenger of Allah, then we are ruined! How are we to know what arrogance is in our hearts, and where it lies?"" The Prophet ﷺ said: > **""Whoever wears wool, milks the sheep, and eats with those whom his right hand possesses has no arrogance in his heart, if Allah wills.""**"
"359","ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Indeed, Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, says: 'Might is My lower garment, and grandeur is My cloak; so whoever contends with Me regarding either of them, I shall punish him.'""**"
"360","Faḍālah ibn ʿUbayd رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""There are three persons about whom you need not ask: a man who contends with Allah regarding His cloak—for His cloak is grandeur and His lower garment is might; a man who is in doubt concerning the decree of Allah; and the one who despairs of His mercy.""**"
"361","ʿAbdullāh ibn Salām رضي الله عنه passed through the market carrying a bundle of firewood upon his back. It was said to him, ""What makes you do this when Allah has made you wealthy enough not to need it?"" He replied, ""I intended to crush pride, for I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: > **'He shall not enter Paradise who has in his heart a mustard seed's weight of arrogance.'""**"
"362","Abū Mūsā al-Ashʿarī رضي الله عنه reported: The Prophet of Allah ﷺ was holding my hand in one of the alleyways of Madīnah when he came upon a beggar woman on the street with dust blowing across her face. Abū Mūsā said to her, ""Move away from the path of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ!"" She retorted, ""The road is wide enough for him; let him pass wherever he wishes."" This was so distressing to Abū Mūsā that he stumbled, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ recognized the distress on his face. He ﷺ said, ""O Abū Mūsā, has what this beggar woman said troubled you?"" I replied, ""Yes, may my father and mother be sacrificed for you, O Messenger of Allah! It was hard upon me when she showed disdain for what I told her regarding the command of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."" He ﷺ said: > **""Do not speak to her, for she is an arrogant tyrant.""** I said, ""May my father and mother be sacrificed for you, what is she that she should be an arrogant tyrant?"" He ﷺ replied: > **""Even if that is not in her power, it resides within her heart.""**"
"363","Anas ibn Mālik رضي الله عنه said: The Prophet ﷺ passed along a street, and a woman passed by. A man said to her, ""Clear the road!"" She said, ""The road is right there!"" The Prophet ﷺ said: > **""Leave her alone, for she is an arrogant tyrant.""**"
"364","Abū al-Ṭufayl رضي الله عنه reported: While the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was on a journey, there was a man ahead of him watching to see if there was anything in the road that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ might dislike so that he could remove it, when suddenly an elderly woman appeared... [and he mentioned the rest of the hadith]."
"365","ʿAbdullāh ibn Abī Awfā رضي الله عنه reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: > **""One does not drink wine while he is a believer at the time of drinking it; one does not commit adultery while he is a believer at the time of committing it; and one does not seize valuable plunder while he is a believer at the time of seizing it.""**"
"366","ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar رضي الله عنهما reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: > **""The fornicator does not commit fornication while he is a believer at the time of committing it; the wine-drinker does not drink wine while he is a believer at the time of drinking it; the thief does not steal while he is a believer at the time of stealing; and one does not seize valuable plunder while he is a believer at the time of seizing it.""**"
"367","ʿĀʾishah رضي الله عنها reported that a man who had been lashed for drinking wine passed by her door. She asked, ""What is this?"" It was said to her, ""A man was caught drunk, so he was lashed."" She said, ""SubḥānAllāh! I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: > **'The drinker does not drink wine when he drinks it while he is a believer; the fornicator does not commit fornication when he commits fornication while he is a believer; the thief does not steal when he steals while he is a believer; and one does not seize valuable plunder that causes people to raise their eyes toward him while he is a believer. So beware, beware!'**"""
"368","ʿAbdullāh ibn Mughaffal رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""The fornicator does not commit fornication while he is a believer at the time of committing it; the thief does not steal while he is a believer at the time of stealing; the wine-drinker does not drink wine while he is a believer at the time of drinking it; and one does not seize plunder while people look on toward him while he is a believer.""**"
"369","Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""The fornicator does not commit fornication while he is a believer at the time of committing it; the thief does not steal while he is a believer at the time of stealing; and the wine-drinker does not drink wine while he is a believer at the time of drinking it.""** We asked, ""O Messenger of Allah, how does that happen?"" He ﷺ replied: > **""Faith departs from him; but if he repents, it returns to him.""**"
"370","A Companion of the Prophet ﷺ reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: > **""Whoever commits fornication, faith departs from him; but if he repents, Allah accepts his repentance.""**"
"371","ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbbās, Abū Hurayrah, and ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar رضي الله عنهم reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: > **""The fornicator does not commit fornication while he is a believer at the time of committing it; the thief does not steal while he is a believer at the time of stealing; the wine-drinker does not drink wine while he is a believer at the time of drinking it; and one does not seize valuable plunder while he is a believer at the time of seizing it.""**"
"372","ʿAlqamah ibn Qays reported: I saw ʿAlī رضي الله عنه upon the pulpit of Kūfah saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: > **""The fornicator does not commit fornication while he is a believer at the time of committing it; the thief does not steal while he is a believer at the time of stealing; one does not seize plunder toward which people raise their eyes while he is a believer; and a man does not drink wine while he is a believer.""** A man stood up and asked, ""O Commander of the Believers, does whoever commits fornication become a disbeliever?"" ʿAlī replied: ""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to command us to leave the traditions of concessions unelaborated. 'The fornicator does not commit fornication while he is a believer' means: believing that such fornication is lawful for him; for if he believes it to be lawful, he has indeed disbelieved. 'The thief does not steal while he is a believer' means: believing that theft to be lawful for him; for if he believes it to be lawful, he has indeed disbelieved. 'He does not drink wine when he drinks it while he is a believer' means: believing it to be lawful for him; for if he drinks it while believing it to be lawful, he has indeed disbelieved. And 'one does not seize valuable plunder while he is a believer' means: believing it to be lawful for him; for if he seizes it while believing it to be lawful, he has indeed disbelieved."""
"373","Abū Hurayrah رضي الله عنه said: I heard my beloved friend Abū al-Qāsim ﷺ say: > **""The thief does not steal while he is a believer, and the fornicator does not commit fornication while he is a believer; faith is far too noble before Allah for that.""**"
"374","Al-Faḍl ibn Yasār reported: I heard Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī being asked about the statement of the Prophet ﷺ: ""The fornicator does not commit fornication while he is a believer, and the thief does not steal while he is a believer."" He drew a wide circle upon the ground, and then drew another circle inside it, and said: > **""The outer circle is Islam, and the inner circle is Faith. When a person commits fornication, he exits from Faith into Islam; and nothing expels him from Islam except polytheism.""**"
"375","Maḥmūd ibn Labīd رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Indeed, that which I fear most for you is the minor polytheism.""** They asked, ""And what is the minor polytheism, O Messenger of Allah?"" He ﷺ said: > **""Ostentation (al-riyāʾ). Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, will say when He recompenses people for their deeds: 'Go to those whom you used to show off before in the world, and see whether you can find any reward with them!'""**"
"376","Anas ibn Mālik رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Nothing effaces Islam as thoroughly as avarice.""**"
"377","ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar رضي الله عنهما reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Indeed, tale-bearing and malice lead to the Fire; they never gather in the heart of a Muslim.""**"
"378","Abū Hurayrah رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Plotting and deception lead to the Fire.""**"
"379","Jābir ibn ʿAbdillāh رضي الله عنهما reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Avoid the major sins.""**"
"380","Abū Hurayrah رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Whoever meets Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, without associating anything with Him, pays the zakāh on his wealth with a willing heart seeking Allah's reward, and listens and obeys, Paradise is his—or he will enter Paradise. And there are five sins for which there is no expiation: associating partners with Allah, taking a life without right, slandering a believer with falsehood, fleeing from the battlefield, and a perjurious oath through which one usurps wealth unjustly.""**"
"381","ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbbās رضي الله عنهما reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: > **""May Allah curse the one who sacrifices to other than Allah; may Allah curse the one who alters the boundary markers of the land; may Allah curse the one who misleads a blind person from the path; may Allah curse the one who reviles his parents; and may Allah curse the one who claims allegiance to other than his rightful patrons.""**"
"382","Abū Hurayrah رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""The major sins: the first of them is associating partners with Allah, taking a life without right, consuming usury, consuming the property of an orphan, fleeing on the day of battle, slandering chaste women, and returning to nomadic Bedouin life after having emigrated.""**"
"383","Abū al-Dardāʾ رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Shall I not inform you of the greatest of major sins? Associating partners with Allah, and disobedience to parents.""** The Prophet ﷺ had been sitting with his legs drawn up and wrapped in his cloak; he loosened his cloak, took hold of the tip of his tongue, and said: > **""Beware, and false speech!""**"
"384","ʿImrān ibn Ḥuṣayn رضي الله عنه reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: > **""What do you say concerning the fornicator, the thief, and the wine-drinker?""** They replied, ""Allah and His Messenger know best."" He ﷺ said: > **""They are shameful obscenities and carry legal penalties. But shall I not inform you of the greatest of major sins?! Associating partners with Allah,""** —then he recited: *{And whoever associates partners with Allah has indeed fabricated a tremendous sin}* [al-Nisāʾ: 48]— > **""and disobedience to parents,""** —then he recited: *{Be grateful to Me and to your parents; unto Me is the final destination}* [Luqmān: 14]. He had been reclining, but he sat upright and said: > **""Beware, and false speech!""** And Ibn ʿAbbās said: ""Everything that Allah has forbidden is a major sin."""
"385","Sahl ibn Abī Ḥathmah reported from his father رضي الله عنه: I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: > **""Avoid the seven major sins.""** The people remained silent and no one spoke. The Prophet ﷺ said: > **""Will you not ask me about them? Associating partners with Allah, taking a life, fleeing from battle, consuming the property of an orphan, consuming usury, slandering a chaste woman, and reverting to Bedouin life after emigration.""**"
"386","ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr رضي الله عنهما reported: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ascended the pulpit and said: > **""I swear by an oath, I swear by an oath!""** Then he descended and said: > **""Receive glad tidings! Receive glad tidings! Whoever performs the five daily prayers and avoids the major sins may enter through whichever gate of Paradise he pleases.""** Al-Muṭṭalib said: I heard a man asking ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr, ""Did you hear the Messenger of Allah ﷺ specify them?"" He replied, ""Yes: disobedience to parents, associating partners with Allah, taking a life, slandering chaste women, consuming the property of an orphan, fleeing from battle, and consuming usury."""
"387","Thawbān رضي الله عنه reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: > **""There are three sins along with which no righteous deed will be of benefit: associating partners with Allah, disobedience to parents, and fleeing from battle.""**"
"388","Salamah ibn Qays رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""They are four cardinal commands, and I have never guarded anything more jealously than them since the day I heard them from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: Beware! Do not associate anything with Allah; do not kill the soul which Allah has made sacred except with justice; do not commit fornication; and do not steal.""**"
"389","ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbbās رضي الله عنهما reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""There are three matters: whoever is free from all of them, Allah will forgive whatever is besides that for whomever He wills: whoever dies without associating anything with Allah, was not a sorcerer following sorcerers, and harbored no malice against his brother.""**"
"390","Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""The major sins are seven: associating partners with Allah, killing a soul which Allah has forbidden except by right, slandering a chaste woman, fleeing from the battlefield, consuming usury, consuming the property of an orphan, and returning to Bedouin life after emigration.""**"
"391","ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbbās رضي الله عنهما reported that a man asked: ""O Messenger of Allah, what are the major sins?"" He ﷺ replied: > **""Associating partners with Allah, despairing of Allah's soothing relief, and losing all hope in the mercy of Allah.""**"
"392","ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd رضي الله عنه said: > **""The greatest major sins are: associating partners with Allah, feeling secure from the plan of Allah, losing hope in the mercy of Allah, and despairing of the soothing relief of Allah.""**"
"393","ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr رضي الله عنهما reported: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to his Companions: > **""I take your pledge of allegiance that you will not associate anything with Allah, nor kill the soul which Allah has forbidden except by right, nor commit fornication, nor steal, nor drink intoxicants. Whoever among you commits any of these things and has its legal punishment executed upon him, it shall be an expiation for him. And whoever has his sin concealed by Allah, his reckoning rests with Allah, the Mighty and Majestic. And whoever does not commit any of these things, I guarantee Paradise for him from Allah.""**"
"394","Anas ibn Mālik رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""His fire shall never be extinguished, its worms shall never die, and his punishment shall never be lightened: the one who associates partners with Allah, the Mighty and Majestic; a man who drags another man before a ruler without any offense so that the ruler kills him; and a man who is disobedient to his parents.""**"
"395","ʿAbdullāh ibn Unays al-Juhanī رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Among the greatest of major sins are associating partners with Allah and the perjurious, engulfing false oath.""**"
"396","Muʿādh ibn Jabal رضي الله عنه reported: A man came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, ""O Messenger of Allah, teach me a deed that, if I perform it, I will enter Paradise."" He ﷺ said: > **""Do not associate anything with Allah, even if you are tortured and burned. Obey your parents, even if they expel you from your wealth and from everything you possess. Do not abandon the obligatory prayer deliberately, for whoever abandons the prayer deliberately, the protection of Allah is free from him. Do not drink wine, for it is the key to every evil. Do not dispute the authority of those who possess it, even if you believe you have a right to it. Spend upon your family from your means, do not raise your stick of discipline from them, and instill in them the fear of Allah.""**"
"397","Buraydah رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Indeed, the greatest of major sins are: associating partners with Allah, disobedience to parents, withholding surplus water, and withholding a stud animal from breeding.""**"
"398","Faḍālah ibn ʿUbayd رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""There are three persons about whom you need not ask: a man who separates from the main body of Muslims, disobeys his leader, and dies in a state of disobedience; an enslaved woman or man who flees from their master and dies; and a woman whose husband is away, having provided for her worldly needs, yet she displays her charms indecently in his absence. And there are three others about whom you need not ask: a man who contends with Allah regarding His cloak—for His cloak is grandeur and His lower garment is might; a man who is in doubt concerning the decree of Allah; and the one who despairs of the mercy of Allah.""**"
"399","Muʿādh ibn Jabal رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""The angels continue to curse a woman—or Allah, His angels, the guardians of mercy, and the guardians of punishment curse her—as long as she persists in violating anything of Allah's prohibitions.""**"
"400","ʿĀʾishah رضي الله عنها reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: > **""Ruined are those who indulge in filthy abominations (al-mutaqadhdhirūn).""** Ibn al-Athīr said in *al-Nihāyah*: ""Al-mutaqadhdhirūn are those who commit foul obscenities and illicit acts."""
"401","Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī رضي الله عنه said: > **""Indeed, you commit deeds that are finer in your eyes than a strand of hair, yet during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ we used to count them among the fatal, destructive sins.""**"
"402","ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar رضي الله عنهما said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Withhold from the people of 'Lā ilāha illā Allāh' (there is no deity worthy of worship except Allah); do not declare them disbelievers on account of any sin. For whoever declares the people of 'Lā ilāha illā Allāh' to be disbelievers is himself closer to disbelief.""**"
"403","Abū al-Dardāʾ, Abū Umāmah, Wāthilah ibn al-Asqaʿ, and Anas ibn Mālik رضي الله عنهم said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out to us while we were disputing concerning a matter of religion. [The narrator mentioned the hadith until he said:] The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Indeed, Islam began as something strange, and it will return to being strange.""** They said, ""O Messenger of Allah, who are the strangers?"" He ﷺ said: > **""Those who remain righteous when the people become corrupt, who do not engage in futile argumentation regarding the religion of Allah, and do not declare anyone from the people of Tawḥīd to be a disbeliever on account of a sin.""**"
"404","ʿAlī and Jābir رضي الله عنهما said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Islam is built upon three foundations: withhold from the people of 'Lā ilāha illā Allāh'—do not declare them disbelievers on account of a sin, nor bear witness against them with polytheism; the recognition of the Divine Decrees, both the good and the bad of them being from Allah; and Jihad continues until the Day of Resurrection, from the time Allah sent Muḥammad ﷺ until the last group of Muslims—neither the tyranny of an oppressor nor the justice of an equitable leader can abrogate it.""**"
"405","Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī رضي الله عنه reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: > **""None shall exit from faith except through the denial of that by which he entered into it.""**"
"406","ʿĀʾishah رضي الله عنها said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: > **""Do not declare anyone from the people of the Qiblah to be a disbeliever on account of a sin, even if they commit major sins; pray behind every imam, and struggle in Jihad alongside every ruler.""**"
"407","Yazīd al-Raqāshī reported from Anas ibn Mālik رضي الله عنه: I said, ""O Abū Ḥamzah, indeed there are people who testify against us with disbelief and polytheism!"" Anas رضي الله عنه said: > **""Those are the worst of creation and humankind.""**"
"408","Abū Sufyān reported: I asked Jābir رضي الله عنه while he was residing near Mecca, staying among Banū Fihr. A man asked him, ""Did you ever call anyone from the people of the Qiblah a polytheist?"" He said, ""Allah forbid!"" and was horrified by that. The man asked, ""Did you ever call any of them a disbeliever?"" He replied: > **""No.""**"
"409","Abū Hurayrah رضي الله عنه said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""I do not fear for my nation anything except weakness of certainty.""**"
"410","Al-Nuʿmān ibn Bashīr رضي الله عنه used to say from his pulpit: > **""Indeed, the calamity of all calamities is that you commit evil deeds alongside corrupted faith.""**"
"411","Abū Hurayrah رضي الله عنه reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: > **""Indeed, the hypocrites have distinguishing marks by which they are recognized: their greeting is a curse, their food is plunder, their war booty is embezzlement, they do not approach the mosques except with avoidance and harshness, and they do not come to the prayer except belatedly, behaving haughtily except in mere speech; they do not bring hearts together nor are they harmonized with; they are like propped-up timber by night and clamorous by day.""**"
"412","Anas ibn Mālik رضي الله عنه said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: > **""Three traits, whoever possesses them is a hypocrite, even if he fasts, prays, performs Hajj and ʿUmrah, and says: 'Indeed, I am a Muslim': when he speaks he lies, when he promises he breaks his word, and when he is entrusted he betrays.""**"
"413","Jābir رضي الله عنه said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""In the hypocrite are three characteristics: when he speaks he lies, when he promises he breaks his word, and when he is entrusted he betrays.""**"
"414","Abū Bakr al-Ṣiddīq رضي الله عنه reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: > **""The signs of the hypocrite are: when he speaks he lies, when he promises he breaks his word, and when he is entrusted he betrays.""**"
"415","Salmān al-Fārisī رضي الله عنه said: Abū Bakr and ʿUmar entered upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""Among the traits of the hypocrite are: when he speaks he lies, when he promises he breaks his word, and when he is entrusted he betrays."" They both departed from the presence of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ feeling heavy-hearted. I met them and said, ""Why do I see you two looking so troubled?"" They replied, ""Because of a hadith we heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said: 'Among the traits of the hypocrite are: when he speaks he lies, when he promises he breaks his word, and when he is entrusted he betrays.'"" Salmān said, ""Did you not ask him for clarification?"" They said, ""We held the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in too much awe."" Salmān said, ""Then I will ask him."" I entered upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, ""I met Abū Bakr and ʿUmar رضي الله عنهما and they were feeling deeply burdened,"" and I recounted what they had said. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""I did speak to them, but I did not intend it in the manner they understood it. Rather, the hypocrite is the one who, when he speaks, tells himself inwardly that he will lie; and when he promises, tells himself inwardly that he will break his word; and when he is entrusted, tells himself inwardly that he will betray.""**"
"416","ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd رضي الله عنه reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: > **""Three traits, whoever possesses them is a hypocrite; and whoever possesses one trait among them possesses a branch of hypocrisy: when he speaks he lies, when he is entrusted he betrays, and when he promises he breaks his word.""**"
"417","ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd رضي الله عنه said: > **""Evaluate the hypocrites by three traits: when he speaks he lies, when he promises he breaks his word, and when he enters into a covenant he acts treacherously.""** Allah, Mighty and Majestic, revealed the confirmation of that in His Book: *{And among them are those who made a covenant with Allah: ""If He should give us of His bounty, we will surely give charity and be among the righteous."" But when He gave them from His bounty, they were stingy with it and turned away while refusing.}* [At-Tawbah: 75–76]."
"418","Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī رضي الله عنه said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Among the signs of the hypocrite are: when he speaks he lies, when he promises he breaks his word, and when you entrust him he betrays you.""**"
"419","Sahl ibn Saʿd al-Sāʿidī رضي الله عنه said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""The intention of the believer is better than his action, and the action of the hypocrite is better than his intention; and each acts according to his intention. When the believer performs a deed, light radiates in his heart.""**"
"420","Abū Hurayrah رضي الله عنه said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by ʿAbdullāh ibn Ubayy ibn Salūl while he was sitting in the shade. Ibn Salūl said, ""The son of Abū Kabshah has kicked up dust upon us!"" His son ʿAbdullāh said, ""By the One Who honored you and sent down the Book upon you, if you wish, I will bring you his head!"" The Prophet ﷺ said: > **""No; rather, show filial piety to your father and treat him with good companionship.""**"
"421","Ṣilah ibn Zufar said: We said to Ḥudhayfah رضي الله عنه, ""How did you come to know the affair of the hypocrites when none of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ knew it, neither Abū Bakr nor ʿUmar رضي الله عنهما?"" Ḥudhayfah said: I was riding behind the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when he fell asleep upon his mount. I heard some men among them saying, ""If we were to push him off his mount so that his neck breaks, we would be relieved of him."" So I rode between them and him, and began reciting aloud, raising my voice. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ awoke and said: > **""Who is this?""** I said, ""Ḥudhayfah."" He asked: > **""Who are those men?""** I said, ""So-and-so and so-and-so,"" until I had enumerated them all. He asked: > **""And did you hear what they said?""** I said, ""Yes, and for that reason I rode between you and them."" He ﷺ said: > **""Indeed, those—so-and-so and so-and-so [naming them]—are hypocrites; do not inform anyone about them.""**"
"422","Ḥudhayfah رضي الله عنه said: I was holding the halter of the she-camel of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, leading it, while ʿAmmār was driving it—or ʿAmmār was leading it and I was driving it—when twelve masked men confronted us. He ﷺ said: > **""These are hypocrites until the Day of Resurrection.""** I said, ""O Messenger of Allah, will you not send to each man of them and have him executed?"" He ﷺ said: > **""I dislike that the people should say that Muḥammad kills his companions. Perhaps the dubaylah will suffice against them.""** We asked, ""And what is the dubaylah?"" He ﷺ said: > **""A brand of fire placed upon the aorta of the heart of one of them, which kills him.""**"
"423","Ḥudhayfah رضي الله عنه said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ took the bed of the valley while the people took the mountain pass. Seven masked individuals approached. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw them—while Ḥudhayfah was leading the mount and ʿAmmār was driving it—he ﷺ said: > **""Guard what is between you two!""** They were unable to carry out their scheme. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ looked towards them and said: > **""O Ḥudhayfah, do you know who these people are?""** I said, ""I do not recognize any of them except the owner of the red camel, for I know that he is so-and-so."""
"424","Jābir رضي الله عنه said: There was an exchange of harsh words between ʿAmmār ibn Yāsir and Wadīʿah ibn Thābit. Wadīʿah said to ʿAmmār, ""You are merely the slave of Abū Ḥudhayfah ibn al-Mughīrah; he has not yet freed you!"" ʿAmmār said, ""How many were the people of the mountain pass (al-ʿAqabah)?"" Wadīʿah replied, ""Allah knows best."" ʿAmmār said, ""Tell me according to what you know!"" Wadīʿah fell silent. Those present said, ""Answer him about what he asked you!""—for ʿAmmār intended that he disclose that he himself was among them. Wadīʿah said, ""We used to discuss that they were fourteen men."" ʿAmmār said, ""And if you were among them, then they were fifteen."" Wadīʿah said, ""Go easy, O Abū al-Yaqẓān! I implore you by Allah not to humiliate me today."" ʿAmmār said: > **""By Allah, I have not named anyone, nor shall I ever name anyone. But I bear witness that of the fifteen men, twelve of them are a faction against Allah and His Messenger in the life of this world and on the Day when the witnesses stand forth.""**"
"425","Abū al-Ṭufayl رضي الله عنه said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ set out for the Expedition of Tabūk. When he reached a mountain pass, he ordered his caller to proclaim: ""Let no one take the mountain pass, for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ is traveling through it."" While the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was traveling—with Ḥudhayfah leading his mount and ʿAmmār ibn Yāsir driving it—a group of masked men riding mounts approached until they swarmed around the Prophet ﷺ. ʿAmmār turned back and struck the faces of their mounts. The Prophet ﷺ said to Ḥudhayfah: > **""Lead on! Lead on!""** Then ʿAmmār caught up with him, and he ﷺ said: > **""Drive on! Drive on!""** He continued until he made his mount kneel down. He ﷺ asked ʿAmmār: > **""Did you recognize the people?""** ʿAmmār replied, ""No, they were masked, but I recognized most of the mounts."" He ﷺ asked: > **""Do you know what they intended against the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?""** I said, ""Allah and His Messenger know best."" He ﷺ said: > **""They intended to startle the mount of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ so as to throw him down from the mountain pass.""** Later, a disagreement arose between ʿAmmār and one of those men, as happens among people. ʿAmmār said, ""I adjure you by Allah, how many were the companions of the mountain pass who plotted against the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?"" The man said, ""We consider that they were fourteen."" ʿAmmār said, ""If you were among them, then they were fifteen; and ʿAmmār bears witness that twelve of them are a faction hostile to Allah and His Messenger in the life of this world and on the Day when the witnesses arise."""
"426","Al-Zubayr ibn Bakkār said: The identification of the conspirators of the mountain pass: Muʿattib ibn Qushayr ibn Mulayl, from Banū ʿAmr ibn ʿAwf, who had witnessed Badr. He was the one who said, ""Muḥammad promises us the treasures of Chosroes and Caesar while none of us feels safe even to go to relieve himself!"" and he was the one who said, ""If we had any say in the matter, we would not have been killed here."" Al-Zubayr said: And he was the one against whom al-Zubayr testified concerning these words. And Wadīʿah ibn Thābit ibn ʿAmr ibn ʿAwf; he was the one who said, ""We were only conversing and playing,"" and he was the one who said, ""I have not seen the likes of our reciters—more gluttonous, more deceitful in speech, and more cowardly upon encountering the enemy."" And Jadd ibn ʿAbdillāh ibn Nabtal ibn al-Ḥārith, from Banū ʿAmr ibn ʿAwf; he was the one concerning whom Gabriel عليه السلام said: ""O Muḥammad, who is this dark-skinned man with abundant hair, whose eyes are like two brass cauldrons, who looks with the eyes of a devil and whose liver is the liver of a donkey, who conveys news of you to the hypocrites, and his own news has been made known?"" And al-Ḥārith ibn Yazīd al-Ṭāʾī, an ally of Banū ʿAmr ibn ʿAwf; he was the one who preceded to the spring (al-Washal) which the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had forbidden anyone to precede him to, and he drew water from it. And Aws ibn Qibṭī, from Banū Ḥārithah; he was the one who said, ""Indeed, our houses are exposed,"" and he was the grandfather of Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd ibn Qays. And al-Julās ibn Suwayd ibn al-Ṣāmit, from Banū ʿAmr ibn ʿAwf; and it has reached us that he repented thereafter. And Saʿd ibn Zurārah, from Banū Mālik ibn al-Najjār; he was the one who raised smoke against the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he was the youngest of them in age and the most wicked of them. And Suwayd and Rāʿish, both from Balḥublā; they were among those equipped by Ibn Ubayy during the Expedition of Tabūk to cause people to desert. And Qays ibn ʿAmr ibn Fahd. And Zayd ibn al-Luṣayb; he was from the Jews of Banū Qaynuqāʿ who feigned Islam while retaining the deceit of the Jews and the hypocrisy of the hypocrites. And Sulālah ibn al-Ḥumām, from Banū Qaynuqāʿ, who also feigned Islam. > **[This is the enumeration of the conspirators of the mountain pass as related by al-Zubayr ibn Bakkār.]**"
"427","Abū al-Ṭufayl رضي الله عنه said: During the Expedition of Tabūk, the caller of the Prophet ﷺ announced: > **""Indeed, the water is scarce, so let no one precede me to it.""** Yet when he arrived at the water, some people had already preceded him to it, so he cursed them."
"428","ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUthmān ibn Khuthaym said: I visited Abū al-Ṭufayl رضي الله عنه and found him in pleasant spirits. I said to myself, ""I must seize this opportunity from him."" So I asked, ""O Abū al-Ṭufayl, who were those men whom the Messenger of Allah ﷺ cursed? Name them for me."" He was about to inform me of them, when his wife Sawdah said to him, ""Restrain yourself, O Abū al-Ṭufayl! Has it not reached you that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **'O Allah, I am only a human being; so whichever servant from among the believers I invoke against, make it for him a source of purification and mercy'?""**"
"429","Abū Masʿūd رضي الله عنه said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ delivered a sermon to us. He praised and glorified Allah, and then said: > **""Indeed, among you are hypocrites; so whomever I name, let him stand up.""** Then he said: > **""Stand up, O so-and-so! Stand up, O so-and-so! Stand up, O so-and-so!""** He continued until he had named thirty-six men. Then he said: > **""Indeed, they are among you—or from you; so fear Allah.""** ʿUmar later passed by one of those men who had been named, who was covering his head and face, and whom ʿUmar recognized. ʿUmar asked, ""What is the matter with you?"" The man told him what the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had said. ʿUmar said, ""May ruin befall you for the rest of your days!"""
"430","Umm Salamah رضي الله عنها said: The Prophet ﷺ said: > **""Among those associated with me are some whom I shall never see and who shall never see me after I die.""** When this reached ʿUmar, he came rushing to her and said, ""I implore you by Allah, am I among them?"" She replied, ""No, and I will not absolve anyone after you."" In another narration: ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAwf entered upon her and said, ""O Mother, I fear that my abundant wealth will ruin me, for I am the wealthiest of Quraysh."" She said, ""O my son, spend in charity! For I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: > **'Indeed, among those associated with me are some who will never see me after I depart from them.'""**"
"431","ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr رضي الله عنهما said: We were sitting in the company of the Prophet ﷺ while ʿAmr ibn al-ʿĀṣ had gone to put on his garments to join me. While we were with the Prophet ﷺ, he said: > **""There shall surely enter upon you an accursed man.""** By Allah, I remained anxious, watching outside and inside, until that man entered—meaning al-Ḥakam."
"432","ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr رضي الله عنهما said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""There will soon appear before you a man who will be resurrected on the Day of Resurrection upon other than my Sunnah—or upon other than my religion.""** I had left my father at home, so I feared that it might be him. But someone else appeared, whereupon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""It is this one.""**"
"433","ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr رضي الله عنهما said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""There will appear before you from this mountain pass a man from the inhabitants of the Fire.""** I had left my father performing ablution, so I feared that it might be him. But someone else appeared, whereupon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""It is this one.""**"
"434","Ibn al-Zubayr رضي الله عنهما said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""The first person to enter through this door is from the people of the Fire.""** Then so-and-so entered."
"435","ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbbās رضي الله عنهما said: > **""One of them says: 'My father accompanied the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ'—whereas a worn-out sandal is better than his father!""**"
"436","Al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī رضي الله عنهما said to Abū al-Aʿwar al-Sulamī: > **""Woe to you! Did not the Messenger of Allah ﷺ invoke curses upon [the tribes of] Riʿl, Dhakwān, and ʿAmr ibn Sufyān?""**"
"437","Safīnah رضي الله عنه reported: The Prophet ﷺ was sitting when a man passed by on a camel, with a leader in front of him and a driver behind him. He ﷺ said: > **""May Allah curse the leader, the driver, and the rider.""**"
"438","Al-Muhājir ibn Qunfudh رضي الله عنه said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw three people riding upon a single camel, whereupon he said: > **""The third is accursed.""**"
"439","Saʿd ibn Ḥudhayfah reported: ʿAmmār ibn Yāsir رضي الله عنه said on the day of Ṣiffīn, mentioning their affair and the matter of reconciliation: > **""By Allah, they did not truly embrace Islam; rather, they merely surrendered and concealed disbelief. When they found supporters for it, they manifested it openly.""**"
"440","ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr رضي الله عنهما said: > **""The caller will proclaim the call to prayer, and a people will establish the prayer, yet they are not believers.""**"
"441","ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAwf رضي الله عنه said: I entered upon ʿUmar رضي الله عنه, and he said, ""O ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAwf, do you fear that the people will abandon Islam and exit from it?"" I said, ""No, if Allah wills. How could they abandon it when among them is the Book of Allah and the Sunnahs of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?"" ʿUmar said: > **""If anything of that sort were ever to occur, it would surely be on account of Banū so-and-so.""**"
"442","Jābir رضي الله عنه said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Every soul shall be resurrected according to its inward desire; whoever desires disbelief will be gathered with the disbelievers, and his deeds will not benefit him in the least.""**"
"443","Faḍālah ibn ʿUbayd رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Whoever dies upon one of these states shall be resurrected upon it on the Day of Resurrection.""**"
"444","A man said to ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd رضي الله عنه: ""Indeed, I fear that I am a hypocrite."" ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd رضي الله عنه said: > **""If you were truly a hypocrite, you would never have feared that.""**"
"445","ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbbās رضي الله عنهما said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Iblīs said to his Lord: 'O Lord, You have sent down Adam to the earth, and I know that there will be scriptures and messengers; so what are their scriptures and messengers?'** > > **Allah said: 'Their messengers are the angels, and the prophets from among them; and their scriptures are the Torah, the Gospel, the Psalms, and the Furqān (the Qur'an).'** > > **Iblīs asked: 'Then what is my book?'** > > **Allah said: 'Your book is tattooing, your recitation is vain poetry, your messengers are the soothsayers, your food is whatever is not mentioned with the name of Allah, your drink is every intoxicant, your truthfulness is falsehood, your house is the bathhouse, your hunting snares are women, your caller to prayer is musical pipes, and your places of assembly are the marketplaces.'""**"
"446","Abū Mūsā al-Ashʿarī رضي الله عنه reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: > **""When morning arrives, Iblīs dispatches his troops and proclaims: 'Whoever misguides a Muslim today, I will place a crown upon his head.'** > > **They return to him, and one of them says, 'I did not cease whispering to him until he divorced his wife.' Iblīs says, 'He will soon marry again.'** > > **Another comes and says, 'I did not cease whispering to him until he was undutiful to his parents.' Iblīs says, 'He will soon treat them with kindness.'** > > **Then another comes and says, 'I did not cease whispering to him until he committed polytheism (shirk)!' Iblīs says: 'You are the one! You are the one!' and crowns him.""**"
"447","Abū Rayḥānah رضي الله عنه said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Indeed, Iblīs places his throne upon the sea, seeking to imitate Allah, Mighty and Majestic, with veils set before him. He summons his legions and says: 'Who will take on so-and-so among the children of Adam?' Two devils step forward, and he says: 'I grant you both a respite of one full year: if you seduce him, I will relieve you of all labor; otherwise, I will crucify you both.'""** The narrator said: Someone remarked to Abū Rayḥānah, ""Indeed, many devils must have been crucified on your account!"""
"448","Muʿāwiyah ibn Qurrah reported from his father رضي الله عنه: I was with my father intending to visit the Prophet ﷺ. While on the journey, we passed by an encampment and stayed the night among them. The shepherd came running to the people of the camp, saying, ""I will no longer graze your sheep for you, because a wolf comes every night and seizes a sheep from the flock, while the idol looks on, neither objecting nor changing anything!"" They said, ""Remain with us until we go to it."" So they approached the idol, spoke around it, and then told the shepherd, ""Stay tonight."" He said, ""I will stay tonight so we can see what happens."" We spent our night there. At the morning prayer, the shepherd came running swiftly to the people of the village, saying to them, ""Rejoice! Do you not see the wolf lying bound before the sheep without any rope?"" They came, and we went along with them. They praised the idol, saying, ""Yes, keep doing like this!"" When we arrived before the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, my father related the incident to him. He ﷺ said: > **""Satan is merely playing with them.""**"
"449","Muʿāwiyah ibn Qurrah reported from his father رضي الله عنه: I set out to embrace Islam when the Prophet ﷺ was commissioned, wishing to enter Islam along with two or three men. I arrived at a watering place where people gathered, and met the shepherd of the village who grazed their sheep. He said, ""I will not graze your sheep for you."" They asked, ""Why?"" He said, ""Every night a wolf comes and takes a sheep, while this idol of ours stands by—neither harming nor benefiting, neither altering anything nor objecting!"" They went back, and I hoped they would accept Islam. The next morning, the shepherd came running, calling out, ""What glad tidings! What glad tidings! The wolf has been brought and lies bound before the sheep!"" I went with them, and they kissed the idol, prostrated before it, and said, ""Keep doing like this!"" I entered upon the Prophet ﷺ and related this story to him. He ﷺ said: > **""Satan has toyed with them.""**"
"450","Al-Sāʾib رضي الله عنه said: My family sent me with a bowl of milk and butter as an offering to their deities. I carried it, being terrified of consuming any of it. I placed it before the idol, when suddenly a dog came along, drank up the milk, ate the butter, and urinated upon the idol!"
"451","Al-Sāʾib رضي الله عنه reported that he was among those who took part in rebuilding the Kaʿbah during the pre-Islamic period of ignorance. He said: I possessed a stone that I had carved with my own hand, and I used to worship it instead of Allah, Exalted is He. I brought thick milk that I would have begrudged even to myself, and poured it over the stone. Then a dog came, licked it up, lifted its leg, and urinated upon it! [The narrator mentioned the rest of the hadith, which appears in full under the rebuilding of the Kaʿbah.]"
"452","Abū Hurayrah رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Indeed, the believer wears down and exhausts his devils just as one of you exhausts his camel on a journey.""**"
"453","ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd رضي الله عنه reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: > **""Indeed, the first person to dedicate free-roaming livestock (sawāʾib) to false deities and introduce idol worship was the father of Khuzāʿah, ʿAmr ibn ʿĀmir; and I saw him dragging his intestines in the Fire.""**"
"454","ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbbās رضي الله عنهما said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""The first person to alter the religion of Abraham was ʿAmr ibn Luḥayy ibn Qamʿah ibn Khindif, the forefather of Khuzāʿah.""**"
"455","ʿAlqamah said: We were sitting in the presence of ʿĀʾishah رضي الله عنها when Abū Hurayrah رضي الله عنه entered. She said to him, ""Are you the one who narrates that a woman was punished on account of a cat which she tied up, neither feeding it nor giving it water?"" He replied, ""I heard it from him""—meaning the Prophet ﷺ. She said: > **""Do you know who that woman was? That woman, in addition to what she did, was a disbeliever. The believer is far too noble in the sight of Allah, Mighty and Majestic, for Him to punish him on account of a cat. Therefore, whenever you narrate from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, be mindful of how you narrate!""**"
"456","Abū Razīn al-ʿUqaylī reported from his uncle رضي الله عنه: I said, ""O Messenger of Allah, where is my mother?"" He ﷺ said: > **""Your mother is in the Fire.""** He said, ""I asked: Where are those who passed away from your family?"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Does it not satisfy you that your mother is with my mother?""**"
"457","Buraydah رضي الله عنه said: We were traveling with the Prophet ﷺ when he halted, and we were nearly a thousand riders with him. He prayed two rakʿahs, then turned his face towards us while tears were flowing from his eyes. ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb stood up and said, ""May my father and mother be ransomed for you, O Messenger of Allah! What has brought you to tears?"" He ﷺ said: > **""I asked my Lord, Mighty and Majestic, for permission to seek forgiveness for my mother, but He did not permit me. So my eyes wept out of compassion for her from the Fire.""**"
"458","Buraydah رضي الله عنه said: We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ until we reached Waddān—or came near the graves—and he requested intercession for his mother. [The narrator said: I believe he said:] Gabriel عليه السلام struck his chest and said: > **""Do not seek forgiveness for one who died a polytheist.""**"
"459","ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbbās رضي الله عنهما said: When the Prophet ﷺ returned from the Expedition of Tabūk and performed ʿUmrah, upon descending from the mountain pass of ʿUsfān, he instructed his Companions: ""Lean against the mountain pass until I return to you."" He went and paused beside the grave of his mother, conversing privately with his Lord for a long time. Then he wept intensely, and the Companions wept because of his weeping. They said, ""The Prophet of Allah ﷺ would not weep in this place unless something had occurred concerning his nation that he cannot bear."" When they wept, he arose and returned to them, asking: > **""What makes you weep?""** They said, ""O Prophet of Allah, we wept because of your weeping; we said: 'Perhaps something has occurred concerning your nation that you cannot bear.'"" He ﷺ said: > **""No, though a part of it was that. Rather, I stopped beside a grave and supplicated Allah to permit me to intercede for her on the Day of Resurrection, but Allah refused to permit me. So I felt compassion for her, for she is my mother, and I wept.** > > **Then Gabriel عليه السلام came to me and recited: *{And the request of forgiveness of Abraham for his father was only because of a promise he had made to him. But when it became clear to him that he was an enemy to Allah, he disassociated himself from him.}* [At-Tawbah: 114]. Gabriel said: 'Disassociate yourself from your mother just as Abraham disassociated himself from his father.' But I felt compassion for her, for she is my mother.** > > **Then I supplicated my Lord to lift four afflictions from my nation, and He lifted two of them and refused to lift two: I asked my Lord to lift from them pelting stones from the sky and drowning into the earth, and that He not divide them into warring factions nor make some of them taste the violence of others. He lifted from them pelting stones from the sky and drowning into the earth, but Allah refused to lift two from them: bloodshed and turmoil (al-harj).'""** [The narrator noted: He only detoured to his mother's grave because she was buried under such-and-such, and ʿUsfān belonged to their maternal lineage.]"
"460","ʿImrān ibn al-Ḥuṣayn رضي الله عنه reported: His father al-Ḥuṣayn came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, ""What do you say concerning a man who used to honor the guest and maintain family ties, who died before your advent, namely your father?"" The Prophet ﷺ said: > **""Indeed, my father, your father, and you will be in the Fire.""** [The narrator noted: And Ḥuṣayn subsequently died as a polytheist.]"
"461","Saʿd ibn Abī Waqqāṣ رضي الله عنه reported: A bedouin came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, ""O Messenger of Allah, where is my father?"" He ﷺ said: > **""In the Fire.""** The bedouin asked, ""Then where is your father?"" He ﷺ said: > **""Wherever you pass by the grave of a disbeliever, give him the tidings of the Fire.""** The bedouin later embraced Islam and said, ""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ assigned me a laborious duty: I never pass by the grave of a disbeliever except that I give him the tidings of the Fire."""
"462","Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""On the Day of Resurrection, a man will take hold of his father's hand, seeking to lead him away from the Fire, desiring to admit him into Paradise. Then it will be proclaimed: 'Indeed, Paradise is forbidden to every polytheist; Allah has forbidden Paradise to any polytheist.'** > > **He will plead: 'O my Lord, my father!'** > > **Then his father will be transformed into an abhorrent form with a foul stench, and he will abandon him.""** The Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ considered that this man was Abraham عليه السلام, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not add anything further to that."
"463","Abū Hurayrah رضي الله عنه reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: > **""A man will meet his father on the Day of Resurrection and say: 'O my father, will you obey me today? Will you follow me today?'** > > **His father will reply: 'Yes.'** > > **So he will take him by the hand and proceed until he brings him before Allah, Blessed and Exalted, as He presents creation for judgment. The man will say: 'O my Lord, You promised me that You would not disgrace me!'** > > **Allah, Blessed and Exalted, will turn away from him. The man will repeat the same appeal. Then Allah will transform his father into a hyena and cast him into the Fire. The father will call: 'I am your father!' But he will reply: 'I do not know you.'""**"
"464","Umm Salamah رضي الله عنها, wife of the Prophet ﷺ, reported: Al-Ḥārith ibn Hishām came to the Prophet ﷺ on the day of the Farewell Pilgrimage and said, ""O Messenger of Allah, you urge maintaining family ties, treating neighbors kindly, sheltering orphans, feeding guests, and providing for the destitute. All of this was done by Hishām ibn al-Mughīrah. What is your judgment regarding him, O Messenger of Allah?"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Every grave whose occupant did not testify that there is no deity worthy of worship except Allah is a blazing pit of the Fire. As for my uncle Abū Ṭālib, I found him in the deepest abyss of the Fire, but Allah brought him out on account of his standing with me and his kindness towards me, placing him in a shallow part of the Fire.""**"
"465","Umm Salamah رضي الله عنها said: I said, ""O Messenger of Allah, my uncle Hishām ibn al-Mughīrah used to provide food, maintain family ties, and do such-and-such; had he lived to your time, he surely would have embraced Islam."" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""He gave only for the sake of the world, its praise, and its renown; and he never once said in all his life: 'O Allah, forgive me my sins on the Day of Judgment.'""**"
"466","Salamah ibn Yazīd al-Juʿfī رضي الله عنه said: My brother, my father, and I went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. We said, ""O Messenger of Allah, our mother Mulaykah used to maintain family ties, honor the guest, and perform virtuous deeds, but she died in the pre-Islamic period of ignorance; will any of that benefit her?"" He ﷺ said: > **""No.""** We said, ""She had saved an infant sister of hers from being buried alive; will that benefit her at all?"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Both the one who buries an infant alive and the infant buried alive are in the Fire, unless the one who buried her alive lived to embrace Islam and Allah pardons her.""**"
"467","ʿAdī ibn Ḥātim رضي الله عنه said: I said, ""O Messenger of Allah, my father used to maintain family ties and do such-and-such."" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Indeed, your father desired a certain matter and he attained it""** — meaning worldly fame and praise."
"468","Sahl ibn Saʿd al-Sāʿidī رضي الله عنه reported: ʿAdī ibn Ḥātim came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, ""O Messenger of Allah, my father used to maintain family ties, bear the burdens of the destitute, and feed the hungry."" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ asked: > **""Did he live to witness Islam?""** ʿAdī replied, ""No."" He ﷺ said: > **""Indeed, your father loved to be remembered, and he was indeed remembered.""**"
"469","ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar رضي الله عنهما said: Ḥātim was mentioned in the presence of the Prophet ﷺ, whereupon he said: > **""That was a man who desired a certain thing, and he achieved it.""**"
"470","Salamah ibn ʿĀmir al-Ḍabbī رضي الله عنه said: I came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, ""O Messenger of Allah, my father used to maintain family ties, honor the guest, and fulfill his covenants."" He ﷺ asked: > **""And he did not live to witness Islam?""** I replied, ""No."" When I turned to depart, the Prophet ﷺ said: > **""Bring the elder back to me.""** He ﷺ then said: > **""That virtue shall remain among your descendants; you will never lose it, nor will you ever be divided.""**"
"471","ʿAfīf al-Kindī رضي الله عنه said: While we were in the company of the Prophet ﷺ, a delegation from Yemen arrived. They mentioned Imruʾ al-Qays ibn Ḥujr al-Kindī and recited two lines of his poetry mentioning Ḍārij, one of the famous water springs of Arabia. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""That is a man remembered in this world but forgotten in the Hereafter; renowned in this world but ignoble in the Hereafter. He will arrive on the Day of Resurrection carrying the banner of the poets, leading them into the Fire.""**"
